2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexios_IV_of_Trebizond
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1395, Alexios married Theodora Kantakouzene. They had at least six children:[15]
2 CONT
2 CONT * A daughter who married Jahan Shah.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jahan_Shah
2 CONT
2 CONT Abu al-Muzaffar Jahan Shah was the leader of the Qara Qoyunlu Oghuz Turkic tribal confederacy in Azerbaijan and Arran who reigned c. 1438 – 1467.  … He was married several times. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Known marriages include: 
2 CONT * a daughter of Alexios IV of Trebizond[7][32] and 
2 CONT * Jan Begüm (daughter Tajuddin Rajab bin Afridun):
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons
2 CONT * Pirbudag – governor of Isfahan and Fars, then Baghdad. Killed by Mirza Muhammad.
2 CONT * Hasan Ali succeeded his father.
2 CONT * Mirza Muhammad – son-in-law to Jahangir Beg, captured on 11 November 1467 at the Battle of Chapakchur and executed.
2 CONT * Mirza Yusuf – captured on 11 November 1467 at the Battle of Chapakchur and blinded. Executed by Ughurlu Muhammad on 22 October 1469.
2 CONT * Qasim Beg
2 CONT Daughters
2 CONT * Saliha Khatun
2 CONT * Habiba Khatun
2 CONT * Tutuq 'Ismat, married to Sultan Muhammad, Timurid ruler[33]
2 CONT * A daughter married to descendant of Nimatullah Vali
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Williams, Kelsey Jackson.  ''A Genealogy of the Grand Komnenoi of Trebizond'' (1/2007) < [https://research-repository.st-andrews.ac.uk/handle/10023/8570 link] > Page 183.  PDF page 13.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexios IV, Emperor of Trebizond, 1417-1429 … 
2 CONT
2 CONT Kuršankis (1979, p.246) summarizes by stating that he believes Alexios to have had five children: Ioannes, Alexander, David, Maria and the anonymous wife of Qara Yoluq. He doubts the existence of the other three daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue by Theodora Kantakouzene (Nicol, 1968, pp.169-170): 
2 CONT
2 CONT viii. (possibly) Anonyma IV. The Pseudo-Chalkokondyles claims that she was married to Jahān Shāh ibn Qara Yūsuf, Emir of the Qarā Quyūnlū (r.1439-1467; Bekker, 1843, p.462), but Kuršankis (1979, pp.245-246) questions this marriage
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT #http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TREBIZOND.htm#dauAlexiosIVMKaraYuluk Emperor Alexios IV & his wife had [nine] children:
2 CONT ## 9.         [daughter .  Laonicus Chalcocondylas records that the emperor of Trebizond made marriage alliances “cum Temiris nepotibus...nati...ab Tzokiis et Carasuphis liberis”, an earlier passage explaining that “Tzanisas Tzoki
2 CONC is nepos et Caraisuphis filius” was the son born "ex filia Tzokiis, quæ matrimonio iuncta fuit Charaisuphi"[198].  Kuršankis suggests that this text is unlikely to be correct, stating that “les Timurides et les Kara-koyonlu étaien
2 CONC t ennemis mortels au début du 15 siècle, et une alliance matrimoniale entre eux est impensable à cette époque”[199].  He also highlights the chronological difficulties, given that Juki, son of Shahrukh, was born in 1402.] 
