2 CONT
2 CONT '''Manuel Angelos Philanthropenos''' (Greek: Μανουήλ Ἂγγελος Φιλανθρωπηνός) was a Byzantine Greek nobleman who ruled Thessaly from c. 1390 until it was conquered by the Ottoman Turks in 1393, as a Byzantine vassal with the title o
2 CONC f Caesar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manuel_Angelos_Philanthropenos#Biography Biography]====
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel was either the son or the brother of the Caesar [https://www.geni.com/people/Caesar-Alexios-Angelos-Philanthropenos/6000000008521882797 '''Alexios Angelos Philanthropenos'''], who had ruled Thessaly since the early 1370s, s
2 CONC ucceeding him upon his death c. 1389/1390. Like Alexios, he recognized the suzerainty of the Byzantine emperor, and was given the title of Caesar in return.[1][2] In 1389, he (or Alexios, if he was still living) sent aid to the ru
2 CONC ler of Ioannina, Esau de' Buondelmonti against the Albanian tribes of Epirus, and their joint forces scored a major victory over them.[3] In 1393, however, the Ottomans sent a large army which occupied Thessaly. Manuel was thus th
2 CONC e last Christian ruler of the entire region until 1878, when it became part of the Kingdom of Greece.[4] Either he or (less likely) [https://www.geni.com/people/Caesar-Alexios-Angelos-Philanthropenos/6000000008521882797 '''Alexios
2 CONC '''] was the grandfather of the Serbian ruler [https://www.geni.com/people/Michael-Angelovi%C4%87/6000000205117708830 '''Mihailo Anđelović'''] and the Ottoman Grand Vizier [https://www.geni.com/people/Mahmud-Angelovi%C4%87-13th-Gr
2 CONC and-Vizier/6000000205117325825 '''Mahmud Pasha Angelović'''].[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT His daughter [https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Philanthropene/6000000008521725742 '''Anna Philanthropene'''] married Emperor [https://www.geni.com/people/Manuel-III-Komnenos-emperor-of-Trebizond/6000000007948731482 '''Manuel III o
2 CONC f Trebizond'''] .[6] 
2 CONT
