2 CONT Bagrat VI (Georgian: ბაგრატ VI) (c. 1439 – 1478), a representative of the Imeretian branch of the Bagrationi royal house, was a king of Imereti (as Bagrat II) from 1463, and a king of Georgia from 1465 until his death.
