1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Recent scholarship identifies him as son of Theodore, which also fits better age-wise.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.researchgate.net/publication/357125088_Serbia_and_Hungary_in_Theodore_Spandounes's_Work_On_the_Origin_of_the_Ottoman_Emperors
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. The Spandounes family had not played any significant role in the history of the Byzantine Empire before this date, but more is known about Theodore’s mother, Eudotia Kantakouzene, and her side of the family. Her grandfather was
2 CONC  '''George Palaiologos Kantakouzenos''', a great soldier and scholar, as well as a direct escendant of Emperor John VI Kantakouzenos (1347–1354). He came to fame during his service under the despot of orea, Constantine Palaiologos
2 CONC  (1428–1449).''' Towards the end of the 1430s, George and his brother Thomas moved to Serbia, where their sister Irene had lived since her marriage to the despot Đurađ Branković''' (1427–1456) in 1414. Members of the Kantakouzenos
2 CONC  family (including George’s numerous offspring) played important political roles in Serbia until its annexation by the Ottoman Empire in 1459.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.  '''George Palaiologos Kantakouzenos''' (Greek: Γεώργιος Παλαιολόγος Καντακουζηνός; ca. 1390 – 1456/59[1] ) was a Byzantine aristocrat, a member of the Kantakouzenos family, and adventurer. He is also known by the Turkish nickn
2 CONC ame Sachatai, which he earned in the service of the Despot Constantine early in his military career.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT George Palaiologos Kantakouzenos was likely the '''son''' of Theodore Palaiologos Kantakouzenos.[3] and his wife Helena Ouresina Doukaina, and '''grandson''' of  Demetrios I Kantakouzenos, Despot of the Morea (1383)
2 CONT
2 CONT Although there is no surviving record of his wife's name, Hugues Busac credits him with a family of nine children, four sons and five daughters. (See below).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Kantakouzenos
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodore's wife was Helena Ouresina Doukaina, a daughter of John Uroš, ruler of Thessaly.[10] He is believed to have had the following issue: ….
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed parents 
2 CONT -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Palaiologos_Kantakouzenos  <br/>
2 CONT /!\ {FR ''...Nicol suppose en outre que son père était [https://www.geni.com/people/Demetrius-I-Kantakouzenos-despot-of-Morea/377256097400012303 Démétrios Cantacuzène][7].'' }
2 CONT
2 CONT George Palaiologos Kantakouzenos was likely the son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodore-Kantakouzenos/6000000173483533910?through=6000000008309265431 Theodore Palaiologos Kantakouzenos].[3] Among his siblings were the Despote
2 CONC ss of Serbia Irene Kantakouzene, the Empress of Trebizond Helena, and the unnamed wife of King George VIII of Georgia. He was also a cousin of the last two Byzantine emperors, John VIII Palaiologos and Constantine XI Palaiologos.[
2 CONC 1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues Busac, compiling the genealogy of his wife Carola Cantacuzene de Flory, describes George Palaiologos Kantakouzenos  as her grandfather and the brother of the Grand Domestic Andronikos Palaiologos Kantakouzenos. Spandounes c
2 CONC laimed him as his maternal grandfather, and elsewhere describes him as the grandson of the Emperor John VI Kantakouzenos. Nicol believes Spandounes is in error, and the Emperor John VI was his great-grandfather and Matthew Kantako
2 CONC uzenos his grandfather.
2 CONT
2 CONT Although there is no surviving record of his wife's name, Hugues Busac credits him with a family of nine children, four sons and five daughters. According to Nicol, they are:[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Theodore Kantakouzenos (died 1459?)
2 CONT # Manuel Kantakouzenos (flourished 1450–1470)
2 CONT # Thomas Kantakouzenos (flourished 1460), only known through Busac's genealogy.[8]
2 CONT # Demetrios Kantakouzenos, of whom nothing certain is known.[9]
2 CONT # An unnamed daughter, who married George Raoul; Raoul served as an envoy for the Despot of the Morea Thomas Palaiologos in July 1460[10]
2 CONT # Another unnamed daughter, who married Nicholas Palaiologos.[11]
2 CONT # Zoe Kantakouzene de Flory, who married James II de Flory, Count of Jaffa, and the parents of Hugues Busac's wife Carola.[12]
2 CONT # Anna Kantakouzene, who married Vladislav Hercegović
2 CONT # Another unnamed daughter, whom Nicol speculates was the mother of Eudokia Kantakouzene, the mother of Theodore Spandounes.[13]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kantakouzenos#Family_tree_of_the_Imperial_House_of_Kantakouzenos
2 CONT
2 CONT John VI Kantakouzenos, rose to be megas domestikos, regent, and eventually emperor (1341–1354) before resigning and retiring to a monastery after a failed civil war.[4] John VI's eldest son Matthew also reigned as his co-emperor a
2 CONC nd as a pretender (1353–1357) before being captured and forced to resign as well. John's younger son Manuel Kantakouzenos remained despotes of the Morea from 1349 until 1380. Of John VI's daughters, Helena Kantakouzene married Joh
2 CONC n and Matthew's rival John V Palaiologos (r. 1341–1391), Maria married Nikephoros II Orsini of Epirus, and Theodora married the Ottoman bey Orhan I.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthew's two sons, John and Demetrios, ruled briefly the Morea.[3] It is generally believed that John, about whom relatively few documents have survived, died childless, and that the numerous Kantakouzenoi of the following genera
2 CONC tion, as well as the historian Theodore Spandounes and the wife of genealogist Hugues Busac, trace their descent from Matthew through Demetrios.[5]  [DIsputed]
2 CONT
2 CONT The possible descendants of Demetrios (the exact parentage is uncertain) were Georgios, called "Sachatai"; Andronikos, the last megas domestikos of the Byzantine Empire; Irene, who married Đurađ Branković; Thomas, who served in Br
2 CONC anković's court; Helena, who became the second wife of David of Trebizond; and an unnamed daughter, who may have become queen of Georgia.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical records 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2012611453.htm#EuphrosyneKMNikolaosP
2 CONT
2 CONT THEODOROS Palaiologos Kantakouzenos, son of [DEMETRIOS] Kantakouzenos & his wife --- (after 1361-1410).  Theodoros Kantakouzenos & his wife had [nine] children: ....
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         GEORGIOS Palaiologos Kantakouzenos "Sachatai" (-before 1459).  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names (in order) Demetrios, Manuel, Georgios, Andronikos, Thomas, as the sons of Theodoros & his wife[594].  Theodoros Span
2 CONC dounes names "il signor Georgio Cantacusino nomato Sachatai…nipote…figliolo del figliolo dell’imperatore Ioanne Cantacusino"[595].  In Peloponnesos 1431/36.  In Trebizond 1436/37.  He lived at the court of his brother-in-law Djura
2 CONC dj Branković of Serbia 1437.  Serbian Archon at Semendria 1454/56.  m ([1424]) MARIA, daughter of MANUEL Razi [Ralli] & his wife ---.  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names Maria, daughter of Manuel Razi as the wife of Georgios, 
2 CONC son of Theodoros, adding that they had twelve sons and twelve daughters, of whom five sons and eight daughters survived[596].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Georgios Kantakouzenos & his wife had 12 sons and 12 daughters: ... 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names (in order) Euphrosyne, Maria, Philippa, Eirene, Cherana, Theodora, Philippa and Zoia as the eight surviving daughters of Georgios & his wife, stating that Anna married Vladislav son of Stefan
2 CONC  duke of Bosnia[634].  .... 
2 CONT
