2 CONT 2.         '''MANUEL''' .  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names (in order) Demetrios, Manuel, Georgios, Andronikos, Thomas, as the sons of Theodoros & his wife, commenting that Manuel was protostrator[581].  Protostrator 1420/29
2 CONC .  Georgios Phrantzes records an incident during the siege of Patras, dated to 29 Mar 1429, when he rescued Konstantinos Palaiologos [the future Emperor Konstantinos XI] but was captured after falling from his horse, a thoroughbre
2 CONC d which "ameras" [the emir, unspecified] had given to “Isaacio Asani” who had later given it to “Georgio Philanthropeno genero [γαμβρω] suo” who, in turn had given it to “Comneno consobrino [ανεψιω], Cantacuzeni protostratoris gen
2 CONC ero [γαμβρω]”, adding that the latter “Galatam fugientem” [fleeing to Galata] had been captured by Phrantzes’s brother (who had been granted the horse as a reward)[582].  Theodoros Spandounes names "signore Emanuel Cantacusino fra
2 CONC tello di Giorgio nomato Sachatai"[583].  Georgios Phrantzes records that Emperor Ioannes VIII installed "stratopedarcham…Cantacuzeni filium propter affinitatem et patrem eius protostratorum"[584].  m ---, daughter of ASEN & his wi
2 CONC fe ---.  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript records that Manuel, son of Theodoros, married a daughter of Asen[585].  Manuel & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         ANDREAS .  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names Andreas and Eudokia as the children of Manuel & his wife[586].  Georgios Phrantzes records that Emperor Ioannes VIII installed "stratopedarcham…Cantacuzeni filium propt
2 CONC er affinitatem et patrem eius protostratorum"[587].  '''m''' ---, daughter of --- Sincrula Palaiologos.  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names her as the wife of Andreas[588].  Andreas Kantakouzenos & his wife had three children:
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT **i)          son (-died aged 15).  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript records that the two (unnamed) sons of Andreas & his wife died aged 15 and 13 respectively[589].  
2 CONT
2 CONT **ii)         son (-died aged 13).  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript records that the two (unnamed) sons of Andreas & his wife died aged 15 and 13 respectively[590]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT **iii)        daughter (-died aged 5).  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript records that the (unnamed) daughter of Andreas & his wife died aged 5[591]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         EUDOKIA .  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names Andreas and Eudokia as the children of Manuel & his wife, stating that Eudokia married a grandson of the emperor of Trebizond but died without issue[592].  Her marriage
2 CONC  appears to be confirmed by Georgios Phrantzes who records an incident during the siege of Patras, dated to 29 Mar 1429, when he rescued Konstantinos Palaiologos [the future Emperor Konstantinos XI] but was captured after falling 
2 CONC from his horse, a thoroughbred which "ameras" [the emir, unspecified] had given to “Isaacio Asani” who had later given it to “Georgio Philanthropeno genero [γαμβρω] suo” who, in turn had given it to “Comneno consobrino [ανεψιω], C
2 CONC antacuzeni protostratoris genero [γαμβρω]”[593].  '''m''' (before 29 Mar 1429) --- Komnenos, son of [Emperor in Trebizond & his second wife Anna Philanthropena. 
