2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Kantakouzenos
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodore's wife was Helena Ouresina Doukaina, a daughter of John Uroš, ruler of Thessaly.[10] He is believed to have had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.  Thomas Kantakouzenos (d. July 25, 1463 in Adrianople), diplomat for Đurađ Branković, Despot of Serbia
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/byzant/byzant5.html
2 CONT
2 CONT E3. Thomas Kantakouzenos, in the diplomatic service of George Brankovic, Despot of Serbia (his brother-in-law) (ca 1433-1456), he defeated the Kral of Bosnia on 16.9.1448 and restored Srebrnica to Serbian rule, +Adrianople 25.7.14
2 CONC 63
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2012611453.htm#TheodoraKantadied1426
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.         THOMAS Kantakouzenos (-25 Jul 1463).  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names (in order) Demetrios, Manuel, Giorgios, Andronikos, Thomas, as the sons of Theodoros & his wife[644].  Georgios Phrantzes names "Thoma Cantacu
2 CONC zeno avunculo" of "Capistranus et Serviæ princeps et despota Georgius Bulcus…filia", when recording that they went "ad ameram et amerissam" after the death of her mother 3 May 1457[645].  He lived at the court of his brother-in-la
2 CONC w Djuradj Branković of Serbia 1433/39.  He was among the defenders during the siege of Smederevo by Sultan Murad II in 1439[646].  Serbian military leader 1448/52.  
2 CONT
