2 CONT Theodore's wife was Helena Ouresina Doukaina, a daughter of John Uroš, ruler of Thessaly.[10] He is believed to have had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.  Andronikos Palaiologos Kantakouzenos (d. June 3/4, 1453, executed), the last Grand Domestic of the Byzantine Empire
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andronikos_Palaiologos_Kantakouzenos
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the genealogy of his wife Hugues Busac compiled, he was the brother of George Palaiologos Kantakouzenos, and with George possibly son of Demetrios I Kantakouzenos or his brother Theodore Kantakouzenos. He was married 
2 CONC and had at least one son who married the daughter of the megas doux Loukas Notaras. Doukas tells how the younger Kantakouzenos was accompanied by his father-in-law to their execution.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/byzant/byzant5.html
2 CONT
2 CONT *E2. '''Andronikos Palaiologos Kantakouzenos''', the last Grand Domestic of Byzantium, +executed ca 3/4.6.1453, soon after the fall of Constantinople; '''m'''.NN
2 CONT
2 CONT **F1. N Kantakouzenos, +executed after the fall of Constantinople ca 3/4.6.1453; '''m'''.N, a dau.of Grand Duke Loukas Notaras (+who was also executed in 1453 with his son-in-law)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2012611453.htm#TheodorosKantadied1410B
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         ANDRONIKOS Palaiologos Kantakouzenos (-murdered Constantinople 3 Jun 1453).  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names (in order) Demetrios, Manuel, Giorgios, Andronikos, Thomas, as the sons of Theodoros & his wife[641].  
2 CONC Megas domestikos.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---, sister of --- Protobestiarios of Trebizond [Giorgios Amiroutzes?].  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript records that Andronikos, son of Theodoros, married a sister of Provestiar of Trebizond and that the couple had sons 
2 CONC who were killed by the Turks[642].  
2 CONT
2 CONT  Andronikos Kantakouzenos & his wife had [---] children:
2 CONT *a)         THEODOROS Kantakouzenos (-murdered Constantinople 3 Jun 1453).  He was beheaded with his brother-in-law and father-in-law on the orders of Sultan Murad II after the fall of Constantinople[643].  <br> '''m''' MARIA Nota
2 CONC raina, daughter of LUKAS Notaras megas dux & his wife --- Palaiologina. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         sons (-murdered Constantinople 3 Jun 1453). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
