2 CONT =The Palaiologos family=
2 CONT
2 CONT The early generations of this family are confused and uncertain. The first certain ancestor is one Andronikos Dukas Komnenos Palaiologos, Gov of Thessalonica, +after 1246; m.his cousin Theodora Palaiologina; they had issue:
2 CONT *A1. MICHAÉL VIII Dukas Komnenos Palaiologos, Emperor of Byzantium (1259-82), *1224/5, +1282; m.1253 Theodora Dukaina Batatzaina (*1240 +1303)
2 CONT **B1. Manuel, *1254/7, +ca 1259
2 CONT **B2. '''ANDRONIKOS II Palaiologos, Emp of Byzantium (1282-1328), *25.3.1259, +Monte Athos 13.2.1332'''; 1m: 1273 Anna (+1281/2) dau.of King Stephen V of Hungary; 2m: 1285 Yolanda=Eirene of Montferrat (*1274 +1317)
2 CONT ***C1. [1m.] MICHAÉL IX Palaiologos, co-emperor of Byzantium (1295-1320), *1277, +12.10.1320; m.1295 Rita of Armenia (*1278 +VII.1333)
2 CONT *** ...
2 CONT ***C2. [1m.] Konstantinos Palaiologos, despot of Thessalonica, +after 1329; 1m: 1295 Theodora Muzalon; 2m: Eudokia Neokaisareitissa
2 CONT ****D1. [illegitimate] Michael Katharos
2 CONT ***C3. [2m.] Ioannes Palaiologos, Despot of Thessalonica, *1286, +1307; m.1303 Eirene Chumnaina (*1292, +1360)
2 CONT ***C4. [2m.] Theodoros Palaiologos, Marquis de Montferrat (1306-38), *Constantinople 1291, +Casale 21.4.1338, he inherted his mothers margravate of Montferrat; m.Hagia Sophia, Constantinople IX.1307 Argentina Spinola (+before 1338
2 CONC ), dau.of Obizino di Corrado Spinola, Duke of Genoa by Violante di Saluzzo; for his issue see HERE
2 CONT ***C5. [2m.] Demetrios Angelodukas Palaiologos, +after 1343
2 CONT ***C6. [2m.] Bartholomaios, +young
2 CONT ***C7. [2m.] Isaakios, +young
2 CONT ***C8. [2m.] Theodora, +young C9. [2m.] Simonis, *1292/93, +after 1336; m.1300 King Stepan Uros II of Serbia (+29.10.1321)
2 CONT ***C10. [illegitimate] Maria; m.Tochtu Khan of the Golden Horde
2 CONT ***C11. [illegitimate] Eirene; m.1315 Ioannes Dukas Angelos, Archon of Neiapatrai
2 CONT ** ...
