1 NOTE {geni:about_me} By Uzun Hasan, Theodora had several children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Yakub, who is not the son of Uzun Hasan who succeeded him as ruler of the Aq Qoyunlu; Bryer believes he was killed by another wife of Uzun Hasan soon after his death in 1478; Marta (also called Halima), who married Shaykh Haydar i
2 CONC n 1471/1472; Martha became the mother of first Safavid king, Shah Ismail I, who became the ruler of Iran and established Shia Islam as the state religion. Two other daughters. These Caterino Zeno met in Damascus, where he spoke to
2 CONC  them in Pontic Greek.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was killed by her son Shah Ismail I because she attempted to divert him from the path of heresy and cruelty. ref: page 119 of
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.academia.edu/4460261/Depicting_the_Other_Qizilbash_Image_in_the_16th_Century_Ottoman_Historiography?email_work_card=view-paper
2 CONT ========
2 CONT
2 CONT She was imprisoned with her 3 sons in the fort of Estakhr in Fars, by Jakub beg (Soltan Yaqub) Aq Qoyunlu/Uzun Hassan's son.:
2 CONT
2 CONT [Being envious of Sultan Haydar's increasing power, Ya'qiib Mirza seized the opportunity of helping Farrukh Yasgr, the ShirwSn Shah, against Sultan Haydar, who had set out from Ardabil for the invasion of CharkaS,' and Daghistan. 
2 CONC In the ensuing battle, on Rajah 20, 893/July 1, 1488, Sultan Haydar lost his life, and his son and successor, Sultan 'All Mirza aroused the suspicion of Ya'qiib Mirza, whereupon, in the end of Rabi' II, 894/end of March 1489, Sult
2 CONC an 'All Mirza, his brothers, Ibrahim Mirza and Isma'il Mirza, and their mother, were imprisoned in the fort of Istakhr in Fars.] ref: https://archive.org/stream/HistoryOfShahIsmailSafawi-GhulamSarwar/119900259-History-of-Shah-Isma
