2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Regnant Bigum khatun of Qara Quyunlu
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Jahanshah (1435-67) she held power before the Hassan Ali came on the throne of the Emirate of Qara Qoyunu, Turkmen vassals of the Jalayirids in Eastern Anatolia. They became independent in 1389, after the Jalayi
2 CONC rids had been overrun by Tamerlane's Timurids. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Blue Mosque also known as the Kabud mosque of Tabriz was built by order of Beygom (Beigum) Khatun, the spouse of Jahan shah and restored by their  daughter Saleheh Jahanshahi. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It is said that the mosque construction is a monument for remembrance of victories of Jahanshah. This is why the Al-fath, verses of Quran, is written around the entrance of the mosque.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jahanshah and his immediate family are buried in the Blue Mosque.
2 CONT
2 CONT For further information please visit the below links:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.irandokht.com/editorial/print.php?area=pro&sectionID=11&editorialID=3147
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=sP_hVmik-QYC&pg=PA588&lpg=PA588&dq=begum+khatun&source=bl&ots=uVMULi-3KV&sig=d5xLoMaCEsUFur1bnPhDEUoavks&hl=en&ei=M6IxSrz_NdrKjAeS7PiOCg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=6
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexios_IV_of_Trebizond
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1395, Alexios married Theodora Kantakouzene. They had at least six children:[15]
2 CONT
2 CONT * A daughter who married Jahan Shah.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jahan_Shah
2 CONT
2 CONT Abu al-Muzaffar Jahan Shah was the leader of the Qara Qoyunlu Oghuz Turkic tribal confederacy in Azerbaijan and Arran who reigned c. 1438 – 1467.  … He was married several times. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Known marriages include: 
2 CONT * a daughter of Alexios IV of Trebizond[7][32] and 
2 CONT * Jan Begüm (daughter Tajuddin Rajab bin Afridun):
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons
2 CONT * Pirbudag – governor of Isfahan and Fars, then Baghdad. Killed by Mirza Muhammad.
2 CONT * Hasan Ali succeeded his father.
2 CONT * Mirza Muhammad – son-in-law to Jahangir Beg, captured on 11 November 1467 at the Battle of Chapakchur and executed.
2 CONT * Mirza Yusuf – captured on 11 November 1467 at the Battle of Chapakchur and blinded. Executed by Ughurlu Muhammad on 22 October 1469.
2 CONT * Qasim Beg
2 CONT Daughters
2 CONT * Saliha Khatun
2 CONT * Habiba Khatun
2 CONT * Tutuq 'Ismat, married to Sultan Muhammad, Timurid ruler[33]
2 CONT * A daughter married to descendant of Nimatullah Vali
