2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pir_Budaq
2 CONT
2 CONT Abu'l-Fath Pir Budaq (died 1466) more commonly known simply as '''Pir Budaq''' (alternatively Pir Budak or Pir Budagh), son of Jahān Shāh of the Qara Qoyunlu dynasty, was governor of Shiraz (1456–1460) and of Baghdad (1460–66) whe
2 CONC re he introduced a period of political and economic stability.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1411–1469 The Qara Quyunlu dynasty controls Iraq. Pir Budaq, governor of Baghdad under his father Jahanshah (r. 1439–67), the most famous Qara Quyunlu ruler, is a noted patron of the arts of the book. Artists invited from differen
2 CONC t parts of the eastern Islamic world bring together the styles of Tabriz and Shiraz in Iran as well as of Timurid Central Asia. It is said that following the death of Pir Budaq in 1467, Baghdad's importance as a center of artistic
2 CONC  production declines.
2 CONT
