2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirza_Yusuf
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mirza Yusuf''' (Persian: میرزا یوسف; Azerbaijani: Mirzə Yusif) died 22 October 1469, r. 1468–1469) was the last sultan of the Qara Qoyunlu, also known as the Black Sheep Turkomans, to have significant authority.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died	22 October 1469
2 CONT Spouse	Daughter of Ali Shukr Beg Baharlu
2 CONT Issue	Khadija Begum
2 CONT Dynasty	Qara Qoyunlu
2 CONT Father	Jahan Shah
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mirza Yusuf's daughter Khadija Begum married Alvand Mirza's son Pir Quli Beg. Their grandson Quli Qutb Mulk later founded the Qutb Shahi dynasty of India.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jahan_Shah was married several times. Known marriages include: a daughter of Alexios IV of Trebizond[7][32] and Jan Begüm (daughter Tajuddin Rajab bin Afridun):
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons
2 CONT * Pirbudag – governor of Isfahan and Fars, then Baghdad. Killed by Mirza Muhammad.
2 CONT * Hasan Ali succeeded his father.
2 CONT * Mirza Muhammad – son-in-law to Jahangir Beg, captured on 11 November 1467 at the Battle of Chapakchur and executed.
2 CONT * Mirza Yusuf – captured on 11 November 1467 at the Battle of Chapakchur and blinded. Executed by Ughurlu Muhammad on 22 October 1469.
2 CONT * Qasim Beg
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
