2 CONT Preljub died in late 1355, or early 1356, shortly after Dušan himself, in a clash with local Albanian clans.[6] His widow, Irene Asanina, a daughter of Dushan, and their son Thomas, soon faced an invasion by Nikephoros Orsini, the
2 CONC  former Despot of Epirus. Orsini managed to rally the Greek inhabitants of the province to his side, forcing Irene to return to Serbia. In 1357, she married Radoslav Hlapen, the governor of much of western Macedonia, including Vod
2 CONC ena and Berrhoea.[7] In 1366/67, Thomas became ruler of the Despotate of Epirus at Ioannina.[8]
