2 CONT i)          ANNA Palaiologina Angelina (-after 1355).  Ioannes Kantakuzenus names "Annæ…filiæ protovestiarii" as the wife of "Ioannis despotæ"[90].  Nicephoras Gregoras names "Anna" as wife of "Ioannes…Angelus…Cephalonum comitis"[
2 CONC 91].  She poisoned her first husband, becoming regent of Epirus in 1335/1339 and 1341-1342.  She was imprisoned in Constantinople 1342/49.  The Historia Epiri records that "mater…Thomaidis…eiusque fratris…Anna regina nostra" marri
2 CONC ed "cuidam ex Bulgaris, Comneno tyranno, fratri regis Stephani", adding that he ruled "Caninam et Belgradam"[92].  
2 CONT
