2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00064448&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT The interesting fact, not noticed in any English record or 
2 CONT  publication, that Hamon married Isabelle d'Ybelin, Queen of 
2 CONT  Cyprus, was discovered by my brother Guy in the French record, 
2 CONT  styled the Assizes de Jerusalem, published at Paris by Comte 
2 CONT  Beugnot in 1843. In the chapter entitled 'Les Lignages d'Outre- 
2 CONT  mer ' x is given a long pedigree of the house of Ybelin, derived from 
2 CONT  ' Balian le Francois, frere au comte Giulin de Chartres,' to whom 
2 CONT  Fulk of Anjou, King of Jerusalem, gave Ybelin, so that he and 
2 CONT  his heirs were called de Ybelin. Balian's grandson, Jehan, received 
2 CONT  the fief of Beyrout from Queen Isabeau of Jerusalem, and he 
2 CONT  and his descendants were thereafter known as ' Sire de Baruth,' 
2 CONT  or ' Dame de Baruth.' Jean, Sire de Baruth, grandson of the 
2 CONT  above-named Jehan, married Aalis, daughter of the Duke of 
2 CONT  Athens, and they had a daughter, called Isabeau or Isabelle, 
2 CONT  who was married four times. Her first husband was Hugh II, 
2 CONT  King of Cyprus, who died at the age of fourteen. Her second 
2 CONT  husband was Hamon le Strange ; after his death she married, 
2 CONT  thirdly, in 1277, Nicholas Prince of Cesarea, and, fourthly, Guil- 
2 CONT  laume Barlais; after all these marriages the chronicler adds, 
2 CONT  ' Et moru sans heirs.' The passage in the ' Lignages d'Outremer ' 
2 CONT  which records the marriage to Hamon runs as follows : 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Jehan fu Seignor de Baruth puis la mort son frere et esposa Aalis fille dou 
2 CONT  Due d'Atenes et orent deus filles, Isabeau et Eschive. Isabeau esposa Hughes 
2 CONT  fis de Henry roy de Chipre, qui moru de quatorze ans, si com a este dit ci- 
2 CONT  devant ; puis esposa un Engles qui avoit nom Reimont l'Estrange. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  The continuator of the chronicle of William of Tyre, printed 
2 CONT  in the 'Recueil des Historiens des Croisades,' also mentions this 
2 CONT  marriage : 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Anno m.cc.lxxii. En cet ans meismes fu marie la Dame de Baruth a 
2 CONT  Sire Heimont l'Estrange. 2 
2 CONT
2 CONT  and the mention of the lady's third marriage in 1277 is proof, if 
2 CONT  that were needed, that Hamon was then dead : 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Anno m.cc.lxx.vij. Nicolas Syres de Cesaire qui novelement avoit espousee 
2 CONT  la Dame de Baruth fu occis en Chypre a Nicosie par la main de Syre Baudouin 
2 CONT
2 CONT  1 Chap. viii. 448-449. * P. 462 @ Lib. xxxiv. cap. xv.  Source: http://www.ebooksread.com/authors-eng/edwin-williams/lestrange-records-a-chronicle-of-the-early-lestranges-of-norfolk-and-the-march--dno/page-14-lestrange-records-a-
2 CONC chronicle-of-the-early-lestranges-of-norfolk-and-the-march--dno.shtml
