2 CONT THEODOROS Kantakouzenos ([1425?]-after 1456).  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names (in order) Theodoros, Manuel, Thomas, Demetrios and Andronikos as the five surviving sons of Georgios & his wife[597].  The manuscript Vaticanus
2 CONC  latinus 4789 records that “le seigneur Georges Cantacuzène” had four sons (in order) “le seigneur Théodore...le seigneur Manuel, le seigneur Thomas et le seigneur Démétrius”[598].  In Serbia 1453/56.  '''m HELENA Kantakouzene, da
2 CONC ughter of IOANNES Kantakouzenos & [his first wife ---] ([1425/30?]-). ''' The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names Helena, daughter of Ioannes as the wife of Theodoros Kantakouzenos, son of Georgios[599].  Her birth date is estimate
2 CONC d from the suggested birth date of her husband, bearing in mind that she gave birth to four children (who may have been born before the 1453 capture of Constantinople by the Ottomans).  Theodoros Kantakouzenos & his wife had four 
2 CONC children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          GEORGIOS .  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names (in order) Georgios, Maria, Eudokia and Alexandra as the children of Theodoros, son of Georgios, and his wife[600].  m EIRENE, daughter of a Grand Chancellor of the Tu
2 CONC rks [Georgios Amiroutzes?].  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names Eirene, daughter of the Grand Chancellor of the Turks, as the wife of Georgios, son of Theodoros, and that the couple had two children[601].  Georgios Kantakouzen
2 CONC os & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       two children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         MARIA .  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names (in order) Georgios, Maria, Eudokia and Alexandra as the children of Theodoros, son of Georgios, and his wife, stating that Maria married Ierachi[602].  m --- Ierachi, so
2 CONC n of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT iii)        EVDOKIA Kantakouzene (-after 9 Dec 1488).  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names (in order) Georgios, Maria, Eudokia and Alexandra as the children of Theodoros, son of Georgios, and his wife, stating that Eudokia marr
2 CONC ied Matthaios Spandounes[603].  Her son, Theodoros Spandounes, described Helena Kantakouzene (see below), widow of David Emperor in Trebizond, as "sorella de mio avo materno"[604], which is consistent with his mother having been t
2 CONC he daughter of one of the ex-empress's brothers (although the existence of that Helena is placed in doubt by other sources: see the last paragraph of the present document).  In Venice 1453/88.  A document dated 18 Jun 1475 records
2 CONC  donations by "domine Anne Paleologine Hermineutine filie quondam…Megaduche Constantinopolis et domine Eudochie Cantacusini uxoris…Mathei Spandonini"[605].  "Catherina comitissa Cillii" donated "castrum Bellogradi" to "Mathaeo Spa
2 CONC ndonino equiti et comiti palatino" for the love of "nepotis sue, uxoris dicti Mathaei" by document dated 9 Dec 1488 at Constantinople[606].  m (before 18 Jun 1475) MATTHAIOS Spandounes [Spandugnino], son of --- (-before 1511).  Ve
2 CONC netian Stratiotes.  Reichsgraf und Herr of Loidoriki and Trizonia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT iv)        ALEXANDRA .  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names (in order) Georgios, Maria, Eudokia and Alexandra as the children of Theodoros, son of Georgios, and his wife, stating that Alexandra married Conneu[607].  m --- Conne
2 CONC u, son of ---. 
