2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT Not to be confused with Mara Branković.
2 CONT Maria of Serbia, Marchioness of Montferrat
2 CONT Princess of Serbia, Marchioness of Montferrat
2 CONT Born	1466
2 CONT Died	27 August 1495
2 CONT Noble family	Branković dynasty
2 CONT Palaiologos
2 CONT Spouse(s)	Boniface III, Marquess of Montferrat
2 CONT Issue	William IX, Marquess of Montferrat
2 CONT John George, Marquess of Montferrat
2 CONT Father	Stefan Branković
2 CONT Mother	Angjelina Arianiti
2 CONT Maria of Serbia or Marija Branković (Serbian Cyrillic: Марија Бранковић; 1466 – 27 August 1495) was Princess of Serbia by birth, and Marchioness of Montferrat by marriage. She was regent of Montferrat during the minority of her so
2 CONC n in 1494-1495.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was daughter of despot Stefan Branković of Serbia and the Albanian Princess Angjelina Arianiti. In 1485, she married Boniface III, Marquess of Montferrat.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Since 1459, when Serbia fell under Ottoman rule,[2] Maria's father, Despot Stefan Branković, was living in exile, mainly in northern Italy, where Maria was born in 1466. In 1485, she married Boniface III Palaiologos, marquess of M
2 CONC ontferrat, who fell ill in 1493, and Maria became regent.[3] Boniface died in 1494, and his widow continued to act as regent since their sons were still minor. Maria died in 1495.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria and Boniface had two sons: William IX (1486-1518), who became Marquess of Montferrat between 1494 and 1518, and John George (1488-1533) who became the last Marquess of Montferrat, between 1530 and 1533.
