2 CONT 1.         FRANCESCO Crispo (-1397).  Baron of Astrogidis in Eubœa.  Lord of Milos 1376.  After murdering his predecessor, he succeeded in 1383 as FRANCESCO I Duke of Naxos, supported by Venice which was pleased that he made no mo
2 CONC ve to succeed the late Duke in his property on the island of Eubœa[801].  He captured the island of Andros which he gave as dowry to his daughter[802].  He left his territories to be divided between his five sons[803].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' FIORENZA Sanudo, daughter of MARCO [Marcolino] Sanudo Lord of Milos & his wife --- (-1437).  Her marriage is confirmed by the 16th century Annali Veneti of Stefano Magno which records that "Pietro Zen et Petronilla sua mog
2 CONC ier" were granted "dominio dell´ isola di Andre" by "Franguli Crispo suo padre et Fiorenza sua madre Duca et Duchessa dell´ Arcipelago"[804].  She succeeded in 1383 as FIORENZA II Dss of Naxos.  
2 CONT
2 CONT  Duke Francesco & his wife had eight children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
