1 OCCU 11th Duke of Naxos and of the Archipelagos 1397, etc., eleventh Duke of the Archipelago (1397-1418)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giacomo_I_Crispo
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20LORDSHIPS%20IN%20GREECE.htm#GiacopoCrispoINaxosdied1418
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         GIACOPO Crispo (-Ferrara 1418).  He succeeded his father in 1397 as GIACOPO I Duke of Naxos.  In 1416, Sultan Mohammed I sent a Turkish fleet to attack the Cyclades, in response to the Duke's failure to salute him at Sm
2 CONC yrna[805].  A Venetian charter dated 17 Nov 1419 records the death "in partibus Ferrarie" of "domini Jacobi Crispo Duche Egeopelagi"[806].  Duke Giacopo died on his way to meet Pope Martin V at Mantua[807].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed''' to ELISABETTA Sanudo, daughter of NICOLÒ Sanudo "Spezzabanda" & his second wife Fiorenza II Dss of Naxos.  1384/1460.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' FIORENZA di Sommaripa, daughter of GASPARO di Sommaripa & his wife Maria Sanudo of Naxos (-after 13 Jan 1436).  The 16th century Annali Veneti of Stefano Magno names "Fiorenza" as wife of "Giacomo Crespo olim Duca", in a l
2 CONC ater passage specifying that she was "Fiorenza Sumaripa" and made her testament 13 Jan 1436[808].  Heiress of Paros, confiscated by her brother-in-law Duke Giovanni II after the death of her husband, but restored after pressure fr
2 CONC om Venice[809].  A Venetian charter dated 19 Jun 1423 records disputes between "Petro Geno", "dominam Mariam Sanuto" and "domina Florentia relicta quondam…domini Jacobi Crispo, olim Duche Egeopelagi" regarding succession to the is
2 CONC lands of "Andre, Parii et Antiparii et Melos"[810].  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Duke Giacopo & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *i)          daughter .  m (1419) ANDREA Dandolo . 
2 CONT
2 CONT *ii)         daughter .  m (1424) GIOVANNI Michieli .  
