1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Roman Mstislavich (Роман Мстиславич, c. 1151 - 1205) was the Prince of Novgorod, Volodymyr, Halych and Kiev. Also known as Roman the Great.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1197 he married Anna, by whom he had four children, including Daniel of Galicia. One of Roman's daughters Maria married Michael of Chernigov, Grand Prince of Kiev.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1205, after the death of his father, Roman Mstyslavich, the ruler of Galicia-Volhynia, the boyars of Galicia forced the four-year-old Daniel into exile with his mother Anna of Byzantium and brother Vasilko.
