2 CONT Amadeus V (between 1249 and 1253 – 16 October 1323, Avignon), surnamed the Great for his wisdom and success as a ruler, was the Count of Savoy from 1285 to 1323. He established Chambéry as his seat. He was the son of Thomas II of 
2 CONC Savoy and Beatrice Fieschi.
2 CONT
