2 CONT '''Süleyman Çelebi''' (also '''Emîr Süleyman''', Ottoman Turkish: سليمان چلبى; 1377 – February 17, 1411) was an Ottoman prince (Turkish: şehzade) and a co-ruler of the empire for several years during the Ottoman Interregnum. There
2 CONC  is a tradition of western origin, according to which Suleiman the Magnificent was "Suleiman II", but that tradition has been based on an erroneous assumption that Süleyman Çelebi was to be recognised as a legitimate sultan.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT #[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%BCleyman_%C3%87elebi#Background Background] ...
2 CONT
2 CONT #[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%BCleyman_%C3%87elebi#Ottoman_Interregnum Ottoman Interregnum] ... ... ...
2 CONT
2 CONT #[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%BCleyman_%C3%87elebi#Aftermath Aftermath] ... 
2 CONT
2 CONT #Family:
2 CONT
2 CONT Süleyman married two times:
2 CONT #A [https://www.geni.com/people/Doria/6000000184198891831 daughter] of Ilario Doria and his wife Zampia Palaiologina, illegitimate daughter of Emperor Manuel II Palaiologos, married in 1403;
2 CONT #A [https://www.geni.com/people/N-a-Palaiologina/6000000063589686821 daughter] of Theodore I Palaiologos, Despot of Morea and his unnamed mistress, married in 1404;
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He had three children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/people/Orhan-%C3%87elebi-Ottoman-Prince/6000000204999693838 Şehzade Orhan Çelebi] (died 1429);
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/people/Mehmed%C5%9Fah/6000000184208918822 Şehzade Mehmedşah] (died 30 December 1421);
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/people/Pa%C5%9Famelek-Hatun/6000000184208893823 Paşamelek Hatun], married to a Sanjak Bey.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
