1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manuel_Komnenos_(son_of_Andronikos_I)_
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel Komnenos (born 1145)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel Komnenos (Greek: Μανουήλ Κομνηνός, Manouēl Komnēnos) (1145 – 1185?) was the eldest son of Andronikos Komnenos (who was Byzantine Emperor 1183-1185) by his first wife, whose name is not recorded.
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps around 1180 Manuel married Rusudan of Georgia, daughter of King George III. He thus became brother-in-law of Queen Tamar of Georgia. Manuel and Rusudan had two sons, Alexios and David Komnenos, who were to be the joint fou
2 CONC nders of the Empire of Trebizond. Alexios was probably born in 1182; David's date of birth must be about 1184.
2 CONT
2 CONT In September 1185, when his father was deposed and killed, Manuel was blinded. He may have died as a result of this; at any rate he disappears from the historical record in that year.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Bibliography
2 CONT
2 CONT C. Toumanoff, "On the relationship between the founder of the Empire of Trebizond and the Georgian Queen Thamar" in Speculum vol. 15 (1940) pp. 299-312.
2 CONT
2 CONT Varzos, K. (1984), written at Thessaloniki, Ē genealogia tōn Komnēnōn
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Manuel Komnenos (Greek: Μανουήλ Κομνηνός, Manouēl Komnēnos) (1145 – 1185?) was the eldest son of Andronikos Komnenos (who was Byzantine Emperor 1183-1185) by his first wife, whose name is not recorded.
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps around 1180 Manuel married Rusudan of Georgia, daughter of King George III. He thus became brother-in-law of Queen Tamar of Georgia. Manuel and Rusudan had two sons, Alexios and David Komnenos, who were to be the joint fou
2 CONC nders of the Empire of Trebizond. Alexios was probably born in 1182; David's date of birth must be about 1184.
2 CONT
2 CONT In September 1185, when his father was deposed and killed, Manuel was blinded. He may have died as a result of this; at any rate he disappears from the historical record in that year.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Bibliography
2 CONT
2 CONT C. Toumanoff, "On the relationship between the founder of the Empire of Trebizond and the Georgian Queen Thamar" in Speculum vol. 15 (1940) pp. 299–312.
2 CONT
2 CONT Varzos, K. (1984), Ē genealogia tōn Komnēnōn, Thessaloniki
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Manuel Komnenos (Greek: Μανουήλ Κομνηνός, Manouēl Komnēnos; 1145–1185?) was the eldest son of Byzantine Emperor Andronikos Komnenos (r. 1183–1185) by his first wife, whose name is not recorded.
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps around 1180 Manuel married Rusudan of Georgia, daughter of King George III. He thus became brother-in-law of Queen Tamar of Georgia. Manuel and Rusudan had two sons, Alexios and David Komnenos, who were to be the joint fou
2 CONC nders of the Empire of Trebizond. Alexios was probably born in 1182; David's date of birth must be about 1184.
2 CONT
2 CONT In September 1185, when his father was deposed and killed, Manuel was blinded. He may have died as a result of this; at any rate he disappears from the historical record in that year.
