1 NOTE {geni:about_me} David married secondly to Tamar (died in 1554), daughter of Kvarkvare II Jaqeli, Atabag of Samtskhe. She might have been the mother of all of David's children, including his eldest son and successor Luarsab I. Prin
2 CONC ce Vakhushti reports that the mother of Luarsab was captured by Shah Tahmasp I at Ateni and carried off to Iran, where she committed suicide by poisoning in 1556. According to Cyril Toumanoff, Nestan-Darejan/Miraingul was the moth
2 CONC er of David's three sons, Luarsab, Adarnase, and Ramaz, and it was she who committed suicide in 1556. He considers Tamar to have been the third name of this queen, such polyonymy not being infrequent in Georgia at that time.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''NOTE:''' Wikipedia claims that Tamar was the daughter of Kvarkvare II Jaqeli. However, Kvarkvare II Jaqeli died about a century before Tamar did, so this relationship is unlikely. Further, Kvarkvare II Jaqeli already has a daug
2 CONC hter named Tamar, and this Tamar is the wife of George VIII of Georgia (who lived from 1417-1476).
2 CONT
2 CONT * From the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_X_of_Kartli#Family '''Wikipedia'''] page of her husband, David X of Kartli:
2 CONT
2 CONT David, as crown prince, first married Nestan-Darejan or Miraingul, daughter of Prince David Baratashvili (fl. 1488–1512), but the union was denounced by David's father, Constantine II.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT David married secondly to Tamar (died in 1554), daughter of Kvarkvare II Jaqeli, Atabag of Samtskhe. She might have been the mother of all of David's children, including his eldest son and successor Luarsab I. Prince Vakhushti rep
2 CONC orts that the mother of Luarsab was captured by Shah Tahmasp I at Ateni and carried off to Iran, where she committed suicide by poisoning in 1556. According to Cyril Toumanoff, Nestan-Darejan/Miraingul was the mother of David's th
2 CONC ree sons, Luarsab, Adarnase, and Ramaz, and it was she who committed suicide in 1556. He considers Tamar to have been the third name of this queen, such polyonymy not being infrequent in Georgia at that time.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT David had eight children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Luarsab I, King of Kartli
2 CONT * Adarnase (fl. 1512–1558)
2 CONT * Prince Ramaz of Kartli
2 CONT * Demetre (Dimitri) (fl. 1516–1540)
2 CONT * Bezhan, died of leprosy
2 CONT * Anonymous daughter (fl. 1519–1560), wife of Baindur, Duke of Aragvi
2 CONT * Anonymous daughter (fl. 1532–1534), wife of Prince Javakh Chiladze
2 CONT * Anonymous daughter
