1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Sommaire=
2 CONT * Marquis de Montferrat (1530-1533) :
2 CONT ** précédé de [http://www.geni.com/people/Bonifacio-IV-Paleologo/6000000009183760948 Boniface IV]
2 CONT ** sans succession; Jean-Georges fût le dernier marquis de Montferrat de la dynastie Paléologue
2 CONT ** [http://www.geni.com/people/Federico-II-di-Mantova/6000000008520003216 Frédéric II de Mantoue] de la [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maison_de_Gonzague maison de Gonzague] prend possession du marquisat de Montferrat
2 CONT * Jean-Georges fut évêque de Cazal et abbé de Locedio.
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT * [http://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000027609064898 Moreri, L., ''Le Grand Dictionnaire Historique -- Les Montferrat'', 1759] (ci-joint)
2 CONT * [http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marchesato_del_Monferrato#Periodo_Paleologo Marchesato del Monferrato, Wikipédia]
2 CONT * [http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giovanni_Giorgio_del_Monferrato Giovanni Giorgio del Monferrato, Wikipédia]
2 CONT * [http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gonzaga Gonzaga, Wikipédia]
2 CONT * [http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federico_II_di_Mantova Federico II di Mantova, Wikipédia]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONFERRATO,%20SALUZZO,%20SAVONA.htm#GianGiorgioSebastianoIdied1533
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.      '''   GIAN GIORGIO SEBASTIANO''' (20 Jan 1488-Casale 30 Apr 1533).  A continuation of the Chronica Jacobi de Aquis names "Gulielmo & Zoanne Georgio" as the two sons of "Bonifacio", third son of "Zoanne Jacobo figlolo di Te
2 CONC odoro", and his wife "Maria di Servia"[376].  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names (in order) Guglielmo and Zanzorzi as the children of Bonifazio marchese of Monferrato and his wife[377].  A manuscript which records details of t
2 CONC he Musaki family names "il primo…signor Guglielmo…l´altro…signor Giorgio" as the two sons of "il signor marchese de Monferrato" and his wife "signora Maria", adding that Giorgio died childless[378].  Signor di Mombelo e Morano to 
2 CONC 1530.  Abbot of Lucedo 1509.  Apostolic protonotary.  Bishop-coadjutor of Casale.  Bishop of Casale 1517.  He resigned his ecclesiastical appointments in 1524.  He succeeded his nephew in 1530 as GIAN GIORGIO SEBASTIANO Marchese d
2 CONC i Monferrato.  He died as his wife made her formal entry to Monferrato.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (Ferrara 29 Apr 1533) GIULIA di Aragona, daughter of FEDERIGO IV King of Naples & his second wife Isabella del Balzo (1492-Valencia 10 Mar 1542).  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript records that Zanzorzi married Isabella cou
2 CONC sin of the king of Naples but died without issue[379].
2 CONT    Marchese Gian Giorgio Sebastiano had one illegitimate child by an unknown mistress: 
2 CONT *a)         FLAMINIO Paleologo (-24 May 1571).  Signor di San Giorgio e Caluso 1532.  He served in the Spanish army.  Governor of Casale and Senator 1559.  He claimed the throne of Monferrato in 1568 and was imprisoned.  -        
2 CONC see below. 
2 CONT
