1 NOTE {geni:about_me}   sources:
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ambrogio_Contarini
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/ambrogio-contarini_(Dizionario-Biografico) 
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/ambrogio-contarini_(Enciclopedia-Italiana) (+1499)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *  [https://www.geni.com/people/Caterina-Cornaro-regina-di-Cipro/6000000008467548795 Caterina Cornaro], regina di Cipro is '''Ambrogio Contarini''', governor of Nauplia[https://www.geni.com/path/Ambrogio-Contarini-governor-of-Naup
2 CONC lia+is+related+to+Caterina-Cornaro-regina-di-Cipro?from=6000000092678596829&path_type=inlaw&to=6000000008467548795  's wife's first cousin!]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT In Sir George Hill's History of Cyprus Volume III p.666 we read that Giorgio Contarini is 'cousin-german and counselor' of Queen Caterina (Catherine) Cornaro of Cyprus.  Cousin-german means first degree cousin. Looking at Catherin
2 CONC e Cornaro's tree (above) I find Ambrogio Contarini as her only first cousin from the Contarini family.  Based on Hill and Catherin Cornaro's tree we can be as sure as we can that Ambrogio Contarini is the father of Giorgio I Conta
2 CONC rini, count of Jaffa and Ascelon. He is the husband of Catherine's first cousin, Margherita Crispo.
2 CONT *[Sir George Hill's History of Cyprus Volume III, Cambridge University Press 1972]  <br> ''{sources for personal notes, not pure quotation}  ''
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
