1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Francesco Cornaro (1478 – 26 September 1543) was an Italian cardinal.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Venice. He was made cardinal on 20 December 1527 by Pope Clement VII in his fourth consistorium. He was installed as Cardinal Priest of San Pancrazio on 27 April 1528.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was appointed Apostolic Administrator (and possibly later bishop) of Brescia in March 1531; he resigned his office in Brescia in March 1532.
2 CONT
2 CONT In April 1534 he was appointed Cardinal Priest of Santa Cecilia in Trastevere, in September 1534, Cardinal Priest of San Ciriaco alle Terme Diocleziane and in May 1535 Cardinal Priest of Santa Prassede. In March 1541 he was appoin
2 CONC ted Cardinal Priest of Santa Maria in Trastevere. Later in 1541, in November, he was appointed Cardinal Bishop of Albano, and in February 1543 Cardinal Bishop of Palestrina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cardinal Cornaro died in Viterbo.
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesco_Cornaro_(cardinal)_#
2 CONT * https://cardinals.fiu.edu/bios1527-iv.htm#Cornaro
