2 CONT Muscovites prepare for the Siege of Moscow
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Tokhtamysh kills his wife "Tovlunbek."
2 CONT Among others, Tokhtamysh had married the widow of Mamai, probably identical with a daughter of Berdi Beg and with the Tulun Beg Khanum who had briefly ruled at Sarai in 1370–1371; in 1386 he had her executed, apparently for partic
2 CONC ipating in an obscure conspiracy.[38] According to the Muʿizz al-ansāb, Tokhtamysh had eight sons and five daughters, as well as six grandchildren, as follows.[39]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jalāl ad-Dīn (1380–1412) (by Ṭaghāy-Bīka), Khan of the Golden Horde 1411–1412
2 CONT Abū-Saʿīd
2 CONT Amān Beg
2 CONT Karīm Berdi, Khan of the Golden Horde 1409, 1412–1413, 1414 (d. 1417?)
2 CONT Sayyid Aḥmad, possibly Khan of the Golden Horde 1416–1417 (he is distinct from Sayyid Aḥmad, Khan 1432–1459)[40]
2 CONT Kebek, Khan of the Golden Horde 1413–1414
2 CONT Chaghatāy-Sulṭān
2 CONT Sarāy-Mulk
2 CONT Shīrīn-Bīka
2 CONT Jabbār Berdi, Khan of the Golden Horde 1414–1415, 1416–1417
2 CONT Qādir Berdi (by a Circassian concubine), Khan of the Golden Horde 1419
2 CONT Abū-Saʿīd
2 CONT Iskandar (by Ūrun-Bikā)
2 CONT Kūchuk Muḥammad (by Ūrun-Bikā) (he is distinct from Küchük Muḥammad, Khan 1434–1459)
2 CONT Malika (by Ṭaghāy-Bīka)
2 CONT Jānika (by Ṭaghāy-Bīka), who married Edigu
2 CONT Saʿīd-Bīka (by Ṭaghāy-Bīka)
2 CONT Bakhtī-Bīka (by Shukr-Bīka-Āghā)
2 CONT Mayram-Bīka (by Ūrun-Bikā)
