2 CONT '''Maria Asanina Palaiologina''' (Greek: Μαρία Ασανίνα Παλαιολογίνα, died 19 December 1477), better known as '''Maria of Mangup''' or '''Maria of Doros''', was the princess consort of Moldavia from September 1472 to 1475 or 1477 a
2 CONC s the second wife of Stephen the Great. Of uncertain parentage, but most likely a descendant of imperial Bulgarian and Byzantine dynasties, she belonged to the ruling class of the small Principality of Theodoro in Crimea. Her clos
2 CONC e relatives included both warring princes of Theodoro, Alexios II and Isaac, as well as Zuan Tzamplakon, diplomat and leader of Stratioti. ...
