2 CONT 2.         '''KATALIN ([1255/57]-''').  Pachymeres records that "cralem Serbiæ Stephanum Uresim…primogenitus" was already married to "regis Pannoniæ filiam" when Emperor Mikhael VIII proposed the betrothal of his second daughter t
2 CONC o Stefan Uroš I's second son[981].  Pachymeres records the marriage of "germani sui maioris Stephani" and "sororem defunctæ Augustæ, matris Augusti iunioris…filia regis Ungariæ"[982].  Her marriage was probably agreed as part of t
2 CONC he terms for her future father-in-law's release from captivity by the Hungarians in 1268[983].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [1267/68] ) STEFAN DRAGUTIN of Serbia, son of STEFAN UROŠ I King of Serbia & his wife Jelena --- (-12 Mar 1316, bur Ras).  Joint King [Mladi Kralj] of Serbia 1271.  He rebelled against his father, whom he defeated with H
2 CONC ungarian support near Gacko, and succeeded 1276 as STEFAN DRAGUTIN King of Serbia, abdicated 1282.  He proposed his son as a rival candidate for the Hungarian throne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT *Her parents: Father: ISTVÁN V, son of BÉLA IV King of Hungary & his wife Maria Laskarina of Nikaia; mother: --- of the Kumans, daughter of --- Khan of the Kumans (1240-after 1290).  
2 CONT *Her siblings:
2 CONT **1.         ELISABETH (1255-[1313/26]). m firstly (1287) as his third wife, ZAVIŠ von Rosenberg zu Skalitz und Falkenstein m secondly ([1295], repudiated [1298/99]) as his third wife, STEFAN UROŠ II MILUTIN King of Serbia
2 CONT **2.         (Herself) '''KATALIN ([1255/57]'''-). m ([1267/68]) STEFAN DRAGUTIN of Serbia
2 CONT **3.         MÁRIA ([1257]-25 Mar 1324, bur Naples, Santa Maria Donna Regina). m (Naples [May/Jun] 1270) CHARLES of Sicily Principe di Salerno. Maria & her husband had fourteen children: 
2 CONT **4.         ANNA ([1260]-[1281]). m (1274) as his first wife, co-Emperor ANDRONIKOS Palaiologos He succeeded his father in 1282 as Emperor ANDRONIKOS II. 
2 CONT **5.         LÁSZLÓ (1262-murdered Kereczeg [Körösszeg] Castle 10 Jul 1290, bur Csanad Cathedral). m (5 Sep 1272) ISABELLE of Sicily
2 CONT **6.         ANDRÁS (1268-1278). 
2 CONT *Her children:
2 CONT **a)         JELISAVETA (-1331). m (after 1283) STJEPAN Kotroman of Bosnia
2 CONT **b)         VLADISLAV (-in Hungary after 1326).  
2 CONT **c)         UROSIČ (-before 1316). He became a monk as STEFAN
2 CONT
