2 CONT
2 CONT Empress Irene, from the Comnenos mosaic in the Hagia Sofia John II Komnenos married Princess Piroska of Hungary (renamed Eirene), a daughter of King Ladislaus I of Hungary in 1104; the marriage was intended as compensation for the
2 CONC  loss of some territories to King Coloman of Hungary. She played little part in government, devoting herself to piety and their large brood of children. Eirene died on August 13, 1134 and was later venerated as Saint Eirene. John 
2 CONC II and Eirene had 8 children:
