2 CONT a)         EIRENE Komnene Angelina (-after 1203).  Niketas Choniates names "Contostephanus Andronicus et Isaacius Comenus" as "duo generi" of Emperor Alexios[776].  Ephræmius records that "filiarum…Irene natu maior" married "Andro
2 CONC nico…de Contostephanis"[777].  Niketas Choniates records the second marriage of "imperator…filias…Irenem" and "Alexio Paleologo"[778].  Georgius Akropolites records that "Palaeologo, qui despotæ dignitate…" married "imperatoris Al
2 CONC exii…filiarum illius…prima Irene"[779].  She went into exile in 1203.  m firstly as his second wife,''' ANDRONIKOS Kontostefanos, son of STEFANOS Kontostefanos, panhypersébastos, megas doux & his wife Anna Komnene (-[1196]).  Mega
2 CONC  drongarios.''' 
