2 CONT ** 1. '''MANFREDO''' (1140-[20/27] Feb 1215). A continuation of the Chronica Jacobi de Aquis names "Manfredo" as oldest of the four sons of "Manfredo" and his wife "Elionor…"[518].  "Mainfredus marchio…cum filio suo Mainfredo" rea
2 CONC ched agreement with the abbot of Fruttuaria by charter dated 4 Jun 1175, witnessed by "Enricus vicecomes…"[519].  He succeeded his father in [1175] as MANFREDO II Marchese di Saluzzo.  "Mainfredus filius quondam Mainfredi et Balen
2 CONC gerius filius quondam Wilielmi" donated property "in territorio de Bordello" to Staffarda by charter dated Mar 1176[520].  "Dominus Manfredus Marchio Salutiarum et domina Alaxia eius uxor…et Manfredus nepos eorum filius quondam Bo
2 CONC nifacii" invested "Wilielmum Constantiam" with "castellum de Costiglolis" by charter dated 22 Apr 1192[521].  m [firstly] (before Jun 1182) ALASIA di Monferrato, daughter of GUGLIELMO V "il Vecchio" Marchese di Monferrato & his wi
2 CONC fe Judith of Austria (-[after 24 Jun 1231]).  A continuation of the Chronica Jacobi de Aquis names "Alasia figlola di Gulielmo Marchese di Monferrato" as the first wife of "Manfredo…Marchese…di Salucio", son of "Manfredo"[522].  "
2 CONC Marchioni Manfredo marchionis Salutii filius" donated property to "Adilasie mee uxor filie Wilielmi marchionis Montisferrati" by charter dated 1182[523].  "Manfredo figlio del Marchese di Saluzzo" donated property by charter dated
2 CONC  Jun 1182 with the consent of "Adelaide sua Consorte figlia del Marchese Guglielmo di Monferrato"[524].  "Dominus Manfredus Marchio Salutiarum et domina Alaxia eius uxor…et Manfredus nepos eorum filius quondam Bonifacii" invested 
2 CONC "Wilielmum Constantiam" with "castellum de Costiglolis" by charter dated 22 Apr 1192[525].  [m secondly ALASIA, daughter of ---.  A continuation of the Chronica Jacobi de Aquis names "altra Alasia" as the second wife of "Manfredo…
2 CONC Marchese…di Salucio", son of "Manfredo", adding that the couple was childless[526].  It is not known whether this information is correct, but the following charter shows that the widow of Marchese Manfredo II was the mother of his
2 CONC  daughter Agnese.]  "Domina Alasia de Saluciis committissa uxor quondam domini Mainfredi filii quondam Bonifacii…marchionis" sold "villam Rivifrigidi" [Rifreddo] to "domine Agneti sue filie et filie dicti domini Mainfredi marchion
2 CONC is", with the advice and consent of "domini Guidonis de Plozasco", by charter dated 14 May 1219[527].  "Domine A Salutiarum comitisse" confirmed an exchange of property by Riffredo monastery by charter dated 24 Jun 1231[528].  Mar
2 CONC chese Manfredo II & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *** a) '''AGNESE''' (-after 31 Mar 1223).  "''Domina Alasia de Saluciis committissa uxor quondam domini Mainfredi filii quondam Bonifacii…marchionis" sold "villam Rivifrigidi''" [Rifreddo] to "''domine Agneti sue filie et filie di
2 CONC cti domini Mainfredi marchionis''", with the advice and consent of "''domini Guidonis de Plozasco''", by charter dated 14 May 1219[529]. Manfredo III Marchese di Saluzzo sold property at Rifreddo to "''domine Agnetis amite sua''" 
2 CONC for the construction of a monastery by charter dated 2 Apr 1220 "''domini Guidonis de Plozasco''", by charter dated 14 May 1219[530]. "''Domina Agnete filia condam domini Mainfredi marchionis de Saluciis''" bought property for Rif
2 CONC reddo monastery by charters dated 7 Dec 1222, 22 Feb 1223, 31 Mar 1223 (twice)[531]. '''m''' as his second wife, '''COMITA Judge of Torres''', son of --- (-1218). 
2 CONT *** b) '''BONIFAZIO di Saluzzo''' (-before 28 Apr 1213). A continuation of the ''Chronica Jacobi de Aquis'' names "''Bonifacio''" as oldest child of "''Manfredo…Marchese…di Salucio''" and his wife "''Alasia figlola di Gulielmo Mar
2 CONC chese di Monferrato''"[532]. "''Bonifacius filius comitissæ''…" witnessed the charter dated 1192 under which "''Petrus Manisel filius quondam Dominici Manisel et eius nepos Oto Manisel filius quondam Johannis Manisel, D. Adalasiæ 
2 CONC comitissæ de Saluciis''" donated property to "''monasterio sancti Laurentii de Ulcio''"[533]. – see below. 
2 CONT *** c) '''MARGHERITA''' (-after 1233). '''m GOFFREDO de Salvaing''', son of ---. 
2 CONT *** d) '''daughter.''' '''m GUGLIELMO II Marchese di Ceva''', son of GUGLIELMO I Marchese di Ceva & his wife --- di Vento (-1219). 
