2 CONT Izyaslav, Pr of Kursk (1125-29), Pr of Polotsk (1129-32), Pr of Turov (1132-34), Pr of Volynia (1135-42), Pr of Pereyaslav (1142-46), Great Pr of Kiev (1146-49)+(1150)+(1151-54), *Novgorod 1096, +Kiev 13.11.1154; 1m: apparently a 
2 CONC Staufen princess (+1151); 2m: 1154 N (Rusudan?) of Georgia; all children from 1m.:
2 CONT *A1. Mstislav II, Pr of Pereyaslav (1146-49)+(1151-55), Pr of Lutzk (1155-57), Pr of Volynya (1157-70), Great Pr of Kiev (V.1167-XII.1169)+(II.1170-IV.1170), +19.8.1170; m.1151/52 Agnieszka of Poland (*1137 +after 1181)
2 CONT **B1. Roman "the Great", Pr of Novgorod (1168-70), Pr of Volynia (1173-87)+(1188-1205), Pr of Galicia (1187-88)+(1199-1205), Grand Pr of Kiev (1203-05), *ca 1205, +murdered nr Zavikhvost 19.6.1205; 1m: bef 1184 (div 1198) Predisla
2 CONC va Ryurikovna of Smolensk (+after 1204); 2m: ca 1200 a Byzantine noblewoman (+after 1219)
2 CONT ***C1. [1m.] Feodora, +after 1200; m.1187 (div 1188) Vasilko of Galicia (+after 1241)
2 CONT ***C2. [1m.] Maria, +after 1241; m.before 1200 Mikhail of Chernigov and Kiev (+20.9.1246)
2 CONT ***C3. Danylo, Pr of Galicia (1211-13)+(1229-64), Pr of Volynia (1215-64), crowned by a papal archbishop in Dorohychyn 1253/55 as 1st King of Galicia, *1201, +1264; 1m: 1218 Anna Mstislavna of Novgorod (+bef 1252); 2m: bef 1252 N,
2 CONC  niece of Duke Mindaugas of Lithuania; all kids by 1m.
2 CONT **** ...
2 CONT ***C3. [2m.] '''Vasilko, Duke of Belz (1207-11), Duke of Brest (1221-31), Duke of Volynya (1231-69), *1203, +1269'''; 1m: 1226 Dobrava of Vladimir (+after 5.12.1247); 2m: after 1248 a Polish princess (+1265)
2 CONT ****D1. Vladimir, Duke of Volynya (1269-89), *after 1248, +10.12.1289; m.1263 Elena Romanovna of Briansk (+after 1288)
2 CONT ****D2. Olga, *after 1248, +after 10.12.1288; m.1259/61 Andrei Vsevolodovich of Chernigov (+after 1262)
2 CONT ** ...
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm#VasilkoRomanovichdied1269
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.         '''VASILKO Romanovich ([1203/04]-1269)'''.  Baumgarten names him and cites a primary source, adding that he was two years old when his father died[609].  Prince of Bielsk, Lutsk and Volynia.  He succeeded his brother in
2 CONC  1260 as '''VASILKO King of Galich''', Prince of Volynia when the latter fled to Poland and Hungary.  He was obliged to destroy his brother's fortifications by the Mongols, whose control over Galich tightened[610].  m firstly (bef
2 CONC ore 1229) DOBRAVA [Ielena] Iurievna of Suzdal, daughter of IURII Vsevolodich Grand Prince of Vladimir Prince of Suzdal & his wife Agafia Vsevolodovna of Kiev (-after 5 Dec 1247).  Baumgarten names her, and cites a Russian primary 
2 CONC source and a letter of Pope Innocent IV dated 5 Dec 1247[611].  m secondly (1248) HELENA of Poland, daughter of LESZKO I "Bialy/the White" Prince of Sandomir and Krakow & his wife Gremislava Ingvarovna of Lutsk and Dorogobuz [Ruri
2 CONC kid] (-1265).  Her origin is confirmed by the Russian source cited by Baumgarten which specifies that Prince Bolesław V was the maternal uncle of the children of Prince Vasilko[612].  Baumgarten records the death in 1265 of Helena
2 CONC , wife of Vasilko, citing a Russian source[613].  Vasilko & his second wife had two children: 
2 CONT *a)         VLADIMIR IVAN Vasilkovich (after 1248-10 Dec 1288 or [1289]).  Baumgarten names him and cites a Russian primary source[614].  Grand Prince of Volynia 1269.  m (1263) IELENA Romanovna, daughter of ROMAN Mikhailovich Pri
2 CONC nce of Briansk & his wife Anna --- (-after 10 Dec 1288).  Baumgarten names her and cites a Russian primary source[615]. 
2 CONT *b)         OLGA Vasilkovna (after 1248-after 10 Dec 1288).  Baumgarten names her and cites a Russian primary source[616].  m (1261) ANDREI Mstislavich Prince of Chernigov, son of MSTISLAV FEDOR Glebovich Prince of Chernigov & his
2 CONC  wife (-killed in battle after 1261). 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Vasilko Romanovich (1203–1269), Prince of Belz (1207–1211), Prince of Brest (1221–1231), and Prince of Volhynia (1231–1269).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Roman the Great, and the younger brother of Daniel of Galicia. Family
2 CONT
2 CONT     Volodymyr
2 CONT     Olha
