2 CONT Frederick Alfono, (Catania, between 1290 and 1294 - between 1335 and 1339), was vicar general of the Duchy of Athens, from 1317, and of the Duchy of Neopatria, from 1319, triarca of the island of Evia, from 1318, lord of Salona, ​
2 CONC ​from 1320 and count of Malta and Gozo, from 1330, to his death.
