1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beatrice_Fieschi<br/>
2 CONT -https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/B%C3%A9atrice_Fieschi
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20ITALY%201100-1400.htm#Beatricedied1283
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         BEATRICE Fiesco (-8/9 Jul 1283).  Matthew Paris dates this marriage to 1251 and specifies that the bride (unnamed) was the niece of Pope Innocent IV who arranged her marriage with Thomas de Savoie, ex-Count of Flanders[
2 CONC 424].  This marriage was arranged as part of the process of reconciliation between Thomas's brother, Amédée IV Comte de Savoie, and Pope Innocent IV following the death of Emperor Friedrich II in 1250[425].  Her dowry consisted of
2 CONC  the castles of Rivoli and Viana with Vallesuessia[426].  The testament of "Beatrice Vedova del Re Berengario Conte di Provenza" dated 14 Jan 1264 makes a bequest to "…Beatrice Vedova del Conte Tomaso di Savoia…"[427].  The testam
2 CONC ent of "Adalasiæ relictæ Alberti junioris domini de Turre Pini et de Coloniaco", dated May 1273, bequeathed property to "…domine Comitisse del Borget consanguinee mee…Thome et Amedeo de Sabaudia filiis eiusdem…"[428].  The relatio
2 CONC nship between Beatrice and the testator has not yet been traced.  The testament of "Thomas de Sabaudia primogenitus…domini Thomæ de Sabaudia comitis" dated 14 May 1282 makes bequests to "…matri meæ dominæ B. comitissæ"[429].  m (1
2 CONC 251 after Jun) as his second wife, THOMAS Conte del Piemonte, son of THOMAS I Comte de Savoie & his wife Béatrice [Marguerite] de Genève (Château de Montmélian 1199-Chambéry 7 Feb 1259, bur Aosta Cathedral).  He succeeded his brot
2 CONC her in 1253 as THOMAS II Comte de Savoie, regent or co-ruler with his nephew. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT Thomas II of Piedmont
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas contracted a second marriage to Beatrice di Fieschi, niece of Pope Innocent IV. The couple had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas, his successor and pretender to the County of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT Amadeus, who later inherited Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis (1250 – after 10 January 1302), Baron of Vaud
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor (died 6 December 1296), married (1270) Louis I of Beaujeu
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (died May 1292)
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice (died 1 August 1277)
