2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter IV of Brienne
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT While a teenager, Walter was sent to Outremer where his uncle John of Brienne was the ruler of Jerusalem. In 1221 John gave him the County of Jaffa and Ascalon, and arranged a marriage with Mary of Cyprus (before March, 1215 – ca 
2 CONC 1252 or 1254), daughter of Hugh I of Cyprus, in 1233.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his elder son John, who died childless. His younger son Hugh of Brienne settled in Southern Italy and became a partisan of Charles of Anjou, who returned to him the family's county of Lecce.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ==(*1215 +ca 1252)==
