2 CONT C.      LORDS of BEIRUT (IBELIN)
2 CONT
2 CONT JEAN Ibelin, son of BALIAN of Ibelin Lord of Nablus, Rama and Mirabel & his wife Maria Komnene (1178-Acre 1236).  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "une fille…Heloys, et un fiz Johan et une autre fille Marguerite, et un fiz 
2 CONC Phelippe" as children of "Belleem de Ybelin" & his wife, specifying that Jean was Lord of Beirut[173].  William of Tyre (Continuator) names him and specifies that he was uterine brother of Queen Isabelle[174].  The Chronicle of Al
2 CONC beric de Trois-Fontaines names "Iohannem de Baruth" as the son of "Bethuliani de Guibelin" & his wife[175].  Henri de Champagne King of Jerusalem appointed him Constable of Jerusalem in 1194, considering that Amaury de Lusignan ha
2 CONC d forfeited the post after his arrest after supporting the Pisan revolt in Tyre[176].  Jean Ibelin resigned his office of Constable and was installed as Lord of Beirut in 1205, the town having been recaptured from the Muslims in O
2 CONC ct 1197 by Henri I Duke of Brabant[177].  He was appointed Regent for Marie Queen of Jerusalem on her accession in 1206[178].  "Philippus de Ibelin" donated property to the Knights Hospitallers, with the consent of "Mariæ domina H
2 CONC ierosolymitanæ et Johannes de Ibelin procuratoris dicti regni, necnon Alicis comitissæ uxoris suæ", by charter dated 15 May 1210[179].   William of Tyre (Continuator) records that "Johan d'Ybelin et Felipe d'Ybelin" were uncles of
2 CONC  Alix of Jerusalem whom they accompanied to Cyprus for her marriage before returning to Acre[180].  He and his brother Philippe left the kingdom of Jerusalem (maybe after rebelling against Jean de Brienne) and settled in Cyprus[18
2 CONC 1], some time before Sep 1217 when they both took precedence over all other liegemen in a document of the High Court of Cyprus[182].  "Johannes de Ybellino dominus Berithi…" subscribed the charter dated Oct 1217 under which "Hugo…
2 CONC rex Cipri" confirmed the grant to the church of Nicosia by "Philippus de Ybellino" for the soul of "domine Marie regine, matris sue"[183].  He succeeded his younger brother Philippe in 1227 as lieutenant for the regent of Cyprus[1
2 CONC 84].  After Emperor Friedrich II landed in Cyprus in Jul 1228, Jean refused the emperor's demand to surrender his fief of Beirut but agreed to accompany him to Palestine[185].  On his return visit to Cyprus in May 1229, Emperor Fr
2 CONC iedrich appointed five new baillis of Cyprus, Amaury Barlais, Gavinde Chenichy, Amaury of Beisan, Hugues of Jebail and Guillaume de Rivet, with instructions to evict all Ibelin supporters from Cyprus[186].  Jean of Ibelin retaliat
2 CONC ed by invading Cyprus in Jun 1229, defeated the five baillis 14 Jul and assumed the government of Cyprus until King Henri came of age in 1232.  Amaury Barlais fled with King Henri and his sisters to the castle of Dieu d'Amour, whi
2 CONC ch they surrendered in summer 1230 due to starvation[187].  He died following a riding accident, on his deathbed being admitted to the Order of the Temple[188]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ([1201/02]) HELVIS of Nephim, daughter of RAYMOND [II] Lord of Nephim & his wife --- (-[1208]).  The Lignages d'Outremer name "fille dou seignor de Nefin…Heloys" as first wife of "Johan…de Ybelin…seignor de Baruth"
2 CONC , naming also her sister "Aiglentine" as wife of "Rohart seignor de Kayphas, ayeulle de cestui seignor de Kayphas qui or est, et dou seignor d'Arsur, et pere de Agnes qui fu feme de Boverel en Gene"[189].  William of Tyre (Continu
2 CONC ator) records that "Johan d'Ybelin…bail du roiaume de Jerusalem" was married to "la suer de Renoart de Nefin", although he supported Bohémond IV Prince of Antioch in his war with Renouard[190]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ([1209]) as her second husband, MELISENDE of Arsur, widow of THIERRY d'Orca, daughter of G[UY] of Arsur & his wife ---.  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Melicent, qui avoit esté feme de Their d'Orguenes,…suer de Joh
2 CONC an…seignor d'Arsur" as second wife of "Johan…de Ybelin…seignor de Baruth", specifying that she had seven daughters by her first husband who all died[191]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Ibelin & his first wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT roglo.eu/roglo?lang=ru;m=N;v=ibelin
2 CONT
2 CONT     "Guillaume de Tyr", célèbre chroniqueur, fût "continué" par Ernoul, chroniqueur, lequel était écuyer de ce *Balian Ibelin, époux d'une fille de Montfaucon/Montbéliard.(PeterW.EDBURY , New Perspectives on the Old French Continu
2 CONC ations of William of Tyre, Society for the study of the Crusades and the Latin East, Conférence faite à Avignon, août 2008) -page 223-).
2 CONT
2 CONT     La chronique d'Ernoul mentionne deux fois une fille de *Amédée de Montfaucon comme épouse d'*Érard de Brienne....
2 CONT
2 CONT     « Ice fu le conte Gautier de Brienne qui fu fiz dou conte Erart de Brienne et de la fille dou conte Ami de Monbliart »
2 CONT     « Il (Gautier de Montfaucon) chargea ses chevaucheures et son hernois et recueilli ses gens, et s'en alla à Acre, ou il trova son neveu, fiz de sa suer, le roi Johan, qui le reçut à grant joie. »
2 CONT
2 CONT     La chronique d'Ernoul s'arrête en 1229... 
