2 CONT =Sibylla of Lusignan=
2 CONT '''Sibylla of Lusignan''' (or Sibylle de Lusignan) (October/November 1198 – c. 1230 or 1252) was the daughter of Amalric II of Jerusalem and Isabella of Jerusalem. She was a member of the House of Lusignan.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the second wife of King Leo I of Armenia, married in 1210, by whom she had one daughter, Isabella of Armenia. She claimed the throne of Armenia for herself after the death of her husband, who had left the throne to their i
2 CONC nfant daughter, but was exiled by the regent Constantine of Baberon.[1]
2 CONT
