2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BULGARIA.htm#KonstantinTihdied1277
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         KONSTANTIN Tih (-killed in battle Autumn 1277).  Georgius Akropolites records that "Toechi filium Constantinum" was elected to "Bulgarorum principatus" after Tsar Koloman was killed[358].  One of the boyars in Trnovo, h
2 CONC e was elected in 1258 as KONSTANTIN Tih Tsar of the Bulgarians by his fellow boyars and was based in Trnovo.  In order to boost his claim, he married as his second wife the granddaughter of Tsar Ivan Asen II.  He took advantage of
2 CONC  his rival Rostislav's temporary absence from Vidin (he was helping his father-in-law Béla IV King of Hungary in his war against Bohemia) to recapture Vidin province.  However, the Hungarians counter-attacked and forced his withdr
2 CONC awal[359].  He fell from his horse in 1264 and was paralysed from the waist down.  His personal leadership of his armies became difficult and his power declined[360].  He fell under the influence of his ambitious second wife who a
2 CONC ssumed greater control due to her husband's physical incapacity.  His third marriage with the niece of Emperor Michael VIII was arranged to confirm a new alliance with Byzantium, under which he was promised Mesembria and Anchialos
2 CONC , although the Byzantines later reneged on the arrangement[361].  He was killed while trying to suppress the rebellion of Ivajlo, who had also proclaimed himself Tsar[362].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (repudiated [1257/58]) ---.  Georgius Akropolites records that "Toechi filium Constantinum" repudiated his first wife to marry "imperatorem Theodorum…filiam suam maiorem…Irene"[363].  The name of the first wife of 
2 CONC Konstantin Tih is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (early 1258) EIRENE Laskarina, daughter of THEODOROS II Emperor in Nikaia & his wife Elena Asenina of Bulgaria (-[1269]).  Georgius Akropolites records the marriage of "Toechi filium Constantinum" and "imperatorem
2 CONC  Theodorum…filiam suam maiorem…Irene"[364].  Ephræmius records the marriage of "Irene filia Cæsaris natu maior" and "Constantino…Ticho"[365].  Tsar Konstantin arranged this marriage with the granddaughter of Tsar Ivan Asen II to b
2 CONC oost his claim to the Bulgarian throne.  After the coup engineered by Mikhail Palaiologos against her brother Emperor Ioannes, Eirene urged her husband to attack the territories which Palaiologos controlled[366].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' thirdly (1269) as her second husband, MARIA Palaiologina Kantakouzene, widow of ALEXIOS Philes, daughter of IOANNES Kantakouzenos & his wife Eirene Palaiologina (-after 1279).  Pachymeres records that "regis Bulgarorum Con
2 CONC stantini" married "imperator…propriam neptem, Eulogiæ suæ sororis filiam secundo genitam Mariam", previously married to "Philes Alexius magnus domesticus", after the death of his first wife[367].  Pachymeres names "Constantini quo
2 CONC ndam…regis ex Maria filium"[368].  Her marriage was arranged to confirm Byzantium's new alliance with Bulgaria, under which her uncle promised to return Mesembria and Anchialos, although the Byzantines later reneged on the arrange
2 CONC ment[369].  With the decline in her husband's effective leadership following his incapacity, she assumed an increasing role in governing Bulgaria.  On behalf of her husband, she negotiated an arrangement with his rival Jakov Sveto
2 CONC slav.  She adopted him as their second son in 1273 but had him poisoned in [1275/77][370].  She continued to rule in Trnovo after her husband was killed in battle, but after Ivajlo besieged Trnovo she opened the city gates to him 
2 CONC in late spring 1278 and married him as her third husband[371].  After Trnovo opened its gates to Byzantine troops in Feb 1279, she was sent to Emperor Mikhael VIII who imprisoned her in Adrianople[372].  
2 CONT
2 CONT  Tsar Konstantin & his [first/second] wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         daughter (-1292 or after).  She died or was repudiated in 1292. ''' m''' ([1284]) as his first wife, SMILEC, ruler in western Sredna Gora (-1298).  He succeeded in 1292 as SMILEC Tsar of the Bulgarians, after Georgi Te
2 CONC rter fled to Byzantium, possibly installed by Nogai Khan of the Tartars. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Tsar Konstantin & his third wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         MIHAIL ASEN ([1270/71]-murdered [1300/01]).  Pachymeres records that "Maria…[et] Constantino" had a son "Michaelem"[373].  He was crowned as co-Tsar of the Bulgarians by his father in 1273[374].  In a Byzantine prison 
2 CONC 1279.  Pachymeres names "Constantini quondam…regis ex Maria filium" when recording that Byzantium unsuccessfully attempted to install him as Tsar[375], dated to 1298 by Fine[376].  '''m''' ---.  The name of his wife is not known. 
