2 CONT
2 CONT Roman Sanguszko (born 1537, died 1571), a duke related to the House of Jagiellon; the Voivode of Bracław and a Sigismund II Augustus’ courtier. Despite the fact that, like many other Lithuanian noblemen, he was against the Polish-
2 CONC Lithuanian union, he eventually signed it. At the time of finalizing the union he fought against the Grand Duchy of Moscow in 1559 and with the Tatars in 1569. Perhaps this was the reason why Matejko pictured him as a worried citi
2 CONC zen who comes to Sejm session in full battle gear, straight from the battle field, in order to see to that Poland's future is secured. 
