2 CONT =========
2 CONT
2 CONT Khalilullah II was the 41st Shirvanshah, governing Shirvan under Safavid suzerainty between 1523—1535.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Born as Khalil, after death of his father, he assumed the regnal name of Khalilullah II in 1524. He was married to Ismail I's daughter, and Tahmasp I's sister Pari Khan Khanum (not to be mistaken for Tahmasp's daughter Pari Khan K
2 CONC hanum)[2] on 4 October 1521.
2 CONT
2 CONT After death of Ismail I, the new shah Tahmasp I was suspicious towards new shirvanshah. This suspicion had grown when latter gave asylum to a traitor to Safavids - Gilan ruler Sultan Muzaffar. But before demanding pardon Khalilull
2 CONC ah died unexpectedly without issue. He was succeed by Farrukh Yassar II.
