2 CONT 1.         GUGLIELMO Sanudo (-1323).  The Istoria of Marino Sanudo Torsello names "Miser Guglielmo Sanudo, 1260 fatto Rè da Balduin" as the son of "Marco Sanudo"[779].  He succeeded his father in 1303 as GUGLIELMO I Duke of Naxos.
2 CONC   He attempted to reassert the suzerainty of Naxos over the islands recaptured from the Byzantines prior to his accession.  He captured Giacopo Barozzi, Lord of Santorini, but was obliged by Venice to release him.  He had more suc
2 CONC cess with Amorgos, although at Siphnos its new leader Januli da Corogna declared himself an independent sovereign as did Januli Gozzadini at Anaphe[780].  "Ser Guillielmus Sanutus Duchatus Nichoxie et Andre dominator fidelis" is i
2 CONC ncluded in the list of Barons "de Romania" with whom Venice maintained relations in 1313[781].  Alfonso Fadrique, as Vicar-General of the Duchy of Athens, conquered the island of Melos in reaction to the support given by Naxos to 
2 CONC the princes of Achaia[782].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Guglielmo's wife is not known.  Duke Guglielmo & his wife had six children:  
