1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Giorgio Contarini, count of Jaffa, was a first cousin to queen Caterina Cornaro through his mother Elisabetta Cornaro, who was the aunt of the queen of Cyprus.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.rikvanhauwe.be/Venice/BO/B.O.IV.C.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Contarini x Contarini anno 1484 ( Giorgio fu Tommaso Ca del Zaffo x Isabella di Nicolo qu Pietro qu Roberto )      Carta 515        
2 CONT
2 CONT Giorgio + in Cyprus , see Sanudo on 15.12.1510 , he is succeeded as conte Zaffo by his son Tommaso  
2 CONT
2 CONT Decima 1514 . Maria Zubenigo . 50 for the widow Isabella . Estimo of 131 ducats *
2 CONT Decima 1514 . Santa Maria Zubenigo . 58 . Tommaso e fratelli . Estimo of 172 ducats
2 CONT Decima 1521 . Santa Maria Zubenigo . Tommaso e fratelli . Estimo of 32 ducats from mezado fo di Nicolo Contarini
2 CONT
2 CONT * She has properties in San Silvestro & in San Stefano minore
2 CONT
2 CONT anno 1506 : Tommaso di Giorgio qu Tommaso ( sponsors are Paolo Contarini qu Tommaso & his sister Catarruzza Contarini qu Tommaso , tt. are Carolo Contarini qu Giovanni di Alvise & Marcus Antonio Manolesso di Francesco )
2 CONT     1) Tommaso entered Great Council on 09.12.1509 after the Barbarella
2 CONT          He is invested as conte Zaffo on 16.09.1526 in hands of Andrea Gritti as titular king of Cyprus , see Sanudo XLII . 631 , his yearly income is 2500 ducats
2 CONT         Tommaso is capitano Famagusta , elected on 04.02.1526 , offered 3400 ducats       
2 CONT         He will leave on 12.02.1530 after the death of the present Angelo Giustiniani , capitano Famagusta
2 CONT         Tommaso qu Giorgio is capitano Famagusta on 01.10.1534                      
2 CONT
2 CONT         Contarini dal Zaffo x Malipiero on 25.08.1526 ( Tommaso fu Giorgio x Elena di Paolo qu Giacomo )   She is a niece of Doge Andrea Gritti
2 CONT
2 CONT         Present at the wedding are the Doge and a 92 year old noble named Francesco De Molin qu Leone
2 CONT
2 CONT        Offspring till the end of the Republic
2 CONT
2 CONT no probation : Giustiniano
2 CONT     2) Giustiniano qu Giorgio comitis Zaffi entered Great Council on 03.03.1515 after payment , his mother Isabella testifies , tt. are Pietro Zen qu Caterino eques & Giovanni Querini qu Pietro
2 CONT         Giustiniano qu Giorgio cavalier conte Zaffo is member of Immortali on 26.05.1520
2 CONT         He is gobernator introitus on 01.07.1526 per ducati 4000
2 CONT         He is elected among 2 proveditori sopra imprestado di Gran Consiglio on 03.10.1528
2 CONT         See also imprestado anno 1528 together with his brother Giulio
2 CONT         He is proveditor sopra imprestedo di Gran Consiglio and can enter the Senate at San Michele without a ballot , see Sanudo LII pagina 23
2 CONT         At 5 judici sopra Paros on 21.06.1532
2 CONT         He is elected among 15 savi sopra la tansa on 29.09.1532
2 CONT
2 CONT        Contarini x Emo anno 1524 ( Giustiniani fu Giorgio x Elisabetta di Leonardo )   Engagement in San Lunardo on 24.02.1524
2 CONT
2 CONT        Extinct anno 1619
2 CONT
2 CONT no probation : Giulio
2 CONT     3) Giulio entered Great Council on 15.11.1521 aged XX , his mother - widow Isabella Contarini relicta Giorgio equitis testifies , tt. are Giovanni Querini qu Pietro & Pietro Contarini qu Agostino  
2 CONT         Giulio qu Giorgio is elected off. X officii on 04.11.1526 
2 CONT         Giulio qu Giorgio is camerlengo di comun on 20.02.1531
2 CONT
2 CONT         No offspring
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contea_di_Giaffa_e_Ascalona
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Infine, durante il regno di [https://www.geni.com/people/Caterina-Cornaro-regina-di-Cipro/6000000008467548795 Caterina Cornaro] , il titolo di Conte di Giaffa si associò definitivamente alla famiglia veneziana dei Contarini quando
2 CONC  la sovrana lo offrì al [https://www.geni.com/path/Giorgio-I-Contarini-count-of-Jaffa-Ascalon+is+related+to+Caterina-Cornaro-regina-di-Cipro?from=6000000080117603855&path_type=blood&to=6000000008467548795 cugino] '''Giorgio I'''. 
2 CONC  I suoi discendenti continuarono a rivendicare questo titolo anche dopo la perdita di Cipro e delle terre ivi contenute durante la conquista ottomana del 1570.
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation:
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Finally, during the reign of Caterina Cornaro, the title of Count of Jaffa became definitively associated with the Venetian Contarini family when the sovereign offered it to her cousin George I. His descendants continued to clai
2 CONC m this title even after the loss of Cyprus and the lands therein during the Ottoman conquest of 1570.
2 CONT ''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From George Hill, 𝘈 𝘏𝘪𝘴𝘵𝘰𝘳𝘺 𝘰𝘧 𝘊𝘺𝘱𝘳𝘶𝘴 𝘝𝘰𝘭𝘶𝘮𝘦 3: 𝘈 𝘍𝘳𝘢𝘯𝘬𝘪𝘴𝘩 𝘗𝘦𝘳𝘪𝘰𝘥 1432-1571, Cambridge University Press 2010 pp794/5 < [https://archive.org/details/a-history-of-cyprus-vol.-3-compressed/page/794/mode/2up Archive.Org] >
2 CONT
2 CONT >Of the great laymen, the chief in rank at the death of James II was the Count of Jaffa and Karpass.4 We have seen that in 1472 James created the barony of Karpass, bestowing it on John Perez Fabregues, who as Count of Jaffa alrea
2 CONC dy took precedence over all other barons of Cyprus. In the charter James ordained that the precedence should belong to the new County. This was an arbitrary act, and ceased to have effect when Catherine deprived the heirs of John 
2 CONC Perez Fabregues of the County of Jaffa and gave it to her cousin [https://www.geni.com/people/Giorgio-Contarini-count-of-Jaffa/6000000080117603855?through=6000000080117262860 George Contarini].5
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT # https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comt%C3%A9_de_Jaffa_et_d%27Ascalon
2 CONT
2 CONT *1474-1510 : '''Giorgio I Contarini''', [https://www.geni.com/path/Giorgio-I-Contarini-count-of-Jaffa-Ascalon+is+related+to+Caterina-Cornaro-regina-di-Cipro?from=6000000080117603855&path_type=blood&to=6000000008467548795 cousin] d
2 CONC e [https://www.geni.com/people/Caterina-Cornaro-regina-di-Cipro/6000000008467548795 Catherine Cornaro].
2 CONT **1510-1560 : Tommaso I Contarini, son fils.
2 CONT ***1560-1578 : Giorgio II Pietro Domenico Contarini, son fils. <br> Après la prise de Chypre par les Turcs, il perd les fiefs chypriotes attachés au titre de « Comte de Jaffa et d'Ascalon ». Le titre de comte de Jaffa et d'Ascalon
2 CONC  est désormais un titre féodal strictement vénitien.
2 CONT ****1578-1617 : Tommaso II Contarini, son fils.
2 CONT *****1617-1630 : Giulio Contarini, son fils.
2 CONT ******1630-1675 : Tommaso III Contarini, provéditeur extraordinaire de Dalmatie, son fils, sans postérité.
2 CONT Le titre et le prérogatives passèrent à une branche cadette des Contarini descendante du comte Giorgio II.
2 CONT *1675-1684 : Frederico Contarini, son cousin, sans postérité.
2 CONT *1684-1714 : Angelo Contarini, son neveu.
2 CONT *1714-1756 : Giorgio III Contarini, membre du Conseil des Dix, son fils.
2 CONT *1756-1783 : Alvise I Contarini, sénateur, son fils.
2 CONT *1783-1810 : Alvise II Giorgio Contarini, sénateur, son fils, sans postérité.
2 CONT *1810-1817 : Alvise III Angelo Contarini del Zaffo, son frère.
2 CONT *1817-18?? : Alvise IV Gaspare Contarini del Zaffo, son fils.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/County_of_Jaffa_and_Ascalon
2 CONT
2 CONT The double County of Jaffa and Ascalon was one of the four major seigneuries comprising the major Crusader state of the Kingdom of Jerusalem, according to 13th-century commentator John of Ibelin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jaffa and Ascalon were then granted to close relatives of the monarch and passed in and out of direct royal control as its holders ascended the throne. Around 1250 it was given to a branch of the Ibelin family. With the capture of
2 CONC  Jaffa by Baibars in 1268, the county became titular. It was bestowed anew upon John Perez Fabrice by James II of Cyprus and Jerusalem. 
2 CONT
2 CONT .......
2 CONT * John Perez Fabrice
2 CONT * Louis Perez Fabrice
2 CONT * '''Georges Contaren'''
2 CONT * N. Contaren
2 CONT * Georges Contaren II (c. 1579)
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT *http://cardinaliserenissima.uniud.it/57-contarini-albero.html   
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT **https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contarini#Contarini_dal_Zaffo
2 CONT
2 CONT Assunsero questa denominazione nel 1473, quando la regina di Cipro [https://www.geni.com/people/Caterina-Cornaro-regina-di-Cipro/6000000008467548795 Caterina Cornaro] creò [https://www.geni.com/people/Giorgio-I-Contarini-count-of-
2 CONC Jaffa-Ascalon/6000000080117603855 Giorgio Contarini conte di Giaffa], rendendolo il primo dignitario dell'isola. .. ...
2 CONT .. ... Il rappresentante più insigne di questa linea fu il cardinale [https://www.geni.com/people/Gasparo-Contarini/6000000175826762833 cardinale Gasparo di Alvise] (1483-1542) [22]
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation:
2 CONT
2 CONT ''They assumed this name in 1473, when the Queen of Cyprus Caterina Cornaro created Giorgio Contarini count of Jaffa, making him the first dignitary of the island. .. ...
2 CONT .. ... The most distinguished representative of this line was Cardinal Gasparo di Alvise (1483-1542) [22]''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palazzo_Contarini_Dal_Zaffo '''Palazzo Contarini Dal Zaffo'''], also known as Palazzo Contarini Polignac is a large palace in Venice, located in the Dorsoduro district, overlooking the Grand Canal, i
2 CONC n an intermediate position between Palazzo Brandolin Rota and Palazzo Balbi Valier.  ...  The Contarini dal Zaffo family,[4] which owned many other famous palazzos, rebuilt the structure between 1562 and 1582 without altering its 
2 CONC exterior. The palazzo was named after ''Giorgio Contarini, who was Count of Jaffa (Zaffo) in Palestine''.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7b/Palazzo_Contarini_Polignac_%28Venice%29.jpg|center|alt=Palace Contarini Dal Zaffo o Polignac Venice. Facade on Grand Canal.}}
2 CONT
