2 CONT #George Hill, 𝘈 𝘏𝘪𝘴𝘵𝘰𝘳𝘺 𝘰𝘧 𝘊𝘺𝘱𝘳𝘶𝘴 𝘝𝘰𝘭𝘶𝘮𝘦 3: 𝘈 𝘍𝘳𝘢𝘯𝘬𝘪𝘴𝘩 𝘗𝘦𝘳𝘪𝘰𝘥 1432-1571, Cambridge University Press 2010 pp794/5 < [https://archive.org/details/a-history-of-cyprus-vol.-3-compressed/page/794/mode/2up Archive.Org] >
2 CONT ##See above, p. 574. On the Counts of Jaffa, see Mas Latrie, ‘Les comtes de Jaffa du Xue au XIXe siecle’ in Arch. Vert. t. 18 (1879), pt. 2, pp. 370-417; the same article under the title ‘Les comtes de Jaffa et d’Ascalon du xne au
2 CONC  xrxe siècle’ in Revue des questions historiques, t. 26 (1879). On those of Karpass, the same, “Les comtes du Carpas’ in B.E.C. xu (1880), pp. 376-92; Doc. Nouv. pp. 421-7.
2 CONT ##5 Above, p. 703. He died in 1510 (Sanudo, x1, 682) and was buried in St Dominic’s {Lusignan, Desc. f. 153b). I have failed to find the source for Mas Latrie’s statement that he died in 1491.
