2 CONT # ''Les comtes du Carpas''. [article]  Louis de Mas-Latrie Bibliothèque de l'École des chartes Year 1880 41 pp. 375-392 le préséance élevée entre les comtes de Jaffa et les comtes du Carpas seront publiés dans le tome IV des Mélan
2 CONC ges historiques de la Coll. des Documents. In French: < [https://www.jstor.org/stable/pdf/42999508.pdf PDF] >; < [https://www.persee.fr/doc/bec_0373-6237_1880_num_41_1_446935 book extract] >; < [https://digital.lib.auth.gr/record/
2 CONC 148312/files/1.pdf PDF] >
2 CONT # https://www.britannica.com/topic/Contarini-family '''Contarini family,''' distinguished Venetian family, one of the 12 that elected the first doge in 697 and later gave Venice eight doges and many other eminent citizens. There w
2 CONC ere at one time no fewer than 18 branches of the family; one of the most important was that of Contarini dallo Zaffo, or di Giaffa, who had been invested with the countship of Jaffa in Syria for their services to Caterina Cornaro,
2 CONC  queen of Cyprus; another was that of Contarini degli Scrigni (“of the Coffers”), so called because of their great wealth. ...
2 CONT # https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contarini#Contarini_dal_Zaffo Contarini They assumed this name in 1473, when the Queen of Cyprus Catherine Cornaro created Giorgio Contarini Count of Jaffa, making it the first dignitary of the isla
2 CONC nd. After the Turkish conquest it was a purely honorary but absolutely prestigious and coveted title: it was recognized in 1476 by the same Republic which, indeed, conferred the knighthood of the Stola d'Oro [also the knighthood o
2 CONC f the Stola d'Oro. They were also called "of the Madonna dell'Orto" from the name of the parish of residence (lived in a palace in Cannaregio, with a beautiful garden and a well-stocked library[). They were not very rich but could
2 CONC  count on several real estate, including houses in Venice and land in Piove di Sacco and Villafranca[. Other assets were in the Duchy of Ferrara, but were later alienated for the expansionist aim of the Papal States[21]. The large
2 CONC st source of income, however, came from the mercantile activity (Puglie and Alexandria of Egypt).[23] ... Their nobility, along with the titles of accounts and knights, was recognized by the Austrian Empire with S.R. 1 December 18
2 CONC 17[[7]. 
2 CONT # https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giaffa Jaffa (Hebrew יָפוֹ?, Yafo; in Arabic يَافَا???????, Yuf?) is a city of Israel now incorporated in the urban area of Tel Aviv, part of the Tel Aviv-Jaffa municipality in the Tel Aviv district
2 CONC . The city is located on a naturally elevated promontory on the Mediterranean coast. ... 
2 CONT # https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contea_di_Giaffa_e_Ascalona The County of Jaffa and Ascalon was one of the four major vassals of the Kingdom of Jerusalem in Palestine, according to the chronicles of the 13th-century jurist John of
2 CONC  Ibelin. 
2 CONT # https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palazzo_Contarini_Dal_Zaffo_(Dorsoduro)
2 CONT # The Rough Guide to Venice & Veneto (Travel Guide eBook) By Rough Guides. < [https://books.google.com/books?id=G_CcDwAAQBAJ&lpg=PT189&dq=Palazzo%20Contarini%20Dal%20Zaffo&pg=PT189#v=onepage&q=Palazzo%20Contarini%20Dal%20Zaffo&f=f
2 CONC alse GoogleBooks] > On the canal's north side, at its eastern end, stands the seventeenth-century Palazo Minelli Spada and the sixteenth-century Palazzo Contarini dal Zaffo, the latter being one of the many palaces owned by the va
2 CONC st Contarini clan.  Numerous though they once were, the last male of the Contarini line died in 1836, thus adding their name to the roll call of patrician dynasties that vanished in the nineteenth century.  Already impoverished by
2 CONC  loans made to the dying Republic and by the endless round of parties, many of the Venetian aristocracy were bankrupted during the Napoleonic and Austrian occupations, and so, no longer having money for dowries and other related e
2 CONC xpenses, they simply chose not to marry.
