1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tulunbeg Khanum - daughter of Berdi Beg and wife of Mamai - Regent for Mohammad Bolagh, a puppet khan for Mamai, from 1370 to 1372
2 CONT ========
2 CONT https://weaponews.com/history/65361263-tolobek-khanum-the-only-khan-of-the-golden-horde.html
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT ref: https://ca.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tulunbeg
2 CONT
2 CONT [Tulunbeg (Tülüngbeg) or Tulunbek was a khan of the Golden Horde towards 1371 to 1373.
2 CONT
2 CONT She may have been the widow of Aig Beg (1373–1376), actual ruler was Mamai. (ref: ORMUS The Secret Alchemy of Mary Magdalene ~ Revealed ~ [Part A]
2 CONT
2 CONT Appears after Hasan Beg Khan and there are some coins dated between 1371 and 1373 minted in New Sarai to mention however is the case in some curious is called khan and other Queen. Some historians think it was a queen and when it 
2 CONC is spoken as a khan is a vague term; could be the widow of Aziz Xaikh we know that he was a person of high influence even sent ambassadors to the Russian principalities as personal representatives alongside representatives of the 
2 CONC khan. Another theory is that it was Khan of Turan , son of Ming Temür (Mangu Timur) and nephew Mahmud Khirz ....]
2 CONT
2 CONT [...Pretender Khan Mamai sacks Riazan in re- venge (1373) 1373 A.D. -Tulun Beg-Khanum (fem) (1370- 1373) dies, Ai Beg becomes Kipchak Khan (1373 d 1376) ] ref : p.233 of ORMUS The Secret Alchemy of Mary Magdalene ~ Revealed ~ [Par
2 CONC t A]
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT Tulunbek-khanum (? - 1386 , Saray-Berke ) - daughter of the Khan of the Golden Horde Berdibek , wife of temnik and beklarbek Mamai , regent of the Golden Horde in 1370-1372 under Khan Muhammad Bulak (773 A.H. [1] ), wife of Khan T
2 CONC okhtamysh since 1380.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography  Tulunbek became the eldest wife of Mamai when her father was only the heir to the throne. Thanks to this marriage, the status of Mamai, who was not a Chingizid, significantly increased, he began to use the title "gurgen
2 CONC " - the khan's son-in-law. There is no doubt that the closeness of Berdibek and Mamai, sealed by this marriage, influenced the receipt by the latter, from Berdibek, who came to power, the post of first minister - beklarbek, the hi
2 CONC ghest position that a nechingizid could claim.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Berdibek, in the midst of an acute struggle for power and a constant change of khans in Sarai , Mamai achieved great authority as a stronghold and protection of the legitimate rulers from the Batu clan from pret
2 CONC enders to the throne descended from other children of Jochi . However, his unnaturalness did not allow him to occupy the khan throne himself, and Mamai tried to find a suitable Chingizid, not too powerful to be an all-powerful min
2 CONC ister with him. In 1370, a situation arose when Mamai could occupy Saray, but Khan Abdullahdied and Mamai could not find a suitable replacement. Then Mamai took an unprecedented step, proclaiming his wife as a khan, whose gentilit
2 CONC y was not in doubt, because she was the daughter of Berdibek Khan, who came from the most legitimate branch of the Chingizids of the Batu clan. She ruled in Sarai from 1370-1372. She was recognized not only in the capital, but als
2 CONC o Tagay , Emir Mokhshi , judging by the fact that he also minted coins on her behalf. At the same time, this appointment was apparently perceived as temporary, and Mamai continued to look for a khan for himself, settling on the ei
2 CONC ght-year-old Muhammad Bulak , the son of Abdullah Khan. Muhammad Bulak was proclaimed khan at the turn of 1371-1372. Nominally Tulunbek was the regent under the minor khan.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1380, after the defeat of Mamai at the Battle of Kalka , Beklarbek fled to the Crimea and was killed there, and Tokhtamysh got his harem (the wives and women under his protection from the Batu house) . To increase his legitimac
2 CONC y in the eyes of the capital's Sarai nobility and possible adherents of the Batu house, Tokhtamysh married Tulunbek-khanum, the daughter of Khan Berdibek and the widow of Mamai [2] .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1386, a conspiracy was drawn up against Tokhtamysh, about which little information has survived. It is known that the khan executed his wife Tulunbek. In the same year, coins were issued with the name of Khan Berdibek. Probably
2 CONC , a conspiracy was drawn up against Tokhtamysh to replace him on the throne with a descendant of Batu; former adherents of Mamai, led by his widow, could become its participants. Some of the participants in this conspiracy, led by
2 CONC  the Mangyt emir Idigu, fled to Maverannahr , to the emir Timur , who began to willingly accept (earlier he supported Tokhtamysh) Horde emigrants who were dissatisfied with Tokhtamysh Khan.
