2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SERBIA.htm#Vladislavdied12671269
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.         STEFAN VLADISLAV (-11 Nov after 1267 [1269]).  The life of St Sava by Domentijan records that "son frère Vladislav" succeeded as king on the abdication of "le roi Radoslav" and was crowned by his uncle Archbishop Sava[1
2 CONC 64].  He succeeded as VLADISLAV King of Serbia after his brother was deposed in late 1233.  He was unable to resist pillage by the Mongols as they passed through Serbia in 1242, on their way back to Karakoram after learning of the
2 CONC  death of Great Khan Ogedei[165].  Vladislav was deposed in 1243 in favour of his younger [half-]brother Stefan Uroš, maybe because of close ties with Bulgaria through his marriage, although he remained on good relations with his 
2 CONC successor and was still referred to as king in some official documents[166].  Regent of Primorje.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([1233]) BELISAVA Asenina of Bulgaria, daughter of IVAN ASEN II Tsar of the Bulgarians & his first wife Anna --- (before 1221-after 1285).  The life of St Sava by Domentijan records that Saint Saba arranged the marriage of
2 CONC  "Vladislav…roi de Serbie" and "la fille d’Aciene roi des Bulgares" soon after his accession as king[167].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified.   
2 CONT
2 CONT    Stefan Vladislav & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         STEFAN.  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         DESA.  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  1281/85.
2 CONT
2 CONT *c)         daughter .  Her parentage is confirmed by the charter dated to [1240/72] under which “Georgius comes, regis Vladislavi gener” made peace with Ragusa[168].  '''m''' DJURE Kačić Knez of Omiš.  “Georgius comes, regis Vlad
2 CONC islavi gener” made peace with Ragusa by charter dated to [1240/72][169].  1239/74. 
2 CONT
