2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Maria of Bulgaria (d. after 1081), protovestiaria, was the wife of protovestiarios and domestikos ton scholon Andronikos Doukas and mother of Irene Doukaina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents  [hide]  1	Life 2	Family 3	References 4	External links Life[edit] Maria was a daughter of Troian of Bulgaria by an unnamed Byzantine noblewoman descended from the families of Kontostephanos and Phokas, and a granddaughter
2 CONC  of Ivan Vladislav of Bulgaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria married Andronikos Doukas well before 1066. Her husband was a son of the Caesar John Doukas, a major power player in Byzantine politics of the era, and Eirene Pelagonitissa. He was also a nephew of Constantine X and first co
2 CONC usin of Michael VII.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria was endowed with an inheritance of vast land holdings around Lake Ohrid, and her considerable income was used to support her husband's lavish lifestyle and political ambitions. As the last descendants of the ruling family of
2 CONC  Bulgaria, Maria and her daughters Irene and Anna, who married the first notable member of the Palaiologos family, carried not only immense wealth but also legitimisation of Byzantine authority over the Bulgarian population: her (
2 CONC and her daughters') prominent marriages are evidence for the eventual integration of the descendants of the Cometopuli dynasty into the court nobility in Constantinople.
2 CONT
2 CONT As mother of the Empress Irene Doukaina, Maria was a woman of some influence in the early years of the reign of Alexios I Komnenos, although she, as a widow, shunned the Imperial court and chose to live in her Lake Ohrid estate. H
2 CONC er granddaughter Anna Komnene praises her beauty and wisdom in the Alexiad.
