2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=e7d61def-c565-4ea0-a9b3-985dd1ba5da5&tid=10145763&pid=-227715008
1 NOTE He ruled from 1235 to 1270. He was driven from the country by the Mongol invasion of 1241 and fled to Dalmatia. Approximately half the population was killed by the invading armies. He was eventually able to reestablish himself and
2 CONC  defeated the Tartar Nogai Khan in 12?1. He had two sons and seven daughters, the most famous being St. Margaret of Hungary.
