1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''FMG: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/AUSTRIA.htm#LeopoldIIIdied1136B AUSTRIA]''' – « 10. '''ERNST''' ([1118]-23 Jan 1137, bur Heiligenkreuz). The ''Continuatio Claustroneoburgensis'' names "''Ensto''" as fourt
2 CONC h son of "''Liupoldus marchio Austrie''" and "''Agnetem imperatoris Heinrici IV filiam''", specifying that he was buried "''apud Sancto Crucem''"[208]. His description as "fourth son" is inconsistent with his estimated birth date,
2 CONC  calculated from the age specified in the entry for his death in the necrology of Heiligenkreuz (see below), which is consistent with his being described as "adolescent" when he died. The necrology of Melk records the death "''X K
2 CONC al Feb''" of "''Ernust fil Liupaldi marchionis''"[209]. The necrology of Lilienfeld records the death "''X Kal Feb''" of "''Ernestus marchio fil fundatoris S Crucis''"[210]. The necrology of Kloster Neuburg records the death "''X 
2 CONC Kal Feb''" of "''Ernestus fil marchionis Austrie Liupoldi''"[211].  The necrology of Heiligenkreuz records the death "''X Kal Feb 1137''" of "''adolescens Ernestus s Leopoldi fundatoris fil quarto genitus 18 annos vixit''" and his
2 CONC  burial "''in capitulo no''"[212]. » —— '''Note:''' The date for death is correct. FMG's sourced "X Kal Feb 1137" (the 10th day before the Calends of February), which converts to 23 January 1137. Translating the last Latin line, t
2 CONC he "young Ernestus, the fourth son of the founder Leopold, lived for 18 years." Since he died in January Ernst probably was in his 19th year. 1137 – 19 = b. 1118
