2 CONT 3) AGNESE di Monferrato (-1208).  Villehardouin records the marriage of Emperor Henri and "the Marquis de Montferrat's…daughter" at Constantinople "in the church of Santa Sophia on the Sunday after Candlemas Day", naming her "the 
2 CONC Empress Agnes"[175].  Her marriage was arranged to confirm her father's alliance against her future husband in the face of Bulgarian aggression in northern Greece[176].  
2 CONT
