2 CONT '''DEMETRIOS Tornikes Komnenos''', son of KONSTANTINOS Tornikes & his wife --- Komnene (-[1252]).  Adontz quotes a letter from Mikhael Akominate addressed to Demetrios Tornikes which names his father Konstantinos and his grandfath
2 CONC er Demetrios[895].  Georgios Akropolites names "Demetrios Tornices, qui summam rerum publicarum administrabat…" among the important nobles at the court of Emperor Ioannes Batatzes[896].  Georgios Akropolites records the death of "
2 CONC Demetrius Tornicius ", dated to the early 1250s from the context[897]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly --- [Palaiologina], daughter of ---.  Georgios Akropolites records that "Demetrius Tornicius…Thessalonicæ magnus domesticus" married "magni domestici consobrinam" (referring to Mikhael Palaeologus, the future Emper
2 CONC or Mikhael VIII)[898].  The text does not state whether the relationship was through the male or female line of the family, so it is uncertain whether Demetrios´s wife was "Palaiologina" by birth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ---.  The name of Demetrios's second wife is not known. 
