1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SICILY.htm#Tancreddied1194B
2 CONT
2 CONT King Tancred & his wife Sibylla had [six] children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. SIBILLA [Madania] . The Thomas Tusci Gesta Imperatorum et Pontificum names (in order) "Alberia, Constantia et Madania" as the three daughters of "Tancredus [rex Siciliæ]" & his wife, specifying that Madania remained unmarried[6
2 CONC 36]. She was confined with her mother and sisters at the convent of Hohenburg in Alsace. According to William of Tyre (Continuator), Gauthier de Brienne married "la suer de sa feme au conte Jame de Tricart"[637], which contradicts
2 CONC  the Thomas Tusci Gesta Imperatorum et Pontificum which names "Iacobo comiti de Tricario" as second husband of Gauthier de Brienne's widow[638]. The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified. m ROBERTO
2 CONC  di Montescaglioso, son of ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NEAPOLITAN%20NOBILITY.htm#RobertoMontescagliosoMSibillaSicily
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         ROBERTO di Montescaglioso .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  m SIBILLA of Sicily, daughter of TANCRED King of Sicily & his wife Sibilla ---.  The primary source which confir
2 CONC ms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
