2 CONT Beatrice of Burgundy (1143 - November 15, 1184) Beatrice was the only daughter of Renaud III, Count of Burgundy and Agatha of Lorraine. She was the second wife and Empress of Frederick I, Holy Roman Emperor. Her maternal grandpare
2 CONC nts were Simon I, Duke of Lorraine and his wife Adelaide of Leuven. Beatrice was active at the Hohenstaufen court, encouraging literary works and chivalric ideals. She accompanied her husband on his travels and campaigns across hi
2 CONC s kingdom, and Frederick Barbarossa was known to be under Beatrice's influence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice and Frederick were married June 9, 1156 at Würzburg. By this marriage Frederick obtained control of the vast county of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick V, Duke of Swabia (1164-1170) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry VI, Holy Roman Emperor (November 1165-1197) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick VI, Duke of Swabia (1167-1191) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto I, Count of Burgundy (1170-killed 1200) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad II, Duke of Swabia and Rothenburg (1173-killed 1196) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip of Swabia (1177-killed, 1208) King of Germany in 1198 
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice of Hohenstaufen (1162-1174). She was betrothed to William II of Sicily but died before they could be married. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes of Hohenstaufen (died October 1184). She was betrothed to Emeric of Hungary but died before they could be married.
2 CONT
