2 CONT Beatrice of Burgundy was the second wife and Empress of Frederick I, Holy Roman Emperor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice was active at the Hohenstaufen court, encouraging literary works and chivalric ideals. She accompanied her husband on his travels and campaigns across his kingdom, and Frederick Barbarossa was known to be under Beatrice's
2 CONC  influence.
2 CONT
2 CONT The poem Carmen de gestis Frederici I imperatoris in Lombardia, written about 1162, describes Beatrice upon her wedding day:
2 CONT
2 CONT     "Venus did not have this virgin's beauty,
2 CONT
2 CONT     Minerva did not have her brilliant mind
2 CONT
2 CONT     And Juno did not have her wealth.
2 CONT
2 CONT     There never was another except God's mother Mary
2 CONT
2 CONT     And Beatrice is so happy she excels her." 
2 CONT
2 CONT She bore 12 children with Frederick, including our ancestor Philip of Swabia.
2 CONT
2 CONT See http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beatrice,_Countess_of_Burgundy for more information.
