2 CONT
2 CONT Mathilde de Brabant, née en 1224, morte le 29 septembre 1288, était fille d'Henri II, duc de Brabant et de Marie de Hohenstaufen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elle épousa en premières noces à Compiègne le 14 juin 1237 Robert Ier d'Artois (1216 † 1250), fils de Louis VIII le Lion et de Blanche de Castille, et donna naissance à :
2 CONT
2 CONT #Blanche (1248 † 1302), mariée avec le roi Henri Ier de Navarre puis avec Edmund de Lancastre, un prince cadet anglais.
2 CONT
2 CONT #Robert II (1250 †1302), comte d'Artois
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert fut tué à Mansourah pendant la septième croisade et Mathilde se remaria avant 1254 à Guy III de Châtillon († 1289), comte de Saint-Pol. Ils eurent :
2 CONT
2 CONT #Hugues V († 1307), comte de Blois
2 CONT
2 CONT #Guy IV († 1317), comte de Saint-Pol
2 CONT
2 CONT #Jacques Ier († Courtrai 1302), seigneur de Leuze
2 CONT
2 CONT #Béatrice († 1304), mariée à Jean Ier de Brienne, comte d'Eu
2 CONT
2 CONT #Jeanne, mariée à Guillaume III de Chauvigny, seigneur de Châteauroux
2 CONT
2 CONT #Gertrude, mariée à Florent, seigneur de Malines
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda of Brabant
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matilda_of_Brabant
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda of Brabant (1224 – September 29, 1288) was the eldest daughter of Henry II, Duke of Brabant and his first wife Marie of Hohenstaufen.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 June 1237, Matilda married her first husband Robert I of Artois. The bride was about thirteen years old and the groom twenty-one. Robert was the fifth son of Louis VIII of France and Blanche of Castile. They had two children
2 CONC :
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche of Artois (1248 - 2 May 1302). Married first Henry I of Navarre and secondly Edmund Crouchback, 1st Earl of Lancaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II of Artois (1250 - 11 July 1302).
2 CONT
2 CONT On 8 February 1250, Robert I was killed while participating in the Seventh Crusade. Sometime between 1250 and 1254, Matilda married her second husband Guy III, Count of Saint-Pol. He was a younger son of consorts and co-rulers Hug
2 CONC h I, Count of Blois and Mary, Countess of Blois. They had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh II of Châtillon (d. 1307), Count of Saint Pol and later Count of Blois
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy III of Châtillon (d. 1317), Count of Saint Pol
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques I of Leuze-Châtillon (d. 1302, Battle of the Golden Spurs), first of the lords of Leuze, married Catherine de Condé and had issue; his descendants brought Condé, Carency, etc. into the House of Bourbon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrix (d. 1304), married John I of Brienne, Count of Eu
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne, married Guillaume III de Chauvigny, Lord of Châteauroux
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrude, married Florent, Lord of Mechelen (French: Malines).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche of Artois (1248 – 2 May 1302) was the queen regent of Navarre from 1274 to 1284, and later became Countess of Lancaster by marrying into the English royal family. She was the daughter of Count Robert I of Artois and Matild
2 CONC a of Brabant. From 1274 to 1284 she ruled Navarre and the counties of Brie, Champagne, Troyes et Meaux for her daughter, Joan I of Navarre (ruled 1274 to 1305).
2 CONT
2 CONT Her paternal grandparents were Louis VIII of France and Blanche of Castile. Her maternal grandparents were Henry II, Duke of Brabant and Marie of Hohenstaufen, daughter of Philip of Swabia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche married Henry I of Navarre (ruled 1270-1274) who died in 1274. They had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Theobald - d. 1270 fell from a battlement at the castle of Estella
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Joan I of Navarre, who became Queen regnant of Navarre and Queen consort of France
2 CONT
2 CONT After Henry's death, Blanche married Edmund Crouchback (1245-1296), in 1276, an English prince who was a younger son of Henry III and Eleanor of Provence. Edmund was also a widower, his young wife having died the same year as Blan
2 CONC che's husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund and Blanche had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Thomas Plantagenet, 2nd Earl of Lancaster (b. 1278)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Henry Plantagenet, 3rd Earl of Lancaster (b. 1281)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * John Plantagenet, Lord of Beaufort (c. 1282 - 1327)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Mary Plantagenet (c. 1284 - c. 1289)
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT Niece of Louis IX of France
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda of Brabant (1224 – September 29, 1288) was the eldest daughter of Henry II, Duke of Brabant and his first wife Marie of Hohenstaufen.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriages and children
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 June 1237, Matilda married her first husband Robert I of Artois. The bride was about thirteen years old and the groom twenty-one. Robert was the fifth son of Louis VIII of France and Blanche of Castile. They had two children
2 CONC :
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Blanche of Artois (1248 - 2 May 1302). Married first Henry I of Navarre and secondly Edmund Crouchback, 1st Earl of Lancaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Robert II of Artois (1250 - 11 July 1302).
2 CONT
2 CONT On 8 February 1250, Robert I was killed while participating in the Seventh Crusade. Sometime between 1250 and 1254, Matilda married her second husband Guy III, Count of Saint-Pol. He was a younger son of consorts and co-rulers Hug
2 CONC h I, Count of Blois and Mary, Countess of Blois. They had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hugh II of Châtillon (d. 1307), Count of Saint Pol and later Count of Blois
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Guy III of Châtillon (d. 1317), Count of Saint Pol
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Jacques I of Leuze-Châtillon (d. 1302, Battle of the Golden Spurs), first of the lords of Leuze, married Catherine de Condé and had issue; his descendants brought Condé, Carency, etc. into the House of Bourbon.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Beatrix (d. 1304), married John I of Brienne, Count of Eu
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Jeanne, married Guillaume III de Chauvigny, Lord of Châteauroux
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Gertrude, married Florent, Lord of Mechelen (French: Malines).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
