2 CONT
2 CONT Vsevolod, Pr of Pereyaslavl (1054-73), Pr of Chernigov (1073-78), Great Pr of Kiev (1076)+(1078-93), *1030, +13.4.1093; 1m: ca 1046 Anastasia Monomachina (+1067), dau.of Emperor Konstantinos IX of Byzantium by N Skleraina; 2m: ca 
2 CONC 1068 Anna (+7.10.1111), dau.of a khan of Kumans; He had issue:
2 CONT *A1. [1m.] Vladimir II "Monomachos", Pr of Rostov (1066-73), Pr of Smolensk (1073-93), Pr of Chernigov (1078-93), Pr of Pereyaslavl (1094-1113), Great Pr of Kiev (1113-25), he was the founder of Vladimir Town 1108, *1053, +nr Alta
2 CONC  River 19.5.1125, bur St Sophia Cathedral, Kiev; 1m: 1072-74 Gytha of Wessex (+Palestine 10.3.(1098)); 2m: ca 1099 a Byzantine noblewoman (+7.5.1107); 3m: N, dau.of a khan of Kumans (+11.7.1127)
2 CONT ** ...
2 CONT **B8. [2m.] Yuriy "Dologoruky" "Long arms", Pr of Rostov and Suzdal (1108-55) settled in Suzdal, Great Pr of Kiev (IX.1149-IV.1151)+(III.1155-V.1157), Founder of Moscow, *ca 1100, +Kiev 15.4.1157, bur Berestovo nr Kiev; 1m: ca 12.
2 CONC 1.1108 N, dau.of Aepa Khan of the Kumans; 2m: ca 1152 possibly Helene of Byzantium (+1183)
2 CONT *** ...
2 CONT ***C13. [2m.] Vsevolod III "Balshoe Gniezdo" "the Great Nest", Grand Pr of Kiev (II.1173-III.1173), 3d Grand Pr of Vladimir (1176-1212), *1154, +15.4.1212, bur Assumption Cathedral, Vladimir; 1m: Tbilisi 1170/72 St.Maria of Osseti
2 CONC a (+Vladimir 19.3.1206); 2m: 1209 Lyubov of Vitebsk (+after 1212); all kids by 1m.
2 CONT **** ...
2 CONT ****D4. Saint Yuriy II, 4th Grand Pr of Vladimir (1212-16)+(1218-38), *1188, +k.a.Sitj River 4.3.1238; m.10.4.1211 Agafia of Chernigov(+7.2.1238)
2 CONT *****E1. Vsevolod, Pr of Novgorod (1221-23), *23.10.1212, +perished during the massacre of Vladimir 7.2.1237; m.14.4.1230 Marina of Kiev (+perished 7.2.1238)
2 CONT *****E2. Mstislav, *1218, +k.a.Vladimir 7.2.1238; m.1236 Maria N (+7.2.1238)
2 CONT *****E3. Vladimir, Pr of Moscow (1237-38), +murdered by the Mongols 3/6.2.1238; m.1236 Christina N (+7.2.1238)
2 CONT *****E4. Feodora, *21.9.1229, +7.2.1238
2 CONT *****E5. '''Dobrava, +1265'''; m.1226 Pr Vasilko I of Volynia (*1203 +1269)
2 CONT **** ...
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leszek_the_White
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children[edit]
2 CONT
2 CONT Leszek married Grzymislawa of Luck in 1207. She was the daughter of Grand Prince Ingvar of Kiev, the ruler of Lutsk and its vicinity, a part of Galicia. Thus this marriage was part of Leszek's policy of eastward expansion. Leszek'
2 CONC s and Grzymislawa's daughter Salomea was born in 1211. She married King Coloman of Galicia-Lodomeria,[6] the son of King Andrew II of Hungary. The marriage occurred in about 1215 when Salome was 4 and Kaloman was 7. They were the 
2 CONC intended rulers of Galicia–Volhynia, but as noted above these plans failed and they never took up rule in that area.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leszek and Grzymislawa were also the parents of Bolesław V the Chaste, who assumed the Polish throne at Kraków in 1243, and '''Helen''', who married Vasylko Romanovich of Halych, son of Roman the Great.[7]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/POLAND.htm#Helenadied1265
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         '''HELENA (-1265)'''.  Her origin is confirmed by the Russian source cited by Baumgarten which specifies that Prince Bolesław V was the maternal uncle of the children of Prince Vasilko[398].  Baumgarten records the deat
2 CONC h in 1265 of Helena, wife of Vasilko, citing a Russian source[399].  m (1248) as his second wife, VASILKO Romanovich of Galicia Prince of Bielsk, Luck and Vladimir in Volynia, son of ROMAN Mstislavich Prince of Galich, Grand Princ
2 CONC e of Kiev & his second wife --- [of Byzantium] (1203-1269).  He succeeded his brother in 1260 as VASILKO King of Galich. 
