1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otho_of_Saint-Omer
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Otho of Saint Omer''' was the lord of half of Thebes in Frankish Greece from 1294 to ca. 1299.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a younger son of Bela of Saint Omer and Bonne de la Roche, sister of the Lord of Athens and Thebes, Guy I de la Roche. Upon their marriage, in 1240, Guy gave Bela the lordship over half of Thebes.[1][2] Otho participated, a
2 CONC long with his brothers Nicholas II and John, in the War of the Euboeote Succession in the ranks of the coalition of most of the princes of Frankish Greece, who opposed the expansionist policies of the Prince of Achaea, William II 
2 CONC of Villehardouin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Otho was married to Margarita da Verona. After Nicholas II's death in 1294, he succeeded him as lord of one half of Thebes until his own death, sometime before 1299
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20LORDSHIPS%20IN%20GREECE.htm#OthonStOmerdiedbefore1299
2 CONT
2 CONT b)       '''  OTHON de Saint-Omer '''(-before 1299).  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis names "Nicolaum, Ottonem et Joannem" as the three sons of "Bilas"[940].  The Livre de la Conqueste de la Morée names “me
2 CONC ssire Belas…de Saint Omer” as father of “ces trois freres de Saint Omer” (“le noble baron Jehan de Saint Omer, le frere monseignor Nicole de Saint Omer, le seignor de la moitié d Estives, et de messire Otthe”)[941].  The Livre de 
2 CONC la Conqueste de la Morée names “messire Jehans et messire Othe de Sainct Omer” as brothers of “messire Nicolas de Saint Omer”[942].  Joint Lord of Thebes 1294-1296.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (after [1262/64] ) as her second husband, MARGHERITA da Verona, widow of GRAPELLA da Verona, daughter of GUGLIELMO I da Verona Triarch of Eubœa & his wife ---.  The Istoria of Marino Sanudo Torsello names "la prima…madonna
2 CONC  Felisa…la seconda…madonna Margarita…la terze…madonna Porzia" as the three daughters of "miser Guglielmo da Verona", adding that Margherita married "miser Grapella signor d´un Terzer" and secondly "miser Oston de S. Homer signor d
2 CONC ella mità di Tebbe"[943].  
