2 CONT Géza II (Hungarian: II. Géza, Slovak: Gejza II, Croatian: Gejza II), (1130, Tolna – 31 May 1162), King of Hungary(1141–1162).[1][2][3] He ascended the throne as a child and during his minority the kingdom was governed by his mothe
2 CONC r. He was one of the most powerful monarchs of Hungary, who could intervene successfully in the internal affairs of the neighbouring countries.
