2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Pierre I de France, sn de Courtenay, de Tanlay, de Champignelles, etc, *1126, +Palestine 1179/10.4.1183 !dwid!; m.1150/55 Elizabeth de Joinville, Dame de Courtenay (*Courtenay 1127, +after 14.9.1205) dau.of Renaud de Courte
2 CONC nay; they had issue:
2 CONT *A1. Cte Pierre II de Courtenay 1193, Cte de Nevers, d'Auxerre et de Tonnerre 1184, Emperor of Constantinople (1216-19), Marquis de Namur, *1155, +Epirus after VI.1219; By his second marriage, he was called upon in 1217 to succeed
2 CONC  to the Latin Empire of the Orient, created following the capture of Constantinople in the course of the Fourth Crusade. But on the way to his Empire, he was victim of a Greek ambush. Baudouin tried to engage the fief of Courtenay
2 CONC  to Villehardouin, but King Louis IX objected. However, his son Philippe was able to engage to the Venetians. Later, through marriage, Courtenay was reunited with the Crown, after a possession by the King of Castile; 1m: 1184 Cts 
2 CONC Agnes de Nevers, d'Auxerre et de Tonnerre (*1170 +1192) dau.of Cte Guy I de Nevers and Mathilde de Bourgogne; 2m: Soissons 1.7.1193 Mgvne Yolande of Namur (*1175 +1219) dau.of Ct Baldwin V of Flanders and Hainaut
2 CONT **B1. [1m.] Mahaut de Courtenay, Cts de Nevers, d'Auxerre et de Tonnerre, *1188, +Abbaye de Fontevrault 12.10.1257, bur there; 1m: 1199 (div 1213) Hervé IV, Seigneur de Donzy; 2m: 1226 Guigues IV d'Albon, Cte de Forez (+1241)
2 CONT **B2. [2m.] Philippe de Courtenay, Margrave of Namur (1217-26), *1195, +k.a. St.Flour-en-Auvergne 1226, bur Abbaye de Vaucelles, Cambrai
2 CONT **B3. [2m.] Pierre de Courtenay, a priest, *1196, living 1212
2 CONT **B4. [2m.] Robert I de Courtenay, Emperor of Constantinople (1221-28), *1201, +Morea/Morée, Loir-et-Cher, France I.1228; m.1228 a dau.of Baudoin de Neufville
2 CONT **B5. [2m.] Henri de Courtenay, Mgve of Namur (1226-29), *1206, +1229
2 CONT **B6. [2m.] Baldwin de Courtenay, Emperor of Constantinople (1237-61) =Baldwin II, *Constantinople 1218, +Naples 1273, bur Barletta; m.Perugia 1229/1234 Marie de Brienne (+after 5.5.1275)
2 CONT *** ..
2 CONT **B7. [2m.] Marguerite, Dame de Chateauneuf-sur-Cher, Mgvne of Namur (1229-37), *1194, +17.7.1270, bur Marienthal; 1m: ca 1210 Raoul I de Lusignan, Seigneur d'Issoudun (+1216); 2m: 1216 Gf Heinrich I von Vianden (+1252)
2 CONT **B8. [2m.] Sibylle, a nun, *1197, +Abbey de Fontevrault V.1210
2 CONT **B9. [2m.] Elizabeth, *1199, +after 1269; 1m: before 1219 Cte Gaucher de Bar-sur-Seine (+1219); 2m: 1220 Eudes I de Bourgogne, sn de Montagu (*1196 +1243/7)
2 CONT **B10. [2m.] '''Yolande de Courtenay, *ca 1194, 1200, +1233, bur Egrecz Abbey'''; m.1215 King András II of Hungary (*1176 +21.9.1235)
2 CONT **B11. [2m.] Agnés, *1202, +after 1247; m.1217 Geoffroy II de Villehardouin, Pr of Achaia (+1246), son of Geoffroy de Villehardouin and Elisabeth de Troyes
2 CONT **B12. [2m.] Marie, *1204, +Nicea IX.1222; m.1219 Emperor Theodoros I of Nicaea (+1222)
2 CONT **B13. [2m.] Eléonore de Courtenay, *1208, +1230, bur Abbaye de St.Antoine-des-Champs, Paris; m.before 1220 Philippe I de Montfort-l'Amaury, sn de Castres-en-Albegeois (+17.3.1270)
2 CONT **B14. [2m.] Constance, a nun at Fontevrault, *1210, +Abbaye de Fontevrault after 1215, bur there
