1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boniface_of_Verona
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT - http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/bonifacio-da-verona_(Dizionario-Biografico)/
2 CONT
2 CONT È ben possibile che il D. fosse un cavaliere povero che giunse alla corte di Guy de la Roche intorno al 1287. fu favorito dal duca, ricevette in moglie una pupilla di questo - la quale forse si chiamava '''Simona''' /!\
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20LORDSHIPS%20IN%20GREECE.htm#BonifazioVeronaEuboeadied1317
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         BONIFAZIO da Verona (-1317).  His parentage is confirmed by the Istoria of Marino Sanudo Torsello which names "miser Francesco da Verona padre de miser Bonifacio"[594].  Guy II Duke of Athens granted him a revenue of 50
2 CONC ,000 sols, his own mother's dowry of Gardiki in Thessaly and the island of Salamis, and arranged his marriage at the ceremony of his coming of age in 1294[595].  He recaptured Karistos from the Greeks, establishing himself as Tria
2 CONC rch of Eubœa (northern part) in 1296[596].  The Istoria of Marino Sanudo Torsello records that "miser Bonifacio da Verona, figlio de miser Francesco" acquired "il castel di Caristo…per sua consorte"[597]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -        EUBŒA - TRIARCHATE (NORTHERN PART).  /!\
2 CONT
2 CONT - - - - - - 
2 CONT
2 CONT /!\ -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20LORDSHIPS%20IN%20GREECE.htm#BonifazioVeronaEuboeadied1317B
2 CONT
2 CONT BONIFAZIO da Verona Lord of 1/3 Eubœa, son of GUGLIELMO [II] da Verona Lord of 1/3 Eubœa & his wife --- (-1317).  Guy II Duke of Athens granted him a revenue of 50,000 sols, his own mother's dowry of Gardiki in Thessaly and the is
2 CONC land of Salamis, and arranged his marriage at the ceremony of his coming of age in 1294[518].  He recaptured Karistos from the Greeks, establishing himself as Triarch of Eubœa (northern part) in 1296[519].  Duke Guy appointed Boni
2 CONC fazio as temporary administrator of the duchy of Athens when he died[520].  He fought at Kephissos River, near Thebes 15 Mar 1311 against the Catalans, but the latter asked him to be their leader after the battle, which he refused
2 CONC [521].  "Ser Bonifacius de Verona, dominator Caristi et Gardichie, Selizirij et Egue" is included in the list of Barons "de Romania" with whom Venice maintained relations in 1313[522]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m AGNES de Cicon, daughter of GUY de Cicon Titular Triarch of Eubœa (northern part) & his wife ---.  The Istoria of Marino Sanudo Torsello records that "miser Bonifacio da Verona, figlio de miser Francesco" acquired "il castel di 
2 CONC Caristo…per sua consorte"[523].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Bonifazio & his wife had two children:  
