2 CONT
2 CONT i)          BARTOLOMEO [III] Ghisi (-[18 Sep 1383/24 Jul 1390]).  Triarch of Eubœa (northern part) and Lord of Mykonos and Tinos, under the guardianship of his mother.  Marshall of the Principality of Achaia.  He was appointed mem
2 CONC ber of the High Council of the Republic of Venice in 1383, in compensation for Venice having bought the suzerainty over Eubœa from Jacques des Baux titular Emperor of Constantinople[743].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' THEODORA Asanina, daughter of --- (-1/21 May 1398).  Bartolomeo [III] & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *(a)       GIORGIO Ghisi (-1390).  Triarch of Eubœa, he bequeathed his share in Eubœa to Venice in 1390[744].  
