1 NAME Jean de Flandre, Bishop of Metz, Bishop of Liège
2 GIVN Jean
2 NSFX de Flandre, Bishop of Metz, Bishop of Liège
1 NAME Jean de Flandre, Bishop of Metz, Bishop of Liège
1 NAME Johann(es) der Juengere
2 GIVN Johann(es) der Juengere
2 SURN
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Flines-lez-Raches
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1250
2 PLAC Anhève
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 14 APR 1292
1 OCCU Bishop of Metz and later of Luettich
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} GUY de Dampierre
2 CONT m firstly (contract 2 Feb 1246) MATHILDE de Béthune
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy & his first wife had eight children:
2 CONT '''3.         JEAN de Flandre ([1250]-Anhève 14 Apr 1292, bur Flines-lez-Raches).  The Genealogia Comitum Flandriæ names (in order) "Robertum, Willelmum, Iohannem episcopum Leodiensum, Balduinem et Philippum" the sons of "Guido…ex
2 CONC  Mathilde filia Roberti Tenremontensis"[684].  The Annales Blandinienses record the death in 1291 of "Iohannes, filius Guidonis comitis Flandrie et Mathildis de Bethunia eius coniugis, episcopus Leodiensis" specifying his burial a
2 CONC t "Felinis" {Flines-lez-Raches, near Douai}[685].  Provost of St Donat at Bruges 1270.  Provost of St Pierre at Lille 1274/77.  Bishop of Metz 1279.  The Gesta Episcoporum Mettensium (Continuatio) records the succession of “filius
2 CONC  comitis Flandrensis dominus Johannes” who was later transferred “ad Leodiensem ecclesiam”[686].  Bishop of Liège 1282.  A letter dated 13 Oct 1291 bears his seal[687].  The Biographie Nationale de Belgique records his death 14 Ap
2 CONC r 1292 at Anhève but does not cite the corresponding primary source[688].  The early 17th century artist Antoine Succa sketched some details of his monument[689].''' 
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLANDERS,%20HAINAUT.htm#Margueritedied1331
