2 CONT Infante don RAMON BERENGUER de Aragón, son of JAIME II King of Aragon & his second wife Blanche of Sicily ([1308]-Barcelona 1364).  The Crónica de San Juan de la Peña names "el primero…Don Jayme…el secundo Don Alfonso…el tercero D
2 CONC on Johan…el quarto Don Pedro…el quinto Don Ramon Berenguer" as the five sons of King Jaime II and his wife Blanca, stating that Ramon Berenguer was "Conte de Pradas" but later exchanged Prades for Empúries with his brother Pedro[1
2 CONC 630].  Conde de Prades 1324-1341.  Comte de Empúries 1341-1364.  Zurita names “los Infantes don Pedro y don Ramon Berenguer, don Alonso Conde de Ribagorça y Denia, don Pedro Conde de Urgel, don Juan Conde de Prades hermano del Con
2 CONC de de Ribagorça y don Juan...Conde de Ampurias hijo del Infante Ramon Berenguer” among Aragonese nobles obliged to swear homage to the king of Navarre in 1364[1631].  He became a priest in Barcelona. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ([1327/28]) BLANCHE di Tarento, daughter of PHILIPPE of Sicily [Anjou-Capet] Principe di Tarento & his first wife Thamar [Catarina] Angelina Komnene Dukaina of Epirus (-before 1337).  Zurita names “doña Blanca...hi
2 CONC ja de Filipo Principe de Taranto y hermana del Despoto de Romania” as first wife of Ramon Berenguer and mother of his daughter Juana, when recording the latter’s marriage[1632]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (Valencia 1338) as her second husband, MARÍA Álvarez de Ejérica, widow of GUGLIELMO of Sicily Principe di Tarento, Duke of Athens and Neopatrai [Aragon], daughter of JAIME [II] de Aragón Barón de Ejérica & his wif
2 CONC e Beatriz de Lauria Señora de Cocentaina ([1310]-before 1364). 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Ramon Berenguer & his first wife had two children:
