2 CONT 8.         [ANNA Komnene.  The name of Count Maio [II]'s wife is attested as Anna.  An unnamed count of Kefalonia is described as "sororius" of Theodoros Angelos, Emperor at Thessaloniki, but it is not known whether this refers to
2 CONC  Maio [II][39].  If it does, his wife may have been the daughter of Ioannes Komnenos Angelos.  This is the solution proposed by Sturdza[40], who says that her brother Theodoros gave her husband Corfu as dowry on his marriage.  How
2 CONC ever, if it is correct that the marriage took place shortly before 1228, there appear to be chronological difficulties with this proposed parentage.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Europäische Stammtafeln[41] suggests that [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodora-Komnene/6000000009049622359 '''Theodora'''], daughter of Mikhael [I] Komnenos Doukas Angelos Lord of Epirus was the same person as Anna, wife of Cou
2 CONC nt Maio [II].  The basis for this speculation is not known, although it would appear more acceptable from a chronological point of view.  It is always possible that "sororius" is an error in the source referred to above.  Another 
2 CONC possibility is that the Count of Kefalonia in question was Maio [I] and that the daughter of Ioannes Angelos was his [first/second] wife who is unrecorded elsewhere.  If that is correct, there would be no basis for stating that he
2 CONC r name was Anna.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 1228) MAIO [II] Orsini Count of Kefalonia, son of [MAIO Orsini Count of Kefalonia & his wife --- Margaritone] (-[1259/64]).] 
