2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20LORDSHIPS%20IN%20GREECE.htm#MaioOrsinidied12591264
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         MAIO [II] [Orsini] (-[1259/64]).  The parentage of Maio [II] is not known.  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[635], he was the possible son of Maio [I].  Sturdza states that his father was Riccardo Orsini[636].  The 
2 CONC basis for these speculations is not known.  It is possible that they are founded on no more than guesswork.  Count of Kefalonia before 1228.  Vassal of Epirus 1228.  Vassal of Achaia 1236.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 1228) ANNA, daughter of ---.  The name of Maio's wife is attested as Anna.  An unnamed count of Kefalonia is described as "sororius" of Theodoros Angelos, Emperor at Thessaloniki, but it is not known whether this r
2 CONC efers to Maio [II][637].  If it does, his wife may have been Anna Komnene [Angelina], daughter of Ioannes Komnenos Angelos & his wife ---.  This is the solution adopted by Sturdza[638], who says that her brother Theodoros gave her
2 CONC  husband Corfu as dowry on his marriage.  However, if the marriage took place shortly before 1228, there appear to be chronological difficulties with this proposed parentage.  Europäische Stammtafeln[639] suggests that Theodora, d
2 CONC aughter of Mikhael [I] Komnenos Dukas Angelos Lord of Epirus was the same person as Anna, wife of Count Maio [II].  The basis for this speculation is not known, although it would appear to be more acceptable from a chronological p
2 CONC oint of view.  It is always possible that "sororius" is an error in the source referred to above.  Another possibility is that the Count of Kefalonia in question was Maio [I] and that the daughter of Ioannes Angelos was his [first
2 CONC /second] wife who is unrecorded elsewhere.  If this is correct, there would be no basis for stating that her name was Anna.  Count Maio [II] & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         daughter .  '''m''' GUILLAUME de Méry, son of GEOFFROY de Méry [Constable of the Latin Empire of Constantinople] & his wife ---. 
