2 CONT a)         GEOFFROY de Milly (-15 Apr 1300).  Minieri Riccio names “Goffredo” as the only son of “Guglielmo de Milly”, recording that he succeeded in his father’s fiefs listed above, was also “signore di Castiglione presso Foggia”
2 CONC , was named at Pentecost 1272, received custody of the castle of Petruro in 1275, was created Seneschal of the kingdom 26 May 1294[401].  He was accused of treason and exiled by order dated 2 Oct 1297 which confiscates the fiefs h
2 CONC eld by “nobilis vir dominus Goffridus de Miliaco”, but was restored to his fiefs and his post of Seneschal 28 Aug 1298[402].  He died 15 Apr 1300[403].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ---.  Minieri Riccio says that Geoffroy’s first wife is not known[404].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly FILIPPA di Manoppello, daughter of GIORDANO Conte di Manoppello & his wife Tommasa di Pagliara Contessa di Manoppello.  Minieri Riccio names “Filippa figliuola primogenita del conte Giordano e di Tommasa di Paglia
2 CONC ra contessa di Manoppello e signore di Guardiagrele”, whose dowry was “Pagliara, Delicastelli e Rivicarraro”, as Geoffroy de Milly’s second wife[405].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' thirdly as her third husband, AGNESE Orsini, widow firstly of JEAN de Cléry and secondly of AMAURY de Saint-Clair, daughter of RICCARDO Orsini Count of Kefalonia & his first wife --- (-after 30 May 1317).  Minieri Riccio n
2 CONC ames “Agnese di Cefalonia signora di S. Martino in Pensile e della metà di Portocandone”, whose dowry was “Palo ed Aricario in Terra di Bari” and whose first husband was “il milite Americo de Saint Claire” by whom she had “un figl
2 CONC iuolo...Giovanni, che ereditò dal padre la terra di Limatola”, as Geoffroy de Milly’s third wife[406].  She married fourthly (before 20 Jul 1300) Gaucher de Noyers Seigneur de Pouilly, de Cérisey, de Vézinnes et de Chassignelles. 
2 CONC
