2 CONT 5.         ALASIA (-Kirenia castle 1233 before Apr, bur Nicosia Santa Sofia).  She is named "Aalais" by William of Tyre (Continuator), who names her husband and specifies that she was "fille dou marquis de Monferrare"[199].  The C
2 CONC hronicle of Amadi records the marriage of "re de Cypro Henrico" and "una donzella sua cugina, figlia del marchese de Monferatho Guielmo Longa Spada, che fo cugin del imperator"[200], although it is chronologically impossible for h
2 CONC er to have been the daughter of the only member of the Monferrato family who is normally referred to as "Longo Spada".  This marriage was arranged by Emperor Friedrich II while he was in Cyprus in May 1229 en route back to Europe 
2 CONC from Jerusalem, the bride's father being one of the emperor's strongest supporters in Italy[201].  She came to Cyprus with imperial troops in 1231 but it is unlikely that she ever met her husband who was in Palestine for most of t
2 CONC he civil war in Cyprus.  She took refuge in the castle of Kirenia with the Lombards but died before the castle's surrender to the Ibelin troops in Apr 1233[202].  William of Tyre (Continuator) records that she had been crowned que
2 CONC en by her husband when he records the coronation of his second wife "come il avoit fait Alays la fille dou marquis de Monferrare"[203].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (May 1229) as his first wife, HENRI I King of Cyprus, son of HUGUES I King of Cyprus & his wife Alix of Jerusalem Ctss of Jaffa (3 Mar 1217-18 Jan 1253). 
