1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In letters patent of 22 November 1670, Charles II of Spain recalls the coat of arms and motto of the arms of Cambrai and describes: "Azure a chevron silver, accompanied by three Besons well, lined with gold, surmou
2 CONC nted by a silver helmet. Crest: a peacock in natural, natural to the tail (beating him) walking on the ridge that hachements is like silver and azure, supported by two savages " But the portrait of Aubert, they are not mirrors of 
2 CONC Besons but clearly drawn as follows: "Azure a chevron silver, accompanied by three antique mirrors round shape even bordered with gold. The ecu stamped with a silver helmet, and grilled free gold, adorned with his Bourlet and mant
2 CONC ling of its blue and silver and over in crest, a peacock in natural beating him. Tenants, two wild carnation, covered and crowned with ivy leaves vert, each holding in hand a club to put on the natural shoulder " It is a test char
