1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephen_of_Armenia
2 CONT =Stephen of Armenia=
2 CONT Stephen of Armenia (died February 7, 1165) was the Marshal of Armenia, the son of Leo I, Prince of Armenia and Beatrice de Rethel.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father made him Marshal in 1138, due to the invasion of John II Comnenus, and escaped capture by sheltering in Edessa. In 1157, he began raiding Byzantine territories around Marash against his half-brother Thoros' will, althou
2 CONC gh he failed to capture Marash itself. The Byzantine governor of Tarsus, Andronicus Euphorbenus, invited him to a banquet and murdered him on February 7, 1165. Thoros revenged his death with a massacre of Greeks within his territo
2 CONC ries, which would have led to war had not Amalric I of Jerusalem intervened to bring about a peace.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had at least three children by his wife Rita of Barbaron: Ruben III, Leo II and Dolete, who married Bertrand Embriaco.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ARMENIA.htm#Stephanedied1165B
2 CONT
2 CONT '''STEPANE''', son of LEWON I Lord of the Mountains & his wife Béatrice de Rethel (before 1110-murdered 7 Feb 1165, bur Arkagaghine).  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "Thoros, Stephane, Mleh et Rupin" as the four sons of L
2 CONC ewon[482].  The Lignages d'Outremer record that "Stephane et Mleh" fled "pour Edesse chez leur oncle" after their father and two brothers were captured by imperial forces and taken to Constantinople[483].  He joined forces with hi
2 CONC s half-brother Thoros after the latter's escape from Constantinople in 1143[484].  The Chronicle of Grégoire le Prêtre records that "Sdéphanê, frère du general des arméniens" and the Templars defeated the Turks "la grande ville de
2 CONC  Tarse et de Mecis" in [1155][485].  The Chronicle of Patriarch Michel le Grand records that "Stéphané frère du baron Thoros" invaded "le territoire de Marach" in 584 (Armenian calendar)[486].  The Lignages d'Outremer record that 
2 CONC "Stephane" was captured after the death of his brother Thoros "sur la frontière de Hamus", was cooked in a boiling cauldron, and buried at "Ark'akarin"[487].  Stepane was murdered, possibly with the complicity of Andronikos Komnen
2 CONC os, Governor of Cilicia, which triggered his half-brother Thoros to attack the Byzantine garrisons at Mamistra, Anazarbus and Vahka[488].  The Chronicle of Patriarch Michel le Grand records that "le prince Andronic…dans la Cilicie
2 CONC " invited "le baron Stéphané à un festin" where he was murdered[489].  Kirakos Ganjaketsi's History of Armenia records that "Andronikos treacherously seized Stepane and had him killed"[490].  The Chronographie of Samuel d'Ani reco
2 CONC rds that "Sdephanê" was killed after being thrown into a boiling cauldron by the Greeks[491].  The Chronicle of Grégoire le Prêtre records the death of "Sdéphanê, frère di grand Thoros, sébaste, et fils de Léon" after the betrayal
2 CONC  "d'un duc scélerat" in 1165[492]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [1143/44] ) RITA, daughter of SMBAT Lord of Barbaron [Armenia-Hethum] & his wife --- (-[1210]).  The Chronique du Royaume de la Petite Arménie of Constable Sempad records that names "fille de Sempad, seigneur de Babaron 
2 CONC et sœur de Pagouran…Ritha" as wife of "Sdephanê"[493].  She succeeded in 1205 as Lady of Lampron. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Stepane & his wife had [three] children:
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
