1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Sommaire=
2 CONT * Marquis de Montferrat (1418-1445) :
2 CONT ** précédé de [http://www.geni.com/people/Teodoro-II-Palaiologos/6000000006405101490 Théodore II]
2 CONT ** succédé par [http://www.geni.com/people/John-IV-Margrave-of-Montferrat/6000000006595911272 Jean IV]
2 CONT * A porté le titre de compte d'Aquofana pendant la vie de son père.
2 CONT * Il se ligua avec les Vénitiens et les Florentins contre Philippe Sforce, duc de Milan; se rendit maître de Cazal et du reste de Montferrat.
2 CONT * Prit sa retraite à Vénice et fut rétabli dans so état par le traité de Ferrare, conclu le 25 avril 1433.
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT * [http://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000027609064898 Moreri, L., ''Le Grand Dictionnaire Historique -- Les Montferrat'', 1759] (ci-joint)
2 CONT * [http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marchesato_del_Monferrato#Periodo_Paleologo Marchesato del Monferrato, Wikipédia]
2 CONT * [http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giovanni_Giacomo_del_Monferrato Giovanni Giacomo del Monferrato, Wikipédia]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====================
2 CONT
2 CONT John Jacob of Montferrat
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT John Jacob Palaeologus (Italian: Giovanni Giacomo Paleologo; March 23, 1395 - March 12, 1445) was the Margrave of Montferrat from 1418 to 1435.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Trino, Piedmont, the son of Theodore II of Montferrat, with whom he collaborated in the government of the marquisate from 1404. In 1412 he married Joanna of Savoy, sister of Duke Amadeus VIII, who gave him numerous 
2 CONC children.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his father's death in 1418, John Jacob received the investiture as marquess by emperor Sigismund. He distinguished himself for some brilliant military campaign in the Apennines area; he also increased his prestige through th
2 CONC e marriage between his sister Sofia and the second last Byzantine Emperor, John VIII Palaeologus.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Jacob's expansion, however, spurred the reaction of the Dukes of Savoy and of Filippo Maria Visconti of Milan. In 1431 they signed an alliance aiming at the cancellation of the Montferrat state. John Jacob was therefore compe
2 CONC lled to ask support to France. In 1432 he was defeated anyway and sued for peace, ceding several territories to Savoy but retaining the seigniory over Montferrat, although with the status of Savoy vassal.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, when Amadeus VIII asked him the payment of the war expenses, John Jacob rebelled; but, after having besieged in Chivasso, he was forced to cease. His state and his prestige were shattered, and he had again to declare hims
2 CONC elf vassal of Savoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Jacob died at Casale Monferrato in 1445, being succeeded by his son John IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT PVD's fifth cousin 15 times removed.
