1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Darvish Mohammed Khan was the Khan of Sheki (1524-1551). He ascended the throne after his father's assassination in May of the year 1524.
2 CONT
2 CONT He 1538 helped Shahrukh of Shirvan against Safavids but without success he retreated to Shaki. Next year he married to Pari Khan Khanum, daughter of Tahmasp I. He sent his son Bagi beg as hostage to Safavid court. In 1551 Tahmasp 
2 CONC I started invasion of Shaki with Levan of Kakheti. Result of massive invasion was death of khan, devastation of castles Galarsan-Gorarsan and Kish. Shaki was given to Toygun beg Qajar. Khan's son Bagi beg was held as prisoner in s
2 CONC hah's court.
2 CONT
2 CONT ref:http://www.vostlit.info/Texts/rus16/Chadzi_Seid_Abdulhamid/text.phtml?id=2210 HAJI SEID ABDULGAMID PEDIGREE OF SHEKINA KHANS AND THEIR DESCENDANTS
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Dervish Muhammad Khan, becoming in 914 (1508 - 1509) 3 Khan after his father, ceased to obey the Persian Shah Shah Takhmasb, the son of Shah Ismail, and rebelled [against him]. Enraged by such behavior of Dervish Muhammad 
2 CONC Khan, Shah Tahmasb-na Sheki, in order to punish Dervish Muhammad Khan. Shah Tahmasb, having collected troops, moved from Iran. Dervish Muhammad Khan fled and fortified himself in a gorge called Gelyasan-gyorasan. Some residents of
2 CONC  Sheki and Nukhi left [for him] to Gelyasan-gyorasan, while others locked themselves in the Kish fortress. Shah Tahmasb sent troops daily against the fortress. Finally , he took the Kish fortress and ordered it to be destroyed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Seeing this circumstance, Dervish Muhammad Khan fled from Gelyasan-Gyorasan, but fell into the hands of the Shah's people. They cut off his head and brought him to the Shah. Sheki residents began to ask [the shah] for mercy. The S
2 CONC hah forgave them and ordered them to settle in their places. Baghi bey, the son of Dervish Muhammad Khan, also appeared to the Shah [confessed]. Although the shah did not order him to be executed, he did not give Bagi-bek the khan
2 CONC 's power. To manage the affairs of Sheki, he appointed one of the noble Nukhians named Huseynjan as his firman as a melik. Melik Huseynjan died in ... year. On the shah's command, his son Kaim yuzbashi became a melik. Melik Kaim d
2 CONC ied in ... year. [Then] his son, named Melik Ahmed, becoming a melik of Nukhi, ruled over the Sheki vilayet.
2 CONT
2 CONT ref: http://www.vostlit.info/Texts/rus16/Chadzi_Seid_Abdulhamid/text.phtml?id=2210 HAJI SEID ABDULGAMID PEDIGREE OF SHEKINA KHANS AND THEIR DESCENDANTS
