2 CONT i)          FIORENZA Sanudo (-1371).  She succeeded her father in 1362 as FIORENZA I Dss of Naxos.  Her first marriage is confirmed by the 16th century Annali Veneti of Stefano Magno which names "Fiorenza Sanudo…fiola…de Marco San
2 CONC udo fradelo fu de Januli Sanudo ducha de Archipielago" as mother of "Nicolò dale Carcere ducha del Arcipielago" when recording the latter´s death "in la citade de Nicosia" in 1383[791].  Venice vetoed her potential second husbands
2 CONC , first the Genoese lord of Chios, then Nerio Acciaiuoli future Duke of Athens, anxious to increase its influence over the duchy by arranging a suitable match for her.  She was kidnapped by Venetian agents, taken to Crete and blac
2 CONC kmailed into marrying her cousin Niccolo[792].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly GIOVANNI dalle Carceri Lord of Euboea, son of PIETRO [Perulli] dalle Carceri Lord of Eubœa & his wife --- (-1358).  ...one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly as his second wife, NICOLÒ Sanudo "Spezzabanda", son of GUGLIELMO Sanudo & his wife --- (-1374).  The candidate of Venice, the republic granted him the title Duke on his marriage.  After the death of his wife, he 
2 CONC continued to govern the duchy as avogier on behalf of his stepson[793].   ... two children:
