1 NAME Sor /de Naves/
2 GIVN Sor
2 SURN de Naves
2 _MARNM de Naves
1 SEX M
1 OCCU Sea Leader/ Sea Pirate
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to a translation from Giuseppe Müller's book in 2014 called ''Documenti sulle relazioni delle città Toscane coll'Oriente Cristiano e coi Turchi fino all'anno MDXXXI'' [https://books.google.com.mt/books?id
2 CONC =r_PCAwAAQBAJ&pg=PA497&lpg=PA497&dq=Sor+de+Naves&source=bl&ots=8JYHoiX3ZD&sig=ACfU3U2vZsdAKhe6qUoeNDlBQc-PukSJhA&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiVwc6vj-PmAhWKQEEAHb7GAGQQ6AEwBHoECAkQAQ#v=onepage&q=Sor%20de%20Naves&f=false] :     
2 CONT
2 CONT The Spanish pirate, against whom the Florentine Republic claims here, can only be the Siciliano Sor De Naves, who played an important part in the war of Charlotte Queen of Cyprus with her brother Iacopo II. He was a sea leader who
2 CONC  possessed various galleys, and at the same time a kind of pirate, who he had a name feared in the East; neither did he, like a Michael of Malta and others, run, nor always distinguish between Saracens and Christians.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was partisan of Queen Charlotte, who in 1461 sailed on her galleys to go to Italy: but when she sailed from Rhodes, she was attacked and robbed by Venetian galleys (see note to Doc. CXLII-CXLVII). Sor de Naves took flight, beca
2 CONC use he was guilty of pirating; as the Senate of Venice asserted. He accompanied Queen Charlotte to the West for another voyage, and on February 3rd  1462 (he apparently promised):  I swear to you, in Lausanne, that from 15th March
2 CONC  to the end of October of that year it would hold to a galley available in the port of Villafranca (near Nice) so that it could return to its island (Cyprus). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Being that Queen Charlotte arrived there (probably in February 1462), Sor de Naves was sent with galleys to Paphos, to establish Father/Brother Pietro as commander. Returning from there, Sor de Naves had a conflict in the Gulf of 
2 CONC Pendaja with Demetrius of Corone, who for Jacopo commanded in the maritime district. In 1463, when Carlotta left Cyprus again to retire to Rhodes, Sor de Naves returned to the command in Cerines (today known as Kyrenia/Girne), the
2 CONC  only city loyal to Queen Charlotte.
2 CONT
2 CONT But being seriously besieged by Jacopo, and without hope of being rescued, and almost abandoned- brought to his senses, Sor de Naves believed it well to hand Cerines over to Jacopo, who through his brother was promised the dignity
2 CONC  of being the constable of Cyprus, and the hand of his natural daughter Charlotte.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sor de Naves' pirating are ascertained from documents such as that of the ship of a Venetian Giovanni Fabrini and of certain Anconitan ships; for which Ancona complained to P. R. Zacosta, Grand Master of Rhodes on 12th January 146
2 CONC 7; who orders for the seizure of all real estate owned by Sor De Naves in Rhodes, although in 1463 he had called him a dear friend and granted him:
2 CONT
2 CONT "(because of his personal merits and the services he rendered to the house of St. John of Jerusalem considering further that his galleys can be of great help in the defense of the Order's forces, which were attacked unceasingly by
2 CONC  the Turks), special and complete Letters of protection for himself and his debts, so that he may remain in Rhodes and in all the lands under  the jurisdiction of the order, assured of complete security for himself, his ships and 
2 CONC his people. " 
