1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In the spring of 1527, the Dieci ordered Girolamo di Giorgio Corner, captaingeneral
2 CONT of the island, to raise an army and attack the rebellious villages, telling
2 CONT him to do whatever it took to “securely eradicate them and have them cut to
2 CONT pieces,” giving him permission “to have their villages destroyed and to confiscate
2 CONT their goods and to make every other harsh provision that seems to you will set an
2 CONT example and terrorize other rebels.”96 Even before his election as captain, Corner’s
2 CONT marriage to the daughter of the Veneto-Cretan feudatory Marco di Antonio
2 CONT Mudazzo meant that he had significant connections to island society, connections
2 CONT that proved useful in his task as captain.97 Corner’s father-in-law, Marco
2 CONT Mudazzo, was married to a daughter of Matteo di Andrea Calergi
2 CONT
2 CONT O'Connell, Men of Empire
