1 NOTE {geni:about_me} It was designed by Andrea Palladio about 1552, for his friend Francesco Pisani, who was part of the Dal Banco arm of the family and whose father was a first cousin of Cardinal Francesco Pisani. Francesco and Pallad
2 CONC io were close in age and became close friends, with the architect spending a lot of time at the villa with his patron. Francesco also influenced further commissions in the area for Palladio through his influence. Palladio had prev
2 CONC iously built the Villa Pisani at Bagnolo di Lonigo for another of the Pisani family, Vettor, son of Giovanni Pisani, Venetian Governer in Vicenza.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Pisani https://sites.google.com/site/thesurnamepisani/history/venice/pisani-properties/villa-pisani-montagnana
