3 CONT
3 CONT Description	
3 CONT English: Reconstructed coat of arms of Theodore Paleologus, 17th-century soldier and assassin. The motive follows (and is a vectorized version of) the arms presented on his tombstone (File:Tombstone_of_Teodoro_Paleologus.png). The
3 CONC  colors are conjectural and follow the speculations in regards to color scheme by John Hall on page 166 of his 2015 book An Elizabethan Assassin: Theodore Paleologus: Seducer, Spy and Killer
3 CONT Date	30 July 2020
