1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yelena_Sheremeteva Yelena Sheremeteva] (c. 1553 – 4 January 1587), was a Russian noblewoman, tsesarevna of Russia as the third wife of Tsarevich Ivan Ivanovich of Russia, son of Ivan 
2 CONC the Terrible.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Yelena Sheremeteva was the daughter of the boyar Ivan Vasilyevich Sheremetev. She was selected to marry the son of the tsar in a Bride-show of daughters from the nobility. Before her marriage to the Tsarevich, his father had consi
2 CONC dered many women as a possible wife for his son, but had found most of them unsuitable for one reason or another. The young Ivan's first and second wives were both thrown into convents on account of their apparent inability to hav
2 CONC e children.
2 CONT
2 CONT In October 1581, Yelena was found to be pregnant. However, on 15 November, the Tsar accused her of supposedly wearing immodest clothing and he began to beat her. Hearing her screams, Yelena's husband hurried to her defense, shouti
2 CONC ng at his father, "You sent my first wife to a convent for no reason, you did the same with my second, and now you strike the third, causing the death of the son she holds in her womb." Subsequently, Yelena did indeed suffer a mis
2 CONC carriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Tsarevich Ivan soon confronted his father on the matter, and a heated argument ensued and only ended when the Tsar struck his son on the head with his staff. The Tsarevich died of his wound on 19 November 1581, leaving Yelena 
2 CONC a widow.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of her spouse, her father-in-law placed her in the Novodevichy Convent. However, unlike her two predecessors, she was not exiled far away from Moscow, but placed in a convent near the court, where she was treated i
2 CONC n accordance to her status as a member of the imperial family.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://historic-times.com/the-fall-of-the-russian-aristocracy-sheremetev-and-golitsyn-stories/
2 CONT https://www.alonereaders.com/article/details/3548/the-murder-of-ivan-the-terribles-heir-a-tragedy-that-shaped-russian-history
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/235687651/elena_ivanovna-sheremeteva
2 CONT
2 CONT Yelena Sheremeteva was a Russian noblewoman, tsarevna of Russia as the third wife of Tsarevich Ivan Ivanovich of Russia, son of Ivan the Terrible
