2 CONT '''Đorđe Nemanjić''' or '''George of Zeta''' (Serbian Cyrillic: Ђорђе Немањић; fl. 1208–1243) was the Grand Prince of Zeta, from at least 1208 until at least 1243. For some time, he also was a self-styled King of Duklja. He was th
2 CONC e son of rival Serbian Grand Prince and titular King Vukan Nemanjić (r. Serbia 1202–1204, Duklja (Zeta) 1190–1208), hence George too was a titular King, for a few years after his father's death. He continued the struggle between h
2 CONC is father and uncle, and accepted the suzerainty of the Republic of Venice. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT /!\ -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONTENEGRO.htm#Vukandied1209
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         DJORDJE (-after 21 Aug 1242).  He succeeded in 1208 as DJORDJE Grand Knez of Zeta on the abdication of his father.  "Rex Georgius et Bladinus frater meus, Stranco et Petrusslao consobrini mei" swore allegiance to "domin
2 CONC o Petro Ziani Venetiarum, Dalmatie atque Croatie duci" by charter dated Jul 1208[151].  Tensions with Serbia continued after his accession and, in order to secure his position, Djordje recognised Venetian suzerainty over Zeta[152]
2 CONC .  His uncle Stefan Grand Župan of Serbia appears to have gained control over Zeta by 1216, putting an end to Zeta's independence[153].  After the succession of Radoslav as king of Serbia in [1224/27], Djordje re-emerged as govern
2 CONC or of Zeta under Radoslav's suzerainty, apparently with the title Prince, although Zeta appears to have reverted to Serbian control after the accession of Stefan Uroš I as King in 1243[154].  After the death od Djordje, the status
2 CONC  of his descendants declined in Zeta:  they were normally referred to with the simple title "Župan", Zeta being granted as an appanage by Stefan Dragutin King of Serbia to his mother Jelena in 1276[155].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Djordje's wife is no known.  Djordje & his wife had [two] children:   
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)        ''' [''' [https://www.geni.com/people/Dmitar-Dimitrijevi%C4%87/6000000026491767231  DIMITRIJE] .  According to Europäische Stammtafeln, he and his brother were sons of one of the two brothers Djordje or Vladin[156].  Žu
2 CONC pan of Zeta [1271]-[1286].  He founded the monastery of Davidovica.  He became a monk in 1286 as DAVID.''']  m''' ---.  The name of Dimitrije's wife is not known.  ''Dmitrije & his wife had one child'':
2 CONT
2 CONT **i)          [https://www.geni.com/people/Vratislav-Vratkovi%C4%87/6000000026491894033 VRATISLAV] .  Knez.  '''m''' ---.  The name of Vratislav's wife is not known.  ''Vratislav & his wife had two children:''
2 CONT
2 CONT ***(a)       [https://www.geni.com/people/Vratko-Dimitrijevi%C4%87/6000000026492110100 VRATKO] [Braktes].  Leader in the battle of Serrhai 1342.  '''m''' ---.  The name of Vratko's wife is not known.  ''Vratko & his wife had [one]
2 CONC  child:''
2 CONT
2 CONT ****(1)       '''[''' [https://www.geni.com/people/Milica-Pribini%C4%87/5122517118000083353 MILICA] (-11 Nov 1405).  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[157], the wife of Knez Lazar was the daughter of Vratoko, but this alleged d
2 CONC escent appears to have been fabricated by later chronicles[158].  Regent of Serbia 1389.  She became a nun as JEVGENIJA[159].  '''m''' ([1353]) LAZAR Hrebeljanović Knez of Serbia, son of PRIBAC Hrebeljanović & his wife --- (Prilje
2 CONC bac, near Novo Brdo [1329]-executed Kosovo 15 Jun 1389, bur Ravanica Monastery).''']''' 
2 CONT ***(b)       RADOSLAV . 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)       '''  ['''STEFAN .  According to Europäische Stammtafeln, he and his brother were sons of one of the two brothers Djordje or Vladin[160].  1252.''']''' 
