2 CONT He was the son of Manuel Erotikos Komnenos, an officer of Emperor Basil II who in 978 defended Nicaea against Bardas Skleros, and one of his two wives, whose names are unknown, and who on his deathbed in 1020 commended his two sur
2 CONC viving sons Isaakios and Ioannes to the emperor's care. Basil had them carefully educated at the monastery of Stoudion, and afterwards advanced them to high official positions. He also had an older son, Nikephoros, who died in 102
2 CONC 6, and a daughter, born in 1012 and married around 1031 to Michael Dokeianos, Captain of Italy, deceased in 1050. It is said that their name was derived from the city of Komne, near Philippopolis, where they were landowners, and t
2 CONC hat they were of Armenian ancestry from Paphlagonia, which is supported by the use of the name Manuel instead of Manolis.
