2 CONT Prof.dr. M. Rebkowski - concluded by his research that Swantopelk I dux Odrensis had sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT a) Wartislaw I (* 1091 - +1135 killed by pagans in the spread of baptism). Under Polish rule he was he regional ruler of Pomerania until his death. He was the founder of the main ducal Pomeranian line.............
2 CONT
2 CONT b) Racibor I (* 1098 - +1156) ... Raciborides branch line .............
2 CONT
2 CONT c) Swantobor II Elder (* 1105- + 1173). In 1122 he resorted to the administration of Piast. When Brother Wartislaw I assumed the administration of Pomerania (as a vassal), he returned to his homeland. His descendants had no ambiti
2 CONC ons for the Ducal See. It is a line of castellan Pomerania. Ritter line Swantoborides - Swantiborides ...............
2 CONT
2 CONT The father of Swantopolk I dux Odrensis was Swantobor (* approx. 1040 - +1107) - a mythical protector of Pomerania. There is a book of legends of Pomerania - "Piesen Swantobora" - published in Poznan, Poland. The Swantiborides (Sw
2 CONC antiboriden) were related to the Griffins, but the link remains unclear. Probably they descend from Swantibor, a Pomeranian duke overthrown in a rebellion and expelled to Poland in 1105/06. This Swantibor might have been a cousin 
2 CONC of Swantopolk, a Pomeranian duke defeated by Boleslaw III of Poland in a campaign of 1111/12. Yet, these assumptions all remain speculative.[5]
2 CONT
