2 CONT Despotate of Epirus 1252-1315During the conflicts between Michael II Komnenos Doukas of Epirus and Emperor John III Doukas Vatatzes, Golem and Theodore Petraliphas, who were initially Michael's allies, defected to John III in 1252
2 CONC .[1][3] He is last mentioned in the sources among other local leaders, in a meeting with George Akropolites in Durrës in 1256.
