2 CONT This family's lands extended from behind Valona towards the north east to Mokro on the western shore of Lake Ohrid[188].  The primary sources which confirm the parentage and marriages of the members of this family have not yet bee
2 CONC n identified, unless otherwise stated below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         '''COMINO Araniti''' .  m ---, daughter of NIKOLA Sakati Lord of Sendir & his wife ---.  Comino & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT *a)         GJERGJ Araniti (-after 1456).  He raised a large rebellion among his own tribesmen against the Ottomans in 1433, which quickly spread throughout Albania from Valona to Skadar and defeated three major Ottoman attacks be
2 CONC tween 1433 and 1436.  The rebellion was finally suppressed in 1436[189].  He was established by Venice as Grand Vojvoda between Skadar and Dürres in 1456, at which time his daughter married the son of Stefan Crnojević, previously 
2 CONC appointed Grand Vojvoda in Zeta[190].  m firstly MARIA Musaki, daughter of ANDREA Musaki & his wife Ana Zenevesi (-before 1444).  A manuscript which records details of the Musaki family notes the marriage of "signor Arainiti Comni
2 CONC no…signor de Cerminica et de Mochino e de Spatennia" and "signora Maria [Musachi]"[191].  m secondly (before 1449) as her second husband, PIETRINA Franco, widow of --- Sarmazza from Corfu, daughter of OLIVIERO Franco Barone di Tau
2 CONC risano & his wife --- (-in Italy after 11 Jul 1489).  The name of Gjergj's wife is not known.  Gjergj & his first wife had nine children:
2 CONT ** ...
2 CONT *b)         COMINO .  m GOJSAVA, daughter of ---. 
2 CONT *c)         VLADEN GOLEM Araniti .  Lord of Biasca and Çermenica.  m ANGJELINA Castriota, daughter of GJON Castrioti & his wife Voisava Tripalda. 
2 CONT *d)         daughter .  m as his first wife, PAL Dukagjin . 
