1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marco_I_Sanudo
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marco Sanudo''' (c. 1153 – between 1220 and 1230, most probably 1227) was the creator and first Duke of the Duchy of the Archipelago, in Italian: '' "Duca del Mare Egeo e Re di Candia", Barone delle Isole di Nasso, Pario, Milo,
2 CONC  Marine ed Andri,'' duchy granted by the Republic of Venice to him and all his descendants, after the Fourth Crusade his lineage became named Sanudo de Candia. .. ...
2 CONT ------
2 CONT - http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/sanudo-marco-i-duca-dell-arcipelago_(Dizionario-Biografico)_ 
2 CONT
2 CONT *''Il suo parente Marino Sanudo Torsello, storico veneziano del XIV secolo, gli attribuisce come padre un altro [https://www.geni.com/people/Marco-Costantinopolitano-de-Sanudo/6000000010031786606 Marco, detto il Costantinopolitano
2 CONC ], ma va ricordato che era contrario alle abitudini veneziane di dare al figlio il nome del padre. 
2 CONT *'''Nel XVI secolo, il genealogista Marco Barbaro lo considera figlio di un Pietro Sanudo, a sua volta figlio di un altro [https://www.geni.com/people/Marco-Costantinopolitano-de-Sanudo/6000000010031786606 Marco]. 
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20LORDSHIPS%20IN%20GREECE.htm#MarcoINaxosdied1227
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.    '''     MARCO Sanudo''' (-1227).  He accompanied his maternal uncle Enrico Dandolo on the Fourth Crusade[746].  After Venice authorised its patricians to acquire territories in Greece, in furtherance of the Acti Partitio Imp
2 CONC erii Romanae of Mar 1204, Marco Sanudo unsuccessfully negotiated with Bonifazio di Monferrato King of Thessaloniki to acquire Crete[747].  He conquered the Cyclades and Dodecanese islands between 1207 and 1211, retaining Naxos for
2 CONC  himself.  Marco refused to acknowledge the suzerainty of Venice, even though the Cyclades islands had been assigned to Venice under the 1204 agreement.  He swore allegiance to Henri Latin Emperor of Constantinople who elevated th
2 CONC e islands into a duchy, installing him as MARCO I Duke of Naxos, or Duke of the Archipelago[748].  He attempted the conquest of Crete in 1212, but after temporarily taking Candia, returned to Naxos.  He also captured Smyrna in 121
2 CONC 3 but was defeated and captured by the fleet of Theodoros Laskaris Emperor in Nikaia[749].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [1213] ) [--- Laskaraina, daughter of --- Laskaris & his wife ---.  According to Miller[750], Theodoros Laskaris Emperor in Nikaia bestowed the hand of his sister on Marco Sanudo after the latter was captured while attem
2 CONC pting to take Smyrna.  He quotes Laurentius de Monachis and several Italian chronicles which do not appear to be contemporary.  According to Sturdza[751], "it is certain" that this marriage did not take place.  It does seem surpri
2 CONC sing that Emperor Theodoros, the main opponent of the Latins, should have arranged the marriage of his sister to one of the newly arrived Latin rulers, assuming that he had any marriageable sisters at all[752].]  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Duke Marco & his wife had two children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
