2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_XIII,_Duke_of_Bavaria Wikipedia] 	
2 CONT *'''Duke of Lower Bavaria:''' Reign 1253–1290
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Otto-II-von-der-Pfalz/6000000003827359914 Otto II] '''Successor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Otto-III-von-Bayern-Duke-of-Lower-Bavaria/294499031220005507 Otto III]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BAVARIA.htm#HeinrichIDukedied1290B
2 CONT
2 CONT '''HEINRICH von Bayern''', son of OTTO II "dem Erlauchten" Duke of Bavaria & his wife Agnes von Braunschweig (Landshut 19 Nov 1235-Burghausen 3 Feb 1290, bur Kloster Seligenthal).  "Otto…Comes Palatini Reni Dux Bawarie" exchanged 
2 CONC property with the abbot of Niederaltaich, naming "Ludovico filio nostro…et Heinrico fratre suo et sororibus suis Elysabet, Sophya et Agnete", by charter dated 17 Oct 1244[502].  The Altahenses Annales record the birth "1235 XIII K
2 CONC al Dec" of "Agnes ducissa Bawarie filium…Heinricus"[503].  He succeeded his father in 1253 as HEINRICH I joint Duke of Bavaria, jointly with his brother Ludwig II.  After joint rule became unworkable, he and his brother agreed a d
2 CONC ivision of the family's territories in 1255, under which Heinrich became Duke of Lower Bavaria (Niederbayern).  "Henricus…dux Bawarie" confirmed the agreement which settled the disputes with his brother by charter dated 5 Sep 1255
2 CONC [504].  He claimed the title Pfalzgraf bei Rhein in Dec 1256, and in 1271 requested Pope Gregory X to confirm his right to an electoral vote.  While there is no evidence about the response he received, Duke Heinrich did act as the
2 CONC  seventh elector in the election of Rudolf von Habsburg as King of Germany in 1273, although his brother Duke Ludwig II registered his non-recognition of his brother's right 29 May 1276[505].  He founded the Cistercian Order near 
2 CONC Passau 1276.  The Notæ Altahenses record the death "1290 III Non Feb" of "Heinricus dux Bawarie"[506].  The necrology of Raitenhaslach records the death "III Non Feb" of "Heinricus dux Bauarie sen"[507].  The necrology of Weltenbu
2 CONC rg records the death "III Non Feb" of "Heinricus dux Babarie"[508].  The necrology of Seligenthal records the death "II Non Feb 1290" of "dominus Heinricus dux Bawarie et com pal Reni ligt bei uns begraben"[509]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (1250) ERSZÉBET of Hungary, daughter of BÉLA IV King of Hungary & his wife Maria Laskarina of Nikaia (1236-24 Oct 1271, bur Kloster Seligenthal).  The Altahenses Annales record the marriage of "Heinricus filius O. ducis Ba
2 CONC varie" and "Elisabeth filia Bele regis Ungarie"[510].  The Altahenses Annales record the death "1271 IX Kal Nov" of "Elizabeth ducissa Bawarie"[511].  The necrology of Tegernsee records the death "IX Kal Nov" of "Elysabeth ducissa
2 CONC  Bawarie filia regis Ungarie"[512].  The necrology of Windberg records the death "IX Kal Nov 1271" of "Elysabet ducissa Bawarie"[513].  The necrology of Seligenthal records the death "IX Kal Nov 1271" of "domina Elizabet filia reg
2 CONC is Ungarie ducissa Bawarie"[514]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Duke Heinrich & his wife had ten children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/wittel/wittel1.html
2 CONT
2 CONT =Wittelsbach=
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Otto I von Scheyern, +4.12.1072/1078; 1m: Haziga von Diessen; 2m: Hadagunda von Scheyern (dau.of N by a dau.of Hartwig II Pfgf of Bavaria); He had issue:
2 CONT * ...
2 CONT *A3. [2m.] Gf Ekkehart I von Scheyern, +by 1088/before 11.5.1094; m.Richgard of Carniola, dau.of Ulrich von Weimar-Orlamünde
2 CONT ** ...
2 CONT **B2. Gf Otto I von Scheyern, Gf von Wittelsbach 1115, Pfgf of Bavaria (1110-20), +1123, bur Indersdorf; m.N, a dau.of Eberhard von Ratzenhofen
2 CONT ***C1. Otto II, Gf von Wittelsbach, Pfgf in Bayern 1121, +4.8.1156, bur Ensdorf; m.Heilika von Lengenfeld-Hopfenohe-Pettendorf (+1170, bur Ensdorf)
2 CONT ****D1. Otto I "der Grosse", Duke of Bavaria (16.9.1180-1183), *Kehlheim (?) ca 1117, +Pfullendorf in Baden 11.7.1183, bur Scheyern; m.Agnes von Looz (*ca 1150 +1191)
2 CONT ***** ...
2 CONT *****E3. Duke Ludwig I of Bavaria (1183-1231), Pfgf bei Rhein (1214-31), *Kelheim 23.12.1173, +murdered on the Kelheimer Bridge 15.9.1231, bur Scheyern; m.1204 Ludmila of Bohemia (*ca 1170 +4.8.1240)
2 CONT ******F1. Duke Otto II "der Erlauchte" Bavaria (1231-53), Pfgf (1227-53), *Kelheim 7.4.1206, +Landshut 29.11.1253, bur Scheyern; m.Worms 1222 Pfgfn Agnes bei Rhein (*after 1201 +1267)
2 CONT *******G1. Duke Ludwig II "der Strenge" of Upper Bavaria (1253-94), Pfgf bei Rhein (1253-94), *Heidelberg 13.4.1229, +there 2.2.1294, bur Fürstenfeld; 1m: 1254 Maria of Brabant (*1226 +beheaded at Donauwörth 1256, bur there); 2m: 
2 CONC 1260 Anna of Glogau (*1250/52, +1271, bur Fürstenfeld); 3m: Aachen 24/27.10.1273 Mechtild von Habsburg (*1251/53 +23.12.1304, bur Fürstenfeld)
2 CONT ******** ...
2 CONT *******G2. '''Duke Heinrich XIII of Lower Bavaria (1253-90), *Landshut 19.11.1235, +Burghausen 3.2.1290, bur Seligenthal'''; m.1244/50 Elisabeth of Hungary (*1236 +24.10.1271)
2 CONT ********H1. Duke Otto III of Lower Bavaria (1290-1312), King of Hungary (1305-07) as Béla III -cr 5.12.1305, *Burghausen 11.2.1261, +Landshut 9.9.1312, bur Seligenthal; 1m: Vienna 1279 Katharina von Habsburg (*1256 +4.4.1282); 2m:
2 CONC  Straubing II.1308 Agnes von Glogau (*1293/96 +25.12.1361 bur Seligenthal)
2 CONT ********* ...
2 CONT ********H2. Heinrich, *23.2.1262, +16.9.1280, bur Seligenthal
2 CONT ********H3. Duke Ludwig III of Lower Bavaria (1290-96), *9.10.1269, +Landshut 13.5.1296, bur Seligenthal
2 CONT ********H4. Duke Stephan I of Lower Bavaria (1290-1310), *14.3.1271, +of the plague at Landshut 21.12.1310, bur Seligenthal; m.1299 Jutta of Schweidnitz (*1285/7 +Landshut 15.9.1320, bur Seligenthal)
2 CONT ********* ...
2 CONT ********H5. Agnes, *I.1254, +Kloster Seligenthal 20.10.1315, bur there
2 CONT ********H6. Agnes, *17.7.1255, +10.5.1260, bur Seligenthal
2 CONT ********H7. Agnes, *29.10.1256, +Landshut 16.11.1260, bur Seligenthal
2 CONT ********H8. Elisabeth, a nun at Seilgenthal, *23.4.1258, +there 8.8.1314, bur there
2 CONT ********H9. Sophie, *ca 1264, +4.2.1282, bur Kloster Vessera bei Erfurt; m.Landshut 1277 Gf Poppo VIII von Henneberg (+1282)
2 CONT ********H10. Katharina, *9.6.1267, +Seilgenthal 9.1.1310, bur there; m.Mgve Friedrich of Meissen-Landsberg (+1291)
2 CONT
