2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00079792&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Ida er av ukjent herkomst ifølge «Våre forfedre» av Mogens Bugge. Hun døde på et korstog i 1101.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilder: Mogens Bugge: Våre forfedre, se nr. 190. Bent og Vidar Billing Hansen: Rosensverdslektens forfedre, side 23. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ida of Austria (c.1055 – September 1101), daughter of Rapoto IV of Cham, also known as Itha, was the wife of Leopold II of Austria, and the mother of Leopold III. She was known as one of the great beauties of her day.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ida joined the Crusade of 1101, and in September of that year was among those ambushed at Heraclea Cybistra by the sultan Kilij Arslan I. Ekkehard of Aura reports that Ida was killed in the fighting, but rumors persisted that she 
2 CONC survived, and was carried off to a harem. Later legends claimed that she was the mother of the Muslim hero Zengi, but this is quite impossible on chronological grounds.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ida of Austria (c.1055 – September 1101), daughter of Rapoto IV of Cham, also known as Itha, was the wife of Leopold II of Austria, and the mother of Leopold III. She was known as one of the great beauties of her day.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ida joined the Crusade of 1101, and in September of that year was among those ambushed at Heraclea Cybistra by the sultan Kilij Arslan I. Ekkehard of Aura reports that Ida was killed in the fighting, but rumors persisted that she 
2 CONC survived, and was carried off to a harem. Later legends claimed that she was the mother of the Muslim hero Zengi, but this is quite impossible on chronological grounds.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ida_of_Formbach-Ratelnberg
