2 CONT Władysław II the Exile, (Polish: Władysław II Wygnaniec; Kraków, Kingdom of Poland, 1105 – May 30, 1159, Altenburg, Holy Roman Empire) was High Duke of Poland, 1138-1146. He was the son of Bolesław III Wrymouth, Duke of Poland, an
2 CONC d Zbyslava, daughter of Sviatopolk II of Kiev.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1125 Władysław married Agnes of Babenberg, granddaughter of Emperor Henry IV. They had three sons: Bolesław I the Tall, Duke of Silesia; Mieszko I Tanglefoot, Duke of Opole; Konrad I of Głogów and a daughter, Richeza of Poland,
2 CONC  who married Alfonso VII, King of Castile and León.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the death of his father, Bolesław III Wrymouth, Władysław II, as his eldest son, became High Duke of Poland. He controlled the high-ducal provinces of Kraków and Gniezno and also his hereditary province of Silesia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1145 he attempted to take control of the country. In 1146 he accepted overlordship by the emperor and became founder of the Silesian Piasts. He was banned by the bishop of Gniezno and mutilated the voivode, the Danish castellan
2 CONC  Peter Wlast (Polish: Piotr Włostowic). Władysław was driven into exile in 1146 by his younger brothers, and in 1159 he died at the Altenburg Kaiserpfalz of Emperor Frederick I Barbarossa.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1163 the province of Silesia was granted to Władysław's sons by Poland's Duke Bolesław IV the Curly. Subsequently Silesia was divided into as many as 17 separate duchies among Władysław's descendants and successors, until the S
2 CONC ilesian Piasts died out with George IV William of Legnica in 1675.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Wladislaw II, Duke of Poland (1) M, #113328, b. 1105, d. 1159 Last Edited=30 Jul 2005 Consanguinity Index=2.34%
2 CONT      Wladislaw II, Duke of Poland was born in 1105. (3) He was the son of Boleslaw III, Duke of Poland and Zbyslawa of Kiev. (2) He married Agnes Babenberg, daughter of Leopold III 'the Saint' Markgraf von Österreich and Agnes Sal
2 CONC ian, between 1125 and 1127. (3)  He died in 1159. (3)
2 CONT      Wladislaw II, Duke of Poland was a member of the House of Piast. (4) Wladislaw II, Duke of Poland also went by the nick-name of Wladislaw 'the Exile' (?). (4) He gained the title of Duke of Silesia in 1138. He gained the titl
2 CONC e of Duke of Cracow in 1138. (2) He gained the title of Duke of Poland in 1140. (1) He was deposed as Duke of Cracow and Silesia in 1146. (2) Child of Wladislaw II, Duke of Poland -1. unknown (?)+ (4)
2 CONT
