2 CONT Władysław II the Exile, (Polish: Władysław II Wygnaniec; 1105 – 30 May 1159) was a High Duke of Poland and Duke of Silesia from 1138 until 1146.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the eldest son of Bolesław III Wrymouth by his first wife Zbyslava, daughter of Sviatopolk II of Kiev. Life Governor of Silesia
2 CONT
