1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William IV (c. 1030 – 1100) was the Margrave of Montferrat from 1084.
2 CONT
2 CONT The date of William's birth is unknown, but it probably took place between 1030 and 1035. He was the eldest son of Otto II and Constance, daughter of Amadeus II of Savoy. He first appears in a document of 1059, when he is placed i
2 CONC n power over the city of Savona, probably as per a request of the citizenry for a ruler of their own.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1093, he was present when the Emperor Henry IV donated the monastery of Breme to the church of Pavia.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his second marriage with Otta di Aglié, William was the father of his successor Rainier. He had two children by his first marriage, but their fate is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_IV_of_Montferrat
