2 CONT Guilliaume l. le Grand oder Guillaume l. Tête Hardie war graf von Burgund und Mâcon. Er war der Sohn von Graf Rainald l. aus den Haus Burgund-Ivera und Adelheid von Normandie aus dem Haus der Rolloniden.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT William I (1020 – 12 November 1087), called the Great (le Grand or Tête Hardie, "the Stubborn"), was Count of Burgundy from 1057 to 1087 and Mâcon from 1078 to 1087. He was a son of Renaud I and Alice of Normandy, daughter of Rich
2 CONC ard II, Duke of Normandy. William was the father of several notable children, including Pope Callixtus II.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1057, he succeeded his father and reigned over a territory larger than that of the Franche-Comté itself. In 1087, he died in Besançon, Prince-Archbishopric of Besançon, Holy Roman Empire -- an independent city within the County
2 CONC  of Burgundy. He was buried in Besançon's Cathedral of St John.
2 CONT
2 CONT William married a woman named Stephanie before 1087.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Stephanie:
2 CONT
2 CONT Renaud II, William's successor, died on First Crusade Stephen I, successor to Renaud II, Stephen died on the Crusade of 1101 Raymond of Burgundy who married Urraca of León and Castile and thus inherited the government of Galicia (
2 CONC Spain) (died 1107) Sybilla (or Maud), married (1080) Eudes I of Burgundy Gisela of Burgundy, married (1090) Humbert II of Savoy and then Renier I of Montferrat Clementia married Robert II, Count of Flanders and was Regent, during 
2 CONC his absence. She married secondly Godfrey I, Count of Leuven and was possibly the mother of Joscelin of Louvain. William married a woman named Etiennette de Longuy circa 1040
2 CONT
2 CONT Other children of either Stephanie or Etiennette:
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy of Vienne, elected pope, in 1119 at the Abbey of Cluny, as Calixtus II William Eudes Hugh III, Archbishop of Besançon Stephanie married Lambert, Prince de Royans (died 1119) Ermentrude, married (1065) Theodoric I (perhaps) Ber
2 CONC tha wife of Alphonso VI of Castile and maybe another daughter
