1 NOTE William I, Count of Burgundy
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=image&guid=fec289b6-9b6f-4f26-921e-5901bc2d08ae&tid=5698773&pid=-1248752716
1 NOTE William I (1020 - 1087), called the Great (le Grand or Tête Hardie, "the Rash") was Count of Burgundy and Mâcon from 1057 to 1087. He was a son of Renaud I and Adelaide, daughter of Richard II of Normandy. William was the father
2 CONC  of several notable children, including Pope Callistus II.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1057, he succeeded his father and reigned over a territory larger than that of the Franche-Comté itself. In 1087, he died in Besançon and was buried there in the cathedral of St John.
2 CONT
2 CONT William married a woman named Stephanie.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had many children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Renaud II, William's successor, died on First Crusade 
2 CONT Stephen I, successor to Renaud II, Stephen died on the Crusade of 1101 
2 CONT Raymond, married (1090) Urraca, the reigning queen of Castile 
2 CONT Guy of Vienne, elected pope, in 1119 at the Abbey of Cluny. as Calixtus II 
2 CONT Sybilla (or Maud), married (1080) Eudes I of Burgundy 
2 CONT Gisela of Burgundy, married (1090) Humbert II of Savoy and then Renier I of Montferrat 
2 CONT Adelaide 
2 CONT Eudes 
2 CONT Hugh III, Archbishop of Besançon 
2 CONT Clementia married Robert II, Count of Flanders and was Regent, during his absence 
2 CONT Stephanie married Lambert, Prince de Royans (d.1119) 
2 CONT Ermentrude, married (1065) Theodoric I 
2 CONT (perhaps) Bertha wife of Alphonso VI of Castile 
