1 NOTE     DE VAJAY,ANNALES DE BOURGOGNE,XXXII 1960 P.247-;BOUCHARD P.273
1 NOTE PARENTS: De Vajay, in Annales de Bourgogne vol. 32 (1960) pp
2 CONT 258-261
2 CONT identifies Stephanie as dau of Clemence de Foix and Albert de
2 CONT Longwy.
2 CONT Moriarty, The Plantagenet Ancestry, disagrees. Garnier, Tableaux
2 CONT Genealogiques
2 CONT des Souverains de France et de ses Grand Feudataires (Table
2 CONT XXVIII) shows her
2 CONT as dau of Raymond II, Count of Barcelona.
1 NOTE
2 CONT Stephanie de Longwy-Metz of Barcelona AKA "Etiennette" was born circa1035 in Longwy, Meurthe-et-Moselle, France. She died circa 1089 or June30 1109.
2 CONT
2 CONT The sources about her parents conflict. In a number of references herparents are listed as:
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Adalbert de Longwy-Metz III, Count of Longwy and Duke of UpperLorraine was born circa 995 in Longwy, Lorraine région, France. He died1048 in Slain at Thuim. Adalbert married Clemence de Foix.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Clemence de Foix was born circa 1010 in Carcassonne, Audedépartement, Languedoc-Roussillon région, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many others say her parents are:
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Raimund Berenger II, Count of Barcelona
2 CONT Mother: Almodede
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT www.dcs.hull.ac.uk/cgi-bin/gedlkup/n=royal?royal12266
1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT 13 children?
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
1 NOTE     DE VAJAY,ANNALES DE BOURGOGNE,XXXII 1960 P.247-;BOUCHARD P.273
1 NOTE RBS:  Etiennette de Barcelona was per new research, probably not the daughter of Adalbert of Longwy, but having instead a kinship (but not too close) to the Counts of Barcelona. cf. Todd A. Farmerie (e-mail address), Etiennette of
2 CONC  Longwy - NOT!!!! In "Etiennette of Longwy - NOT!!!!", newsgroup message to soc.genealogy.medieval, 2001-04-25
1 NOTE
2 CONT from &quot;Our Folk&quot; by Albert D Hart, Jr.
1 NOTE Ancestral File Number:<AFN> 9HM0-SF
2 CONT Despite many sources that indicate this pedigree including Stephanie/Etienette's mother and father, her mother did not exist, and her father may not have married or had children.  Clemence de Foix was "calculated to have existed" 
2 CONC based on certain evidence which proved false.  Some people think that Stephanie/Etienette was Ettienette, daughter of one of the Ramon Berenger, Counts of Barcelona.  I am leaving the pedigree in place for these three people until
2 CONC  more information is available.
2 CONT ##check ancestry
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestral File Number:<AFN> 9HM0-SF
