1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===== Not the wife of https://www.geni.com/people/Guy-de-Baug%C3%A9/6000000003827826486  (son of Ulric); or of https://www.geni.com/people/Guy-II-de-Baugé/6000000009479193350 (son of Renaud).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beatrice_of_Montferrat
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice of Montferrat (c.1210 – 1274) was an Italian noblewoman, the eldest daughter of William VI, Marquess of Montferrat, and the third wife of Guigues VI of Viennois, by whom she had two sons.[citation needed]. Beatrice died o
2 CONC n an unrecorded date in 1274.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice was immortalised as the domna of the troubadour Gauseran de Saint-Leidier, who extolled his idealised and unconsummated love for Beatrice in his cansos, of which only two are extant.
2 CONT
2 CONT   Marriages and issue
2 CONT On 21 November[citation needed] 1219, at the age of about nine (or possibly younger), Beatrice married Guigues VI of Viennois. Their marriage was recorded in Aymari Rivalli De Allobrogibus.[citation needed] He was over twenty year
2 CONC s her senior and she was his third wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1228 until Guigues' death in 1237, as his wife, she was the Dauphine consort of Viennois as well as the Countess of Albon, Briançon, Grenoble and Oisans. Together they had two sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Guigues VII of Viennois (1225–1269), married Beatrice of Savoy, by whom he had issue
2 CONT *John of Viennois (1227–1239)
2 CONT
2 CONT When her husband died in 1237, she help guide their eldest son during his early years as Dauphin.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disproved husband 
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondo alcuni cronisti, Beatrice dopo essere rimasta vedova si sposò in seconde nozze con Guido II, Signore di Bâgé, ma secondo ''la Histoire généalogique de la royale maison de Savoie'' è una errata interpretazione di un documen
2 CONC to dove Beatrice viene citata, come Delfina ''(Beatrix de Montferrat veuve du Daufin André)''[11].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Many secondary sources state that Beatrice married, as her second husband, Guy [II] Seigneur de Bâgé (see BURGUNDY DUCHY NOBILITY).''' Guichenon, in his Histoire de Savoie, explains the background to this error, recording that 
2 CONC "Pingon, du Buttet, du Chesne et les sainte Marthe…moi après eux" confused the name "Dauphine", under which Guy´s widow is recorded with the title "Dauphine [de Viennois]"[198], the widow of André Comte d´Albon being the only avai
2 CONC lable person with that title. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT - http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONFERRATO,%20SALUZZO,%20SAVONA.htm#BeatriceMonferratodied1274
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         BEATRICE di Monferrato ([1204/10][195]-after Mar 1276).  The Aymari Rivalli De Allobrogibus records the marriage of "Andreas Delphinus" and "Beatricem, Guillermi marchionis Montisferrati filiam" after repudiating his fi
2 CONC rst wife[196].  The testament of "Dom. Andreas Dalphinus Viennensis et Albonis comitis" is dated 4 Mar 1236, names as his heir "Guigonem filium suum", and appoints "Beatricem uxorem suam comitissam matris eiusdem Guigonis" as his 
2 CONC tutor[197].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (21 Nov 1219) as his third wife, ANDRE de Bourgogne Comte de Gap et d'Embrun, son of HUGUES III Duke of Burgundy [Capet] & his second wife Béatrix de Viennois (1184-14 Mar 1237, bur Grenoble, église collégiale de Saint-And
2 CONC ré).  He succeeded his mother in 1228 as Comte d'Albon, Dauphin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkvien.htm#GuiguesVIdied1237 
2 CONT
2 CONT   André & his third wife had [two] children:
2 CONT *3.         GUIGUES de Viennois (1225-Aug 1269, bur Chartreuse Abbaye de Prémol). … Betrothed (contract [Jan/May] 1240) to CECILE des Baux, daughter of BARRAL Seigneur de Baux & his wife Béatrice d'Anduze (-21 May 1275).  … Betrot
2 CONC hed (contract before Jun 1240, annulled Jun 1240) to SANCHA de Provence, daughter of RAYMOND BERENGER IV Comte de Provence & his wife Beatrix de Savoie (Aix-en-Provence [1225]-Berkhamstead Castle, Buckinghamshire 5 or 9 Nov 1261, 
2 CONC bur Hayles Abbey, Gloucestershire).  … m (Betrothed 3 Dec 1241, [before 22 Apr 1253]) as her first husband, BEATRIX de Savoie Dame de Faucigny, daughter and heiress of PIERRE Comte de Savoie, Duc de Chablais & his wife Agnès Dame 
2 CONC de Faucigny 
2 CONT *4.          [JEAN de Viennois (1227-1239).  Ludovico della Chiesa’s Histoire de Piedmont names "Guigo quarto et Gioanni mori intorno al 1239" as the sons of André Comte d’Albon and his wife Beatrice di Monferrato[348].  The prima
2 CONC ry source on which this information is not cited, and has not yet been identified.  It is not known how accurate this information might be, but until more definite corroboration comes to light, Jean is included here in square brac
2 CONC kets.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
