2 CONT 3.         GIACOMO di Sanseverino .  It is possible that this was the same person as Giacopo di Tricarico who is named above, but the primary source which confirms that this is correct has not yet been identified.  Conte di Tricar
2 CONC ico.  The Ryccardus de Sancti Germano Chronica records that "comes Gualterius" [Gauthier [III] de Brienne] allied himself with "Iacobo Tricaricensi et comite Roggerio de Theate" in 1204[133].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (after Jun 1205) as her second husband, ELVIRA [Albinia] of Sicily, widow of GAUTHIER [III] Comte de Brienne, daughter of TANCRED King of Sicily & his wife Sibilla --- (-after 1216).  The Thomas Tusci Gesta Imperatorum et 
2 CONC Pontificum names (in order) "Alberia, Constantia et Madania" as the three daughters of "Tancredus [rex Siciliæ]" & his wife, naming the first husband of "Alberia vel Alceria" as "comes Gualterius de Brenna, frater regis", her seco
2 CONC nd husband as "Iacobo comiti de Tricario", and her third husband "comiti Tigrino palatino comiti in Tuscia", specifying that her third marriage was arranged by "papa Honorius" and that her dowry was "comitatum Licie et Montis Isca
2 CONC liosi in regno Apulie"[134].  Giacomo & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         SIMON di Sanseverino .  The Thomas Tusci Gesta Imperatorum et Pontificum names "comytem Symonem et dominam Adalitam" as the children of "Iacobo comiti de Tricario" & his wife[135].  [The Ryccardus de Sancti Germano Chr
2 CONC onica records that "Roggerium de Aquila, Thomam de Caserta, Iacobum de Sancto Severino, et filium comitis Tricaricensis, regni comites" rebelled against Emperor Friedrich II in Sicily in 1223[136].  It is not known whether "filium
2 CONC  comitis Tricaricensis" refers to Simon or to another unidentified son of the conte di Tricarico.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         ADALITA di Sanseverino .  The Thomas Tusci Gesta Imperatorum et Pontificum names "comytem Symonem et dominam Adalitam" as the children of "Iacobo comiti de Tricario" & his wife[137]. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CENTRAL%20ITALY.htm#MobiliaCeccanoMGiacopoTriarico
2 CONT
2 CONT *7.         LANDOLFO (-16 May 1182).  The Annales Ceccanenses record the death "1182 17 Kal Iun" of "Landalfus comes Ceccani"[476]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT **a)         sons .  The Annales Ceccanenses record that in Nov 1182 "filii Landulfi de Ceccano" handed over the castle to Pope Lucio[477]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT **b)         MABILIA .  The Annales Ceccanenses record the marriage "1188 8 Id Nov" of "Mobilia filia Landulfi de Ceccano" and "comiti Iacobo de Triearico"[478].  '''m (6 Nov 1188) GIACOPO di Triarico, son of ---.''' 
2 CONT
