2 CONT
2 CONT Henry I of Brabant (in French: Henri I de Brabant; in Dutch: Hendrik I van Brabant), was nicknamed "The Courageous." He became Duke of Brabant in 1183/1184 and succeeded his father as Duke of Lower Lotharingia in 1190.
2 CONT
2 CONT Under Henry I, there was a town policy and town planning. Henry's attention went out to those regions that lent themselves to the extension of his sovereignty and in some locations he used the creation of a new town as an instrume
2 CONC nt in the political organization of the area.
2 CONT
2 CONT See http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_I,_Duke_of_Brabant for more information.
