4 CONC  wars. She supported Edward's turn to the Lusignans in 1258, and was abroad with him between 1260 and 1263. When he returned from France in February 1263, mercenaries whom Eleanor obtained from Ponthieu were among the troops he in
4 CONC stalled in Windsor Castle. Contrary to general belief, she did not leave England during the crisis. She lived at Windsor after the battle of Lewes, when ordered her to join him (17 June 1264), probably at Montfort's wishes as it w
