2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry's duchies Saxony and Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry had the following known children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * by his first wife, Clementia (divorced 1162), daughter of Conrad, Duke of Zähringen and Clemence of Namur:
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Gertrude of Bavaria (1155-1197), married first Frederick IV, Duke of Swabia, and then King Canute VI of Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Richenza (c. 1157 - 1167)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * by his second wife, Matilda, daughter of King Henry II of England (married 1168):
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Matilda (1171-1210), married Godfrey, Count of Perche, and Enguerrand III, Lord of Coucy
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Richenza (1172-1204), was engaged to King Valdemar II of Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Henry V, Count Palatine of the Rhine (c. 1173-1227)
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Lothar of Bavaria (c. 1174-1190)
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Otto IV, Holy Roman Emperor and Duke of Swabia (c. 1175-1218)
2 CONT
2 CONT           o William of Winchester (1184-1213)
2 CONT
2 CONT Three other children are listed, by some sources, as having belonged to Henry and Matilda;
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Eleanor (born 1178); died young
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Ingibiorg (born 1180); died young
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Infant Son (b.&d. 1182)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * by his lover, Ida of Blieskastel:
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Matilda, married Henry Borwin I, Prince of Mecklenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Benjamin Arnold, "Henry the Lion and His Time", Journal of Medieval History, vol. 22, pp. 379-393 (1996)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Karl Jordan, Henry the Lion. A Biography, ISBN 0-19-821969-5
2 CONT
