2 CONT
2 CONT BOLESŁAW of Poland, son of WŁADYSŁAW I HERMAN Prince of Poland & his second wife Judith of Bohemia (20 Aug [1086]-28 Oct 1138).  The Chronicæ Polanorum names "Bolezlavum" as son of King Władysław and his wife "filiam Wratislavi Bo
2 CONC hemici regis"[200].  The Annales Capituli Cracoviensis record the birth in 1086 of "Bolezlaus tertius" followed immediately by the death of "Iudith mater sua"[201].  He succeeded his father in 1102 as BOLESŁAW III "Krzywousty/Wrym
2 CONC outh" Prince of Poland.  The Annales Cracovienses Compilati record that "Boleslaus duos Pomeranos duces devicit aput Nakel.  Iste tercius Boleslaus terras obtinuit"[202].  Duke of Pomerania 1122-1138.  Before his death Bolesław II
2 CONC I arranged a division of his lands among his sons.  The Annales Capituli Cracoviensis record the death "1138 V Kal Nov" of "dux Bolezlaus tercius"[203]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ([16 Nov 1102/1103]) ZBISLAVA Sviatopolkovna, daughter of SVIATOPOLK II Iziaslavich Grand Prince of Kiev & his first wife --- (-[1109/12]).  The Primary Chronicle names Sbyslava daughter of Svyatopolk when recording that
2 CONC  she was taken to Poland 16 Nov 1102 to marry Boleslav[204].  The Chronica principum Polonie records that the mother of "Boleslaus suo primogenito Wladislao filio" was "ex  quadam Ruthena nobili"[205].  The Annales Cracovienses Ve
2 CONC tusti record the marriage in 1103 of "Bolezlaus tercius"[206].  The Annales Kamenzenses record the marriage in 1104 of "Bolezlaus tercius" and "uxorem Rutenam"[207]. 
2 CONT
