2 CONT d)         ALIX de Châtillon (-1235 or after).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Aleydem [uxor] marchionis Eystensis in Italia" as third of the three daughters of "Raynaldus de Castellione uxor…relictam principis
2 CONC  Raymundi"[709], although it is chronologically unlikely that Alix could have been the daughter of Renaud by his first wife who died [1163/67].  Pope Innocent III confirmed his protection of "nobili mulieri Aliz, filiæ quondam pri
2 CONC ncipis Rainaldi" by charter dated 16 Jun 1198[710].  A charter dated 22 Feb 1204 records the marriage contract for "dominus Azo Estensis marchio" and "domina Aliz filia quondam Rainaldi principis Antiocheni"[711].  The testament o
2 CONC f "dominus Azzo Estensis marchio", dated 18 Nov 1212, bequeathes property to "filie sue domine Beatrici…Aldeurandinum et Azzolinum novellum filios", a codicil naming "uxori mee domine Ailisii…filie mee Constantie"[712].  "Domini A
2 CONC zoni Estensis Marchionis" donated property to the monastery of Santa Maria at Carceres, with the consent of "Domina Adelice sua matre", by charter dated 1235[713].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (22 Feb 1204) as his second wife, AZZO VI "Azzolino" d'Este, son of AZZO V d'Este & his wife --- ([1170]-Nov 1212, bur Vangadizza monastery).    
