2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         [--- ([1095/1105]-).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines records that "principe Antiochie Renaldo" had a sister who was the mother of "Renaldum de Monte Falconis in Bituria et duas sorores illius"[681].  Dame d
2 CONC e Crépy et de Nanteuil-le-Haudoin.  Her birth date range, which is very approximate, is estimated based on the probable birth date range of her daughter.  As will be observed, this means that she was very much older than her suppo
2 CONC sed brother Renaud de Châtillon.  This suggests that, if they were brother and sister, they were born from different marriages of their father.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' --- de Monfaucon [en Berri], son of ---.] 
