1 NOTE Peter Asen of Eastern Bulgaria was killed by dissident nobles in 1196.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter II Asen regained the 2nd Kingdom of Bulgaria from Isaac II Angelus of the Eastern Roman Empire in 1186.  Peter II and his brother John (Ivan) were of the Boyar (noble) family of Asen.  They re-established the Bulgarian (free
2 CONC ) state and established the Second Bulgarian Kingdom.
2 CONT The Magyar, Serbian and Norman armies all attacked Byzantium, and conquered Sofia.  Then the northern Bulgarians rose up against the Buyzantine, and were assisted by the Blachs and cumans, and the Bulgarians succeed in liberating 
2 CONC their country.  In 1187 a peace treaty was signed between Bulgaria and the Byzantine, and Bugaria was again independent.  Peter ruled the eastern provinces of Bulgaria, with his capital at Preslav.  He was killed by a dissident no
2 CONC ble in 1196. and succeeded by his younger brother Kaloyan.
