1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Medlands (13 Feb 2024): [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HOLLAND.htm#FlorisVdied1296 Holland]
2 CONT * '''FLORIS''' (Jul 1254-murdered Utrecht 27 Jun 1296, bur Rijnsburg Monastery). The ''Chronologia Johannes de Bek''e names "''Florencium''" as son of Count Willem & his wife[584]. The ''Cronica Principum Saxonie'' names "''Floren
2 CONC cium comitem Hollandie''" as the son of "''Wilhelmus de Hollandia rex''" & his wife[585]. He succeeded his father in 1256 as '''FLORIS V Count of Holland'''. He was a claimant to the throne of Scotland in 1291, through his great-g
2 CONC randmother, first in order on the Great Roll of Scotland. The ''Chronologia Johannes de Beke'' records the murder "''Traiectum…1296 V Kal Iul''" of Count Floris by "''Gerardus de Velsen''" and his burial in Rijnsburg monastery[586
2 CONC ]. 
2 CONT * '''m''' ( [1270] ) '''BEATRIX de Flandre''', daughter of GUY Count of Flanders & his first wife Mathilde de Béthune (1260-23 Mar 1296). The ''Genealogia Comitum Flandriæ'' refers to the three (unnamed) daughters of "''Guido…ex M
2 CONC athilde filia Roberti Tenremontensis''", specifying that one (listed second) married "''Florentie comiti Hollandie''"[587]. The ''Chronologia Johannes de Beke'' records the marriage of Count Floris and "''Beatricem filiam Guidonis
2 CONC  Flandrensis comitis''"[588]. The ''Chronologia Johannes de Beke'' records the death "''1296 X Kal Aug''" of "''Beatricem conthoralem suam''"[589]. Count Floris V & his wife had eleven children:…
2 CONT ** a) '''DIRK''' (-young). “The Chronologia Johannes de Beke names (in order) "Theodricum, Florencium, Wilhelmum, Ottonem, Wilhelmum, Florencium et Iohannem Hollandie comitem, Beatricem, Machtildim, Elizabeth et Margaretam Anglie 
2 CONC reginam" as children of Count Floris & his wife"[''Chronologia Johannes de Beke'' 74e, p. 227.].
2 CONT ** b) '''FLORIS''' (-young). Ditto.
2 CONT ** c) '''WILLEM''' (-young). Ditto.
2 CONT ** d) '''OTTO''' (-young). Ditto.
2 CONT ** e) '''WILLEM''' (-young). Ditto.
2 CONT ** f) '''FLORIS''' (-young). Ditto.
2 CONT ** g) '''BEATRIX''' (-young). Ditto.
2 CONT ** h) '''MECHTILD''' (-young). Ditto.
2 CONT ** i) '''ELISABETH''' (-young). Ditto.
2 CONT ** j) '''MARGARETA''' (-after 12 Aug 1284). The ''Chronologia Johannes de Beke'' names (in order) "''Theodricum, Florencium, Wilhelmum, Ottonem, Wilhelmum, Florencium et Iohannem Hollandie comitem, Beatricem, Machtildim, Elizabeth
2 CONC  et Margaretam Anglie reginam''" as children of Count Floris & his wife[599], the reference to “''Anglie reginam''” being explained by her betrothal. Floris V Count of Holland betrothed "''Margaretam filiam nostram''" to “''domino
2 CONC  Edwardo...regi Anglie...domino Alfonso eius filio''” by charter dated 5 Jul 1281[600]. Floris V Count of Holland agreed the dowry for the marriage of "''Edwardi regis Anglorum...dominum Alfonsum dicti domini regis primogenitum''"
2 CONC  and “''Margaretam filiam nostram''” by charter dated 12 Aug 1283, which also provides for the marriage between “''Johannis filii nostri''” and “''eius filiam''”[601]. '''Betrothed''' (5 Jul 1281) to '''ALFONSO of England''', son 
2 CONC of EDWARD I King of England & his first wife Infanta doña Leonor de Castilla (Bayonne or Bordeaux or in Maine 24 Nov 1275-Windsor Castle 19 Aug 1284, bur Westminster Abbey). 
2 CONT ** k) '''JAN.''' (before 12 Aug 1283-Haarlem 10 Nov 1299). &c….
2 CONT * '''Count Floris V had [seven] illegitimate children by unknown mistresses:'''
2 CONT ** l) '''WITTE''' ([1280/82]-[6 Jan/26 Dec] 1321). &c….
2 CONT ** m) '''CATHARINA bastaarde van Holland''' (-after 12 Aug 1328). &c….
2 CONT ** n) '''GERHARD''' (-before 28 Jul 1327). [No source cited.]
2 CONT ** o) '''WILLEM''' [No source cited.]
