0 @N6000000002187757189@ NOTE Margaret of Hungary
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Margaret (Margit) (1175 – 1223), was the eldest daughter of King Bela III of Hungary and his second wife Agnes of Antioch. Her maternal grandparents were Raynald of Chatillon and Constance of Antioch.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1185, Margaret married the Eastern Roman Emperor Isaac II Angelos. They had two sons:
1 CONT
1 CONT John (Ioannes) Angelos. 
1 CONT Manuel Angelos. 
1 CONT Her husband died in February, 1204. Later that year the widowed Margaret married Boniface of Montferrat, who was soon to become king of Thessalonica. To Boniface she bore a son Demetrius in 1207. In the same year, on his father's 
1 CONC death, Demetrius became king of Thessalonica.
