0 @N6000000002187891824@ NOTE Stefan Prvovencani
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Stefan Prvovencani (lit. meaning: Stephen the first-crowned) or Stefan II, Nemanja (?????? ???????????, ?????? II, ??????) (d. September 24, 1228) was the ruler of the Serbian state of Raška who managed to promote it to the status
1 CONC  of kingdom and to establish a long lasting ruling dynasty of Nemanjic.
1 CONT
1 CONT Stefan Prvovencani was the second eldest son of the Grand Župan Stefan Nemanja, younger brother of Vukan who ruled over Zeta and older brother of Rastko Nemanjic (known as Saint Sava) who became the founder of the independent Serb
1 CONC ian Orthodox Church. He inherited the title of Grand Župan in 1196 when his father retired as a monk.
1 CONT
1 CONT His reign began with a struggle against Vukan, who expelled Stefan from Serbia with Hungarian support. Stefan turned to King Kaloyan of Bulgaria, who gave him an army of Cumans in exchange for eastern Serbian territories. The cris
1 CONC is ended when Sava negotiated a peace between the two brothers and Stefan's power was cemented. The Pope granted him the title of the King of Raška in 1217 resulted from his skillful diplomacy and persuasion. However, after Sava m
1 CONC anaged to gain an archbisphoric from the Greek patriarch, he crowned Stefan as an Orthodox King of the Serbs in 1219 and the Catholic Church made no further gains in Serbia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Stefan was married, about 1185–1187, to Eudocia Angelina, youngest daughter of Alexius Angelus and niece of the Byzantine emperor Isaac II Angelus. According to the Greek historian Nicetas Choniates, Stefan and Eudocia quarrelled 
1 CONC and separated, accusing one another of adultery, about 1198. They had two daughters, whose names are unknown, and four sons.
1 CONT
1 CONT See also: List of Serbian monarchs - History of Serbia
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Stefan Nemanja
1 CONT  House of Nemanjic
1 CONT  Succeeded by:
1 CONT Stefan Radoslav
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Source
1 CONT The Catholic Encyclopedia (1907) article at http://www.newadvent.org/cathen/13732a.htm 
1 CONT A Concise Historical Atlas of Eastern Europe 
1 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT Stephen II of Serbia
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT (Redirected from Stefan Prvovencani)
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT
1 CONT Map of Stefan's realmStefan II or Stephen II, known afterwards as Stefan Prvovencani (lit. meaning: Stephen the first-crowned) or Stefan II, Nemanja (?????? ???????????, ?????? II, ??????) (d. September 24, 1228) was the ruler of 
1 CONC the Serbian state of Raška who managed to promote it to the status of kingdom and to establish a long lasting ruling dynasty of Nemanjic.
1 CONT
1 CONT Stefan Prvovencani was the second eldest son of the Grand Župan Stefan Nemanja, younger brother of Vukan who ruled over Zeta and older brother of Rastko Nemanjic (known as Saint Sava) who became the founder of the independent Serb
1 CONC ian Orthodox Church. He inherited the title of Grand Župan in 1196 when his father retired as a monk.
1 CONT
1 CONT His reign began with a struggle against Vukan, who expelled Stefan from Serbia with Hungarian support. Stefan turned to King Kaloyan of Bulgaria, who gave him an army of Cumans in exchange for eastern Serbian territories. The cris
1 CONC is ended when Sava negotiated a peace between the two brothers and Stefan's power was cemented. Pope Honorius III granted him the title of the King of Raška in 1217 resulted from his skillful diplomacy and persuasion. However, aft
1 CONC er Sava managed to gain an archbisphoric from Patriarch of Constantinople Manuel I, he crowned Stefan as an Orthodox King of the Serbs in 1219 and the Catholic Church made no further gains in Serbia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Stefan was married, about 1185–1187, to Eudocia Angelina, youngest daughter of Alexius Angelus and Euphrosyne Doukaina Kamaterina. Eudocia was also niece of the current Byzantine Emperor Isaac II Angelus. According to the Greek hi
1 CONC storian Nicetas Choniates, Stefan and Eudocia quarrelled and separated, accusing one another of adultery, about 1198. They had two daughters, whose names are unknown, and four sons.
1 CONT
1 CONT See also: List of Serbian monarchs - History of Serbia
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Stefan Nemanja
1 CONT  House of Nemanjic
1 CONT  Succeeded by:
1 CONT Stefan Radoslav
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
