0 @N6000000002188017719@ NOTE Renier I of Montferrat
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Renier I of Montferrat (1084-c. 1136) was marquess of Montferrat from around 1100 to around 1136. He was the son of marquess William IV of Montferrat and his wife Otta d'Aglie, a daughter of Tibaldo d'Aglie.
1 CONT
1 CONT Renier married Gisela, daughter of William I, Count of Burgundy. Gisela was the widow of Humbert II of Savoy, who had died in 1103, and by whom she was mother of Adelasia of Moriana (fr. Adélaide de Maurienne), who in 1115 became 
1 CONC the second queen of Louis VI of France. She and Renier had three or four daughters:
1 CONT
1 CONT Johanna, who married William Clito, Count of Flanders in 1127, and was widowed a year later. 
1 CONT Matilda, who married Alberto 'Zueta', marquess of Parodi. 
1 CONT Name unknown (possibly Isabella), who married Guido, Count of Biandrate (although it is possible that this may be a second marriage of Johanna). 
1 CONT Adelasia, who became a nun. 
1 CONT They also had one son, William, who succeeded his father.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT Usseglio, Leopoldo. I Marchesi di Monferrato in Italia ed in Oriente durante i secoli XII e XIII, 1926. 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT William IV Marquess of Montferrat
1 CONT c. 1100-c. 1136 Succeeded by:
1 CONT William V 
