0 @N6000000002187834401@ NOTE Frederick VI, Duke of Swabia
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Frederick VI of Hohenstaufen (1167 – January 20, 1191) was duke of Swabia from 1170 to his death at the siege of Acre. He was the third son of Frederick III Barbarossa and Beatrice I, Countess of Burgundy and brother of Henry VI, 
1 CONC Holy Roman Emperor. Frederick married (or only bethroted) with the princess Constanze of Hungary, but had no known descendants.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] See also
1 CONT Dukes of Swabia family tree 
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Frederick V Duke of Swabia
1 CONT 1170–1191 Succeeded by
1 CONT Conrad II 
0 @N6000000005599189924@ NOTE When his father died, Frederick took command of what was left of his f athers army on its way to Palestine.  He arrived in the Holy Land in a bout October of 1190.
