0 @N6000000002187829736@ NOTE Thomas I of Savoy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas I or Tommaso I (1178 – March 1, 1233) was Count of Savoy from 1189 - 1233. He was the son of Humbert III of Savoy and Beatrice of Viennois. His birth was seen as miraculous; his monkish father had despaired of having a male
1 CONC  heir after three wives. Count Humbert sought counsel from St. Anthelm, who blessed Humbert three times, and it was seen as a prophecy come true when Thomas was born shortly after Anthelm himself died on June 26, 1178. He was name
1 CONC d in honor of St. Thomas Becket.
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas possessed the martial abilities, energy, and brilliance that his father lacked, and Savoy enjoyed a golden age under his leadership. He had taken over effective rule of Savoy by August 1191, and despite his youth he began t
1 CONC he push north-west into new territories. He conquerored Vaud, Bugey, and Carignano. He supported the Hohenstaufens, and was known as "Thomas the Ghibelline" due to his career as Imperial Vicar of Lombardy.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1195 he ambushed the party of Count William I of Geneva, which was escorting the count's daughter, Marguerite, to France for her intended wedding to King Philip II of France. Thomas carried off Marguerite and married her himsel
1 CONC f, producing some eight sons and six daughters.
1 CONT
1 CONT Amedeo 
1 CONT Umberto, d. between March and November 1223 
1 CONT Tommaso 
1 CONT Aimone, d. August 30, 1237, Lord of Chablais 
1 CONT Guglielmo, Bishop of Valence and Dean of Vienne 
1 CONT Amadeo of Savoy, Bishop of Maurienne 
1 CONT Pietro 
1 CONT Filippo 
1 CONT Bonifacio 
1 CONT Beatrice, d. 1265 or 1266, married in December 1219 to Ramon Berenguer IV, Count of Provence (1209-1245) 
1 CONT Alasia of Savoy, abbess of the monastery of St Pierre in Lyon 
1 CONT Ágatha of Savoy, abbess of the monastery of St Pierre in Lyon 
1 CONT Margherita of Savoy, d. 1273, married in 1218 to Hartmann I of Kyburg 
1 CONT Avita of Savoy, married Baldwin de Reviers, 8th Earl of Devon 
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Humbert III Count of Savoy
1 CONT  Succeeded by:
1 CONT Amadeus IV 
