0 @N6000000002188572472@ NOTE Alfonso IV of Aragon
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Alfonso IV, called the Kind (also the Gentle or the Nice, Catalan: Alfons el Benigne) (1299 – 24 January 1336) was the King of Aragon[1] and Count of Barcelona[2] (as Alfonso III) from 1327 to his death. He was the second son of J
1 CONC ames II and Blanche of Anjou. His reign saw the incorporation of the County of Urgell, Duchy of Athens, and Duchy of Neopatria into the Crown of Aragon.
1 CONT
1 CONT During the reign of his father, he was the procurator general of the Crown. He married Teresa d'Entença, heiress of Urgell, in 1314. In 1323–1324, he undertook the conquest of Sardinia. He became heir after his older brother James
1 CONC  renounced his rights to become a monk. In 1329, he began a long war with the Republic of Genoa. The city of Sassari surrenderd in 1323, but rebelled three more times and was contested by Genoa.
1 CONT
1 CONT After widowing, Alfonso married Eleanor of Castile, who was betrothed to his brother James, who had refused to consummate the marriage. She was the sister of Alfonso XI of Castile.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Ancestors
1 CONT Alfonso's ancestors in three generations Alfonso IV of Aragon Father:
1 CONT James II of Aragon Paternal Grandfather:
1 CONT Peter III of Aragon Paternal Great-grandfather:
1 CONT James I of Aragon
1 CONT Paternal Great-grandmother:
1 CONT Violant of Hungary
1 CONT Paternal Grandmother:
1 CONT Constantia of Sicily Paternal Great-grandfather:
1 CONT Manfred of Sicily
1 CONT Paternal Great-grandmother:
1 CONT Beatrice of Savoy
1 CONT Mother:
1 CONT Blanche of Anjou Maternal Grandfather:
1 CONT Charles II of Naples Maternal Great-grandfather:
1 CONT Charles I of Naples
1 CONT Maternal Great-grandmother:
1 CONT Beatrice of Provence
1 CONT Maternal Grandmother:
1 CONT Maria Arpad of Hungary Maternal Great-grandfather:
1 CONT Stephen V of Hungary
1 CONT Maternal Great-grandmother:
1 CONT Elisabeth of Kuthan
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Children
1 CONT
1 CONT By Teresa d'Entença:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Alfonso, lived only one year
1 CONT     * Peter IV, successor
1 CONT     * James I, Count of Urgell, also inherited Entença and Antillon
1 CONT     * Fadrique, died young
1 CONT     * Constance (1322-1346), married James III of Majorca
1 CONT     * Elizabeth, died young
1 CONT     * Sancho (1327), lived only a few days
1 CONT
1 CONT By Eleanor of Castile:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Ferdinand, Marquis of Tortosa
1 CONT     * John, married Isabel Núñez de Lara and was killed by order of his cousin Pedro of Castile
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Notes
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. ^ He held the Crown of Aragon, which included not just Aragon, but also the kingdoms of Valencia, Sardinia, and Corsica.
1 CONT    2. ^ He was also the holder of most of the Catalan counties
