1 CONT REIGNED: Emperor of the Holy Roman Empire and King of Germany (1106 - 1125)
1 CONT With the blessing of Pope PASCHAL II, Henry V, 1081-1125, emperor (1111-25)
1 CONT and German king (1105-25), forced his father, Henry IV, to abdicate (1105),
1 CONT but he soon fell out with the pope. In 1111 he took Paschal and his cardinals
1 CONT prisoner. To secure his release the pope crowned Henry emperor and made other
1 CONT concessions. The conflict continued but was finally resolved by the Concordat
1 CONT of Worms (1122).
1 CONT SOURCE: Concise Columbia Electronic Encyclopedia Copyright 1994, Columbia
