1 CONT Henry V invades Italy in 1110 and negotiates with Pope Paschal II.
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry V is to be crowned by Pope Paschal II in St. Peter's, but Paschal explodes over terms of a peace treaty. Henry leaves Rome in 1111, taking Paschal along. Unable to obtain help, Paschal crowns Henry Emperor.
1 CONT
1 CONT Holy Roman Emperor Henry V is excommunicated by the Synod of Vienna in 1112.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1125, Holy Roman Emperor Henry V dies at Utrecht and is succeeded by Lothair II.
1 CONT
