0 @N6000000002187570039@ NOTE William I, Count of Burgundy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT William I (1020 – 1087), called the Great (le Grand or Tête Hardie, "the Rash") was Count of Burgundy and Mâcon from 1057 to 1087. He was a son of Renaud I and Adelaide, daughter of Richard II of Normandy. William was the father o
1 CONC f several notable children, including Pope Callistus II.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1057, he succeeded his father and reigned over a territory larger than that of the Franche-Comté itself. In 1087, he died in Besançon and was buried there in the cathedral of St John.
1 CONT
1 CONT William married a woman named Stephanie.[1]
1 CONT
1 CONT They had several children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Renaud II, William's successor, died on First Crusade 
1 CONT Stephen I, successor to Renaud II, Stephen died on the Crusade of 1101 
1 CONT Raymond, married (1090) Urraca, the reigning queen of Castile 
1 CONT Guy of Vienne, elected pope, in 1119 at the Abbey of Cluny. as Calixtus II 
1 CONT Sybilla (or Maud), married (1080) Eudes I of Burgundy 
1 CONT Gisela, married (1090) Humbert II of Savoy and then Renier I of Montferrat 
1 CONT Adelaide 
1 CONT Bertha 
1 CONT Eudes 
1 CONT Hugh III, Archbishop of Besançon 
1 CONT Clemence married Robert II, Count of Flanders and was Regent, during his absence 
1 CONT Stephanie 
1 CONT Ermentrude, married (1065) Thierry I of Montbéliard 
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Renaud I Count of Burgundy
1 CONT 1057 – 1087 Succeeded by
1 CONT Renaud II 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Note
1 CONT ^ She was identified as the daughter of Adalbert, Duke of Lorraine in an article by Szabolcs de Vajay in Annales de Bourgogne, XXXII:247-267 (Oct-Dec 1960), but the author subsequently made an unqualified retraction of this claim 
1 CONC in "Parlons encore d'Etiennette" in Prosopographica et Genealogica, vol. 3: Onomastioque et Parenté dans l'Occident medieval, K. S. B. Keats-Rohan and C. Settipani, eds. (2000), pp. 2-6. 
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT Portail sur Histoire Bourgogne et Histoire Franche-Comté, Gilles Maille
1 CONT FMG on William I, Comté de Burgundy
