0 @N6000000003658751366@ NOTE From Plantagenet Ancestry:
1 CONT
1 CONT ARTHUR OF BRITTANY, Duke of Brittany, Count of Anjou, Earl of Richmond], son and heir, born 29 March 1187, at Nantes.  On his uncle, King Richard's death in 1199, he led a force into Anjou and Maine.  On Easter Day 1199 the barons
1 CONC  of Anjou, Touraine, and Maine acknowledged him as the rightful heir.  In 1202 he supported King Philippe Auguste of France against his uncle, King John.  IN July 1202 King Philippe knighted him at Gournay and betrothed him to the
1 CONC  king's infant daughter, Marie.  On 1 August 1202, when besieging his grandmother, Eleanor of Aquitaine, at Mirebeau, he was surprised and captured by John, who sent him to Falaise.  Early in 1203 John transferred him to Rouen, wh
1 CONC ere he disappeared before Easter.  He died probably about 3 April 1203, almost certainly at Rouen, bur possibly at Cherbourg, murdered either by John himself or at his command.  His body is alleged to have been bured at Nôtre Dame
1 CONC  des Prés.
0 @N6000000000437083494@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Count
0 @N6000000002187834429@ NOTE Renaud III, Count of Burgundy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Renaud III (c. 1093 – 1148), son of Stephen I (Tête-hardi) and Beatrix of Lorraine, was the count of Burgundy between 1127 and 1148. Previously, he had been the count of Mâcon since his father's death in 1102, with his brother, Wi
1 CONC lliam of Vienne.
1 CONT
1 CONT He proclaimed independence from the Holy Roman Emperor Lothair III, but was defeated by King Conrad III of Germany and forced to relinquish all his lands east of the Jura. The name of the region Franche-Comté is derived from his t
1 CONC itle, franc-compte, meaning "free count".
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT
1 CONT About 1130, he married Agatha (d. April 1147), daughter of Simon I, duke of Lorraine.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Children of Renaud and Agatha
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Beatrice (c.1145 – 15 November 1184) married the Emperor Frederick Barbarossa in 1156
1 CONT
1 CONT Beatrice became countess of Burgundy on her father's death.
