1 CONT Had 15 children: Eleanor, Joan, John, Henry, Julian (Katherine), Joan of Acre, Alfonso (Earl of Chester), Margaret, Berengaria, Mary, Alice, Elizabeth, Edward II (King of England), Beatrice and Blanche.
1 CONT
1 CONT Eleanor was only about ten years old when married to the 15-year-old Edward of Westminster at Las Huelgas in 1254. Such child marriages were commonplace , and the brides were usually consigned to their husbands' families to comple
1 CONC te their education. The marriages were not consummated until the bride reached a suitable age; in Eleanor's case, this seems to have been 18 or 19. Source: Royal Genealogies <http://ftp.cac.psu.edu/~saw/royal/>Had 15 children: Ele
1 CONC anor, Joan, John, Henry, Julian (Katherine), Joan of Acre, Alfonso (Earl of Chester), Margaret, Berengaria, Mary, Alice, Elizabeth, Edward II (King of England), Beatrice and Blanche.
