0 @N6000000005598882392@ NOTE Raymond is styled as tall, well built and reputedly quite handsome. Wh ile of great physical strenght, he could neither read nor write.  He w as very close to his niece Eleanor, Queen of France and England, when she was a child.  
1 CONC He became a protege of Henry I of England.  He was t rained for knighthood at the English court and left there in 1133.  H e was selected as the Prince of Antioch by Fulk of Jerusalem.  When h e arrived in Antioch, he was disquise
1 CONC d as a pedlar and asked Alice wid ow of Bohemond to marry him.  Initially, whe accepted, but while makin g arrangements Raymond had secretly married her daughter with the assi stance of the Patriarch of Antioch.  In the fall of 11
1 CONC 45, he sent mess ages requesting assistance against Nureddin - Governor of Mosul and Al eppo.  Subsequently, there were rumors of a relationship between Raymo nd and Eleanor d'Aquitaine - Queen of France.
