0 @N6000000002187757242@ NOTE Mstislav of Kiev
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Mstislav I Vladimirovich the Great (Russian: ???????? ???????????? ???????) (June 1, 1076 – April 14, 1132), was the Velikiy Kniaz (Grand Prince) of Kiev (1125-1132), the eldest son of Vladimir Monomakh by Gytha of Wessex. He figu
1 CONC res prominently in the Norse Sagas under the name Harald, taken to allude to his grandfather, Harold II of England.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT St Nicholas Cathedral, built by Mstislav I near his palace at Yaroslav's Court, Novgorod, contains 12th-century frescoes depicting his illustrious familyAs his father's future successor, Mstislav reigned in Novgorod the Great from
1 CONC  1088-93 and (after a brief stint at Rostov) from 1095-1117. Thereafter he was Monomakh's co-ruler in Belgorod-on-the-Dnieper, and inherited the Kievan throne after his death. He built numerous churches in Novgorod, of which St. N
1 CONC icholas Cathedral (1113) and the cathedral of St Anthony Cloister (1117) survive to the present day. Later, he would also erect important churches in Kiev, notably his family sepulchre at Berestovo and the church of Our Lady at Po
1 CONC dil.
1 CONT
1 CONT Mstislav's life was spent in constant warfare with Cumans (1093, 1107, 1111, 1129), Estonians (1111, 1113, 1116, 1130), Lithuanians (1131), and the princedom of Polotsk (1127, 1129). In 1096, he defeated his uncle Oleg of Chernigo
1 CONC v on the Koloksha River, thereby laying foundation for the centuries of enmity between his and Oleg's descendants. Mstislav was the last ruler of united Rus, and upon his death, as the chronicler put it, "the land of Rus was torn 
1 CONC apart".
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1095, Mstislav wed Princess Christine of Sweden, daughter of King Ingold I. They had many children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Ingeborg of Kiev, married Canute Lavard of Jutland, and was mother to Valdemar I of Denmark 
1 CONT Malmfrid, married (1) Sigurd I of Norway; (2) Eric II of Denmark 
1 CONT Eupraxia, married Alexius Comnenus, son of John II Comnenus 
1 CONT Vsevolod of Novgorod 
1 CONT Maria, married Vsevolod II of Kiev 
1 CONT Iziaslav II of Kiev 
1 CONT Rostislav of Kiev 
1 CONT Sviatopolk of Pskov 
1 CONT Rogneda, married Yaroslav of Volinya 
1 CONT Xenia, married Briachislav of Izyaslawl 
1 CONT Christine died on January 18, 1122; later that year Mstislav married again, to the daughter of Dmitry Zavidich, a nobleman of Novgorod. Their children were:
1 CONT
1 CONT Vladimir II Mstislavich (1132-1171) 
1 CONT Euphrosyne of Kiev, married King Geza II of Hungary 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Vladimir Monomakh
1 CONT  Rulers of Kievan Rus
1 CONT  Succeeded by:
1 CONT Yaropolk II
1 CONT
